{"level":30,"time":1776957932136,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NvBXNvHX5X9UxQHQCCSSb7","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 35 — Landscape Calculations\n     2→\n     3→Provides landscape calculations, plant lists, and tree preservation notes.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains landscape and tree preservation calculations, plant schedules, and standard municipal notes for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to demonstrate compliance with City of Austin landscape, buffering, and tree mitigation requirements, detailing exact plant species, quantities, and associated fees for tree removal.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Site & Landscape Areas:** Total Site Area: 94,203 SF; Total Street-Yard Area: 6,314 SF; Street-Yard Landscape Provided: 5,206 SF (Required: 1,263 SF)\n    11→*   **Open Space & Buffering:** Private Common Open Space Provided: 5,855 SF (Required: 4,715 SF); Buffer Points Provided: 57 (Required: 40)\n    12→*   **Parking Lot Landscape:** Non-Street-Yard Landscape Provided: 816 SF (Required: 60 SF)\n    13→*   **Tree Preservation & Mitigation:** Total App F Tree Inches Surveyed: 606 inches; Total App F Tree Inches Removed: 240 inches; Total Invasive Tree Inches Removed: 137 inches\n    14→*   **Mitigation Requirements:** Total Mitigation Inches Planted on Site: 55 inches; Remaining Mitigation Inches Required: 162 inches; Amount to be Paid into Fund: $26,900\n    15→*   **Key Plant Quantities (Minimum specs):** 10 Cedar Elm (100 gal.), 2 Live Oak (100 gal.), 6 Mexican Redbud (45 gal.), 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (45 gal.)\n    16→*   **Groundcover Quantities:** 92 Obedient Plant (4\" flat), 72 Frogfruit (4\" flat)\n    17→\n    18→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    19→\n    20→**Calculations & Mitigation Data**\n    21→*   **Block 14:** City of Austin Landscape Calculations. READ for required versus provided area metrics for street yards, parking lots, buffering points, and private common open space.\n    22→*   **Blocks 11 & 17:** Tree Preservation Calculations (Heading and Table). READ for an exact breakdown of existing trees, trees removed by size/category, replacement inches required (including 300% multipliers for heritage trees), and final fee-in-lieu calculations. \n    23→*   **Block 15:** COA Required Trees Chart. READ for street yard, buffer, and parking lot tree inch requirements (Total required: 13 inches) versus proposed inches. \n    24→*   **Block 3:** Tree preservation notes. READ for exemptions (Chinaberry, Bradford Pear, and Ash trees require no mitigation).\n    25→\n    26→**Plant List Schedules**\n    27→*   **Blocks 6 & 16:** Plant List heading and Shade Trees schedule. READ for exact shade tree species, quantities (10 Cedar Elm, 2 Live Oak), and minimum planting specifications (100 Gal., 4\" Cal.). Use VISION to see the associated plan symbols.\n    28→*   **Block 12:** Ornamental Trees schedule. READ for species, quantities, and container specs. Use VISION to map symbols to the landscape plan.\n    29→*   **Block 18:** Shrubs schedule. READ for shrub species, quantities, container sizes, and maximum spacing requirements. \n    30→*   **Block 13:** Groundcovers schedule. READ for groundcover species, quantities, and spacing specifications.\n    31→*   **Block 5:** Plant list notes. READ for contractor instructions regarding unit cost formatting, substitutions, and plant sourcing responsibilities.\n    32→\n    33→**Municipal Notes & Specifications**\n    34→*   **Block 1:** Remedial Tree Care Notes. READ for aeration and supplemental nutrient requirements for trees within construction areas.\n    35→*   **Block 2:** Special Construction Techniques (ECM 3.5.4 D). READ for specifications on rock sawing, mulch applications, and grading near critical root zones.\n    36→*   **Block 4:** Modified & Natural Area Protection Notes. READ for fencing, wrapping, and pruning rules before, during, and after construction.\n    37→*   **Block 7:** Site Development Permit Landscape notes. READ for requirements on protective barriers, vegetation buffering, and temporary seeding during specific dates.\n    38→*   **Block 8:** Site Development Permit Irrigation notes. READ for TCEQ Chapter 344 compliance, water conservation rules, and final inspection deliverable requirements.\n    39→\n    40→**Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    41→*   **Blocks 9, 10, 19, 20, 21, 22, 23, 24:** Project and sheet administrative data. READ for project name (Valley View Townhomes), owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), location (3759 Valley View Road), engineering firm (Blu Fish Collaborative), landscape architect seal, and sheet number (32 of 35).\n    42→\n    43→---\n    44→\n    45→- `block-1.md` — notes: Notes on remedial tree care, aeration, and supplemental nutrient requirements.\n    46→- `block-2.md` — notes: Notes related to site development permit irrigation.\n    47→- `block-3.md` — notes: Notes on modified and natural area protection.\n    48→- `block-7.md` — notes: Notes related to site development permit landscape.\n    49→\n    50→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    51→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8dbaef9-50fb-4056-bee6-2c0dccabc43f","uuid":"7afe6d94-b335-473a-8243-7ab29a91f619","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-35/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 35 — Landscape Calculations\n\nProvides landscape calculations, plant lists, and tree preservation notes.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains landscape and tree preservation calculations, plant schedules, and standard municipal notes for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to demonstrate compliance with City of Austin landscape, buffering, and tree mitigation requirements, detailing exact plant species, quantities, and associated fees for tree removal.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Site & Landscape Areas:** Total Site Area: 94,203 SF; Total Street-Yard Area: 6,314 SF; Street-Yard Landscape Provided: 5,206 SF (Required: 1,263 SF)\n*   **Open Space & Buffering:** Private Common Open Space Provided: 5,855 SF (Required: 4,715 SF); Buffer Points Provided: 57 (Required: 40)\n*   **Parking Lot Landscape:** Non-Street-Yard Landscape Provided: 816 SF (Required: 60 SF)\n*   **Tree Preservation & Mitigation:** Total App F Tree Inches Surveyed: 606 inches; Total App F Tree Inches Removed: 240 inches; Total Invasive Tree Inches Removed: 137 inches\n*   **Mitigation Requirements:** Total Mitigation Inches Planted on Site: 55 inches; Remaining Mitigation Inches Required: 162 inches; Amount to be Paid into Fund: $26,900\n*   **Key Plant Quantities (Minimum specs):** 10 Cedar Elm (100 gal.), 2 Live Oak (100 gal.), 6 Mexican Redbud (45 gal.), 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (45 gal.)\n*   **Groundcover Quantities:** 92 Obedient Plant (4\" flat), 72 Frogfruit (4\" flat)\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n**Calculations & Mitigation Data**\n*   **Block 14:** City of Austin Landscape Calculations. READ for required versus provided area metrics for street yards, parking lots, buffering points, and private common open space.\n*   **Blocks 11 & 17:** Tree Preservation Calculations (Heading and Table). READ for an exact breakdown of existing trees, trees removed by size/category, replacement inches required (including 300% multipliers for heritage trees), and final fee-in-lieu calculations. \n*   **Block 15:** COA Required Trees Chart. READ for street yard, buffer, and parking lot tree inch requirements (Total required: 13 inches) versus proposed inches. \n*   **Block 3:** Tree preservation notes. READ for exemptions (Chinaberry, Bradford Pear, and Ash trees require no mitigation).\n\n**Plant List Schedules**\n*   **Blocks 6 & 16:** Plant List heading and Shade Trees schedule. READ for exact shade tree species, quantities (10 Cedar Elm, 2 Live Oak), and minimum planting specifications (100 Gal., 4\" Cal.). Use VISION to see the associated plan symbols.\n*   **Block 12:** Ornamental Trees schedule. READ for species, quantities, and container specs. Use VISION to map symbols to the landscape plan.\n*   **Block 18:** Shrubs schedule. READ for shrub species, quantities, container sizes, and maximum spacing requirements. \n*   **Block 13:** Groundcovers schedule. READ for groundcover species, quantities, and spacing specifications.\n*   **Block 5:** Plant list notes. READ for contractor instructions regarding unit cost formatting, substitutions, and plant sourcing responsibilities.\n\n**Municipal Notes & Specifications**\n*   **Block 1:** Remedial Tree Care Notes. READ for aeration and supplemental nutrient requirements for trees within construction areas.\n*   **Block 2:** Special Construction Techniques (ECM 3.5.4 D). READ for specifications on rock sawing, mulch applications, and grading near critical root zones.\n*   **Block 4:** Modified & Natural Area Protection Notes. READ for fencing, wrapping, and pruning rules before, during, and after construction.\n*   **Block 7:** Site Development Permit Landscape notes. READ for requirements on protective barriers, vegetation buffering, and temporary seeding during specific dates.\n*   **Block 8:** Site Development Permit Irrigation notes. READ for TCEQ Chapter 344 compliance, water conservation rules, and final inspection deliverable requirements.\n\n**Boilerplate & Administrative**\n*   **Blocks 9, 10, 19, 20, 21, 22, 23, 24:** Project and sheet administrative data. READ for project name (Valley View Townhomes), owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), location (3759 Valley View Road), engineering firm (Blu Fish Collaborative), landscape architect seal, and sheet number (32 of 35).\n\n---\n\n- `block-1.md` — notes: Notes on remedial tree care, aeration, and supplemental nutrient requirements.\n- `block-2.md` — notes: Notes related to site development permit irrigation.\n- `block-3.md` — notes: Notes on modified and natural area protection.\n- `block-7.md` — notes: Notes related to site development permit landscape.\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":51,"startLine":1,"totalLines":51}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776957932157,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UmhHSvxKfrBphF3GdLUAMW","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 31 — Landscape Plan\n     2→\n     3→Landscape design plan featuring planting details and irrigation notes.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet presents the Landscape Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, detailing the layout of plantings, open spaces, hardscape features, and site contours. It serves as the primary reference for landscape grading, planting mitigation requirements, and automatic irrigation system specifications.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Drawing Scale:** 1\" = 20'-0\"\n    11→*   **Topsoil Placement Depth:** Finished elevation for parking lot islands and similar areas must be at least 6 inches below the finished parking lot/curb elevation.\n    12→*   **Irrigation Spray Limits:** No spray irrigation is permitted on areas less than 10 feet wide (e.g., medians, buffer strips).\n    13→*   **Irrigation Setbacks:** Above-ground irrigation emission devices must be set back at least 6 inches from impervious surfaces.\n    14→*   **Rain Shut-off Threshold:** Automatic rain shut-off devices must trigger after more than 1/2 inch (0.5\") of rainfall.\n    15→*   **Tree Mitigation Size:** Street yard and parking lot trees exceeding 1.5 caliper inches count towards mitigation.\n    16→*   **Site Elevations:** Topographic contour lines indicate site elevations ranging generally from approximately 660 to 690 feet.\n    17→\n    18→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    19→\n    20→*   **Block 2: drawing — Main Landscape and Site Plan**\n    21→    A comprehensive site plan illustrating building footprints, parking layouts, sidewalks, utility lines (Water, Storm Drain, Overhead Electric), topographical contours, and the distribution of landscape elements.\n    22→    *Use VISION to examine* the spatial layout of the site, locate specific landscape zones (using H-series key notes), trace contour grading, and identify the placement of mitigation trees.\n    23→\n    24→*   **Block 5: notes — Key Notes & Legend**\n    25→    Defines the hatch patterns and symbols used in the main drawing, including paving (H.1), street yards (H.2, H.3), parking lot landscaping (H.4), common open space (H.5), wooden privacy fences (H.6), and sod (H.7). It also defines abbreviations for tree types (SY, PL, P, M).\n    26→    *READ the block content for* exact definitions of hatch patterns, symbols, and mitigation tree sizing requirements (>1.5 cal. inch) to accurately interpret the main drawing.\n    27→\n    28→*   **Block 3: notes — Irrigation Notes**\n    29→    Technical specifications ensuring the automatic irrigation system complies with TCEQ Chapter 344. It covers hardware requirements (master valves, rain shut-offs), spatial constraints, and deliverables required from the installer (as-built plans, water budgets).\n    30→    *READ the block content for* specific compliance metrics, installation constraints, and administrative requirements for final plumbing inspection.\n    31→\n    32→*   **Block 4: notes — General Landscape Notes**\n    33→    Specific grading and soil requirements for landscaped areas adjacent to paving, detailing the necessary finished elevation offsets to accommodate topsoil placement. Also provides guidance on drought variance procedures.\n    34→    *READ the block content for* exact grading dimensions (6 inches below finished elevation) and supplemental irrigation requirements.\n    35→\n    36→*   **Block 1: diagram — Scale and Orientation**\n    37→    Provides the graphical scale and North arrow for the main drawing.\n    38→    *READ the block content for* the exact scale (1\" = 20'-0\") and *Use VISION to* orient the site layout.\n    39→\n    40→*   **Blocks 6, 7, 8, 9: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    41→    Contains the title block information, including the project name (Valley View Townhomes), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX), property owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), and the licensed landscape architect's professional seal (dated 02/13/2026).\n    42→    *READ the block content for* general project context, property address, and professional certification details.\n    43→\n    44→---\n    45→\n    46→- `block-3.md` — notes: Irrigation notes detailing requirements for automatic irrigation systems to comply with TCEQ Chapter\n    47→\n    48→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    49→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ea0af40-45f3-4b07-b50e-bf4188546a20","uuid":"6f60a8f3-8df1-425b-8b78-bfe718b01ab5","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 31 — Landscape Plan\n\nLandscape design plan featuring planting details and irrigation notes.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet presents the Landscape Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, detailing the layout of plantings, open spaces, hardscape features, and site contours. It serves as the primary reference for landscape grading, planting mitigation requirements, and automatic irrigation system specifications.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Drawing Scale:** 1\" = 20'-0\"\n*   **Topsoil Placement Depth:** Finished elevation for parking lot islands and similar areas must be at least 6 inches below the finished parking lot/curb elevation.\n*   **Irrigation Spray Limits:** No spray irrigation is permitted on areas less than 10 feet wide (e.g., medians, buffer strips).\n*   **Irrigation Setbacks:** Above-ground irrigation emission devices must be set back at least 6 inches from impervious surfaces.\n*   **Rain Shut-off Threshold:** Automatic rain shut-off devices must trigger after more than 1/2 inch (0.5\") of rainfall.\n*   **Tree Mitigation Size:** Street yard and parking lot trees exceeding 1.5 caliper inches count towards mitigation.\n*   **Site Elevations:** Topographic contour lines indicate site elevations ranging generally from approximately 660 to 690 feet.\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 2: drawing — Main Landscape and Site Plan**\n    A comprehensive site plan illustrating building footprints, parking layouts, sidewalks, utility lines (Water, Storm Drain, Overhead Electric), topographical contours, and the distribution of landscape elements.\n    *Use VISION to examine* the spatial layout of the site, locate specific landscape zones (using H-series key notes), trace contour grading, and identify the placement of mitigation trees.\n\n*   **Block 5: notes — Key Notes & Legend**\n    Defines the hatch patterns and symbols used in the main drawing, including paving (H.1), street yards (H.2, H.3), parking lot landscaping (H.4), common open space (H.5), wooden privacy fences (H.6), and sod (H.7). It also defines abbreviations for tree types (SY, PL, P, M).\n    *READ the block content for* exact definitions of hatch patterns, symbols, and mitigation tree sizing requirements (>1.5 cal. inch) to accurately interpret the main drawing.\n\n*   **Block 3: notes — Irrigation Notes**\n    Technical specifications ensuring the automatic irrigation system complies with TCEQ Chapter 344. It covers hardware requirements (master valves, rain shut-offs), spatial constraints, and deliverables required from the installer (as-built plans, water budgets).\n    *READ the block content for* specific compliance metrics, installation constraints, and administrative requirements for final plumbing inspection.\n\n*   **Block 4: notes — General Landscape Notes**\n    Specific grading and soil requirements for landscaped areas adjacent to paving, detailing the necessary finished elevation offsets to accommodate topsoil placement. Also provides guidance on drought variance procedures.\n    *READ the block content for* exact grading dimensions (6 inches below finished elevation) and supplemental irrigation requirements.\n\n*   **Block 1: diagram — Scale and Orientation**\n    Provides the graphical scale and North arrow for the main drawing.\n    *READ the block content for* the exact scale (1\" = 20'-0\") and *Use VISION to* orient the site layout.\n\n*   **Blocks 6, 7, 8, 9: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    Contains the title block information, including the project name (Valley View Townhomes), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX), property owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), and the licensed landscape architect's professional seal (dated 02/13/2026).\n    *READ the block content for* general project context, property address, and professional certification details.\n\n---\n\n- `block-3.md` — notes: Irrigation notes detailing requirements for automatic irrigation systems to comply with TCEQ Chapter\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":49,"startLine":1,"totalLines":49}}}
