Registered Professional Land Surveyor who performed the survey.\n    23→\n    24→THIS SURVEY WAS PERFORMED WITHOUT THE BENEFIT OF A CURRENT\n    25→TITLE COMMITMENT AND THERE MAY BE EASEMENTS, BUILDING LINES,\n    26→CONDITIONS, OR RESTRICTIONS OF RECORD NOT SHOWN OR NOTED\n    27→HEREON.\n    28→DATE OF SURVEY: DECEMBER 27, 2024\n    29→RYAN T. LENZ\n    30→REGISTERED PROFESSIONAL LAND SURVEYOR NO. 7624\n    31→SINCLAIR LAND SURVEYING, INC.\n    32→TBPELS FIRM No. 10089000\n    33→4150 FREIDRICH LANE, SUITE A-1\n    34→AUSTIN, TEXAS 78744\n    35→(512) 443-1174\n    36→\n    37→## Block 9: notes — A legend explaining the symbols and abbreviations used in the site plan drawing. It defines various symbols for pins, monuments, lines, and utility features.\n    38→\n    39→LEGEND\n    40→\n    41→- 1/2\" STEEL PIN FOUND UNLESS NOTED\n    42→- 1/2\" STEEL PIN SET W/CAP MARKED S.L.S. RPLS 518\n    43→- 1/2\" STEEL PIN FOUND W/CAP MARKED CARTER BURGESS\n    44→- 1/2\" STEEL PIN FOUND W/CAP MARKED LIND & ASSOC.\n    45→- MAG NAIL SET\n    46→- 3/4\" BRASS MONUMENT FOUND\n    47→- NAIL FOUND\n    48→- 60D NAIL FOUND\n    49→- CHAIN LINK FENCE\n    50→- IRON PIPE FOUND\n    51→- MAG NAIL FOUND\n    52→- \"X\" FOUND IN CONCRETE\n    53→- WATER METER\n    54→- WATER VALVE\n    55→- SPRINKLE FOUND\n    56→- WOOD FENCE\n    57→- UTILITY POLE\n    58→- WIRE FENCE\n    59→- LIGHT POLE\n    60→- CRETE FENCE\n    61→- PUBLIC UTILITY EASEMENT\n    62→- ELECTRIC EASEMENT\n    63→- WATER, WASTEWATER EASEMENT\n    64→- P.U.E. D.U.E. DRAINAGE EASEMENT\n    65→- W.W.L.E. WASTEWATER LINE\n    66→- W.L. WATER LINE\n    67→- O.H.U.L. OVERHEAD UTILITY LINE\n    68→- T.L. TOWN LOT\n    69→- C.I. CURB INLET\n    70→- (BRG-DIST) RECORD CALL ADJOINER\n    71→- - DECIDUOUS TREE (VARIOUS TYPES)\n    72→- - CLEAN-OUT\n    73→- - FIRE HYDRANT\n    74→- - AIR CONDITIONER\n    75→- - SIGN POST\n    76→- - TRANSFORMER ON PAD\n    77→- O.P.R.T.C.TX. OFFICIAL PUBLIC RECORDS OF TRAVIS COUNTY, TEXAS\n    78