{"level":30,"time":1776957935919,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AdqNLdJfECjdiqzDaL7gjC","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 21 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 2: diagram — A graphic scale bar showing distances of 0, 20, and 40 feet, along with the text 'Scale 1\" = 20''. A north arrow is also present above the scale bar.\n     4→\n     5→[Graphic scale bar showing distances 0, 20, 40]\n     6→Scale 1\" = 20'\n     7→[North arrow pointing upwards and slightly to the right]\n     8→\n     9→## Block 3: drawing — This block contains a detailed site plan showing multiple buildings (Bldg. 1 to Bldg. 8) and their respective units, with FFE (Finished Floor Elevation) and square footage information. The plan includes electrical elements such as transformers, pull boxes, underground electric lines, and electrical meters. Additionally, the plan shows topography lines, property boundaries, and various easements like drainage, public utility, and wastewater. Information on adjoining properties is provided, detailing acreage, zoning, and use.\n    10→\n    11→A detailed site plan showing multiple buildings (Bldg. 1 to Bldg. 8) and their respective units, with FFE (Finished Floor Elevation) and square footage information. The plan includes electrical elements such as transformers, pull boxes, underground electric lines, and electrical meters. Additionally, the plan shows topography lines, property boundaries, and various easements like drainage, public utility, and wastewater. Information on adjoining properties is provided, detailing acreage, zoning, and use.\n    12→\n    13→## Block 4: notes — This block contains 'Utility Notes' detailing contractor responsibilities regarding existing utilities and specific requirements for private domestic water and wastewater branches. Below the notes are disclaimers about the application not verifying all data and the reliance on record information for existing utilities.\n    14→\n    15→**Utility Notes**\n    16→1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\n    17→2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\n    18→3. All Private Domestic Water Branches to the buildings are to be 2\" HDPE service tube per Detail 520-AW-01B\n    19→4. All Private Wastewater Branches to the building are to be 6\" PVC service connections per Detail 520-AW-01C\n    20→\n    21→Release of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her submittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n    22→\n    23→The location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\n    24→\n    25→## Block 5: notes — A small block containing text that references another sheet for profile information.\n    26→\n    27→See Sht. 19\n    28→for Profile\n    29→\n    30→## Block 6: notes — A block containing a 'Tree List' reference stating 'Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.' Below it is a 'Note' regarding a Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule that requires trenching over 5 feet deep to be inspected by a geologist.\n    31→\n    32→**Tree List**\n    33→Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\n    34→\n    35→**Note**\n    36→This project is subject to the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule (COA ECM 1.12.0 and COA Item No. 658S of the SSM) provision that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist (Texas P.G.) or a geologist's representative.\n    37→\n    38→## Block 7: notes — A block listing two benchmarks (B.M. #1 and B.M. #2) with descriptions indicating they are mag nails set in asphalt, along with their respective elevations in NAVD 88 (GEOID 18).\n    39→\n    40→**Benchmarks**\n    41→B.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    42→Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    43→\n    44→B.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    45→Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    46→\n    47→## Block 12: text_block — A block providing the legal description of the property, identifying it as Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision.\n    48→\n    49→**Legal Description**\n    50→Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n    51→\n    52→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c394a41f-2cb6-411b-ae31-3b8268d295eb","uuid":"65d9d0fc-c14c-4646-bbe2-bd9e4adf3e33","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-21/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 21 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 2: diagram — A graphic scale bar showing distances of 0, 20, and 40 feet, along with the text 'Scale 1\" = 20''. A north arrow is also present above the scale bar.\n\n[Graphic scale bar showing distances 0, 20, 40]\nScale 1\" = 20'\n[North arrow pointing upwards and slightly to the right]\n\n## Block 3: drawing — This block contains a detailed site plan showing multiple buildings (Bldg. 1 to Bldg. 8) and their respective units, with FFE (Finished Floor Elevation) and square footage information. The plan includes electrical elements such as transformers, pull boxes, underground electric lines, and electrical meters. Additionally, the plan shows topography lines, property boundaries, and various easements like drainage, public utility, and wastewater. Information on adjoining properties is provided, detailing acreage, zoning, and use.\n\nA detailed site plan showing multiple buildings (Bldg. 1 to Bldg. 8) and their respective units, with FFE (Finished Floor Elevation) and square footage information. The plan includes electrical elements such as transformers, pull boxes, underground electric lines, and electrical meters. Additionally, the plan shows topography lines, property boundaries, and various easements like drainage, public utility, and wastewater. Information on adjoining properties is provided, detailing acreage, zoning, and use.\n\n## Block 4: notes — This block contains 'Utility Notes' detailing contractor responsibilities regarding existing utilities and specific requirements for private domestic water and wastewater branches. Below the notes are disclaimers about the application not verifying all data and the reliance on record information for existing utilities.\n\n**Utility Notes**\n1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\n2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\n3. All Private Domestic Water Branches to the buildings are to be 2\" HDPE service tube per Detail 520-AW-01B\n4. All Private Wastewater Branches to the building are to be 6\" PVC service connections per Detail 520-AW-01C\n\nRelease of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her submittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n\nThe location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\n\n## Block 5: notes — A small block containing text that references another sheet for profile information.\n\nSee Sht. 19\nfor Profile\n\n## Block 6: notes — A block containing a 'Tree List' reference stating 'Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.' Below it is a 'Note' regarding a Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule that requires trenching over 5 feet deep to be inspected by a geologist.\n\n**Tree List**\nRefer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\n\n**Note**\nThis project is subject to the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule (COA ECM 1.12.0 and COA Item No. 658S of the SSM) provision that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist (Texas P.G.) or a geologist's representative.\n\n## Block 7: notes — A block listing two benchmarks (B.M. #1 and B.M. #2) with descriptions indicating they are mag nails set in asphalt, along with their respective elevations in NAVD 88 (GEOID 18).\n\n**Benchmarks**\nB.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\nB.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\n## Block 12: text_block — A block providing the legal description of the property, identifying it as Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision.\n\n**Legal Description**\nLot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n\n","numLines":52,"startLine":1,"totalLines":52}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776957935933,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q4cBabGYMJHGgxPomyMJsa","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 10 — Fire Protection Plan\n     2→\n     3→Site plan illustrating fire lanes, hydrants, and fire zone details.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the Fire Protection Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the site's fire access routing, fire lane markings, fire hydrant locations, and necessary suppression system requirements to ensure compliance with the City of Austin Fire Code and NFPA standards. \n     8→\n     9→**Key values**:\n    10→* Building 1: 3,290 sf, FFE = 687.50'\n    11→* Building 2: 4,830 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n    12→* Building 3: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n    13→* Building 4: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n    14→* Building 5: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0'\n    15→* Building 6: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0'\n    16→* Building 7: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.0'\n    17→* Building 8: 4,997 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n    18→* Total private fire hydrants on site: 1\n    19→* Required fire suppression system: NFPA 13D for all buildings\n    20→* Fire Zone curb stenciling: 4-inch high white letters at 30-foot intervals on painted red curbs\n    21→* Fire Zone signage dimensions: 305 mm x 457 mm overall, with 38 mm to 76.2 mm lettering heights\n    22→* Benchmark 1: Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    23→* Benchmark 2: Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    24→\n    25→**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n    26→\n    27→* **Block 2: drawing — Main Site Plan**\n    28→  Contains the detailed site layout showing buildings 1-8, fire lanes, fire hydrants, walls, fences, and utility easements.\n    29→  Use VISION for spatial layout of fire access routing, hydrant placement, and building footprints.\n    30→\n    31→* **Block 11: notes — Fire Zone Notes**\n    32→  Contains rules for fire zone demarcation, including standard detail references and curb painting instructions.\n    33→  READ for exact specifications on signage placement, red curb painting with 4-inch stenciling, and the requirement that all private hydrants must be painted red.\n    34→\n    35→* **Block 9: notes — General System Notes**\n    36→  Contains requirements for underground main installation and testing for sprinkler systems.\n    37→  READ for exact testing specifications (NFPA 13 and NFPA 24) and the required Knox-box location at the exterior fire riser room doors.\n    38→\n    39→* **Block 7: notes — Private Hydrant Note**\n    40→  Details the City of Austin Water and Wastewater Utility requirements regarding the site's hydrants.\n    41→  READ to confirm the presence of 1 private hydrant and the owner's legal obligation for annual service and flow testing.\n    42→\n    43→* **Block 3: notes — Fire Riser Room Note**\n    44→  Specifies the required internal fire suppression system.\n    45→  READ to confirm the NFPA 13D system requirement for all proposed buildings.\n    46→\n    47→* **Block 1: diagram — Fire Zone Signage Detail**\n    48→  Contains City of Austin Standard Detail 901S-6 for \"NO PARKING FIRE ZONE TOW-AWAY ZONE\" signs.\n    49→  READ for exact values of sign dimensions, letter heights, and material colors (red transparent over silver reflective background), and use VISION for the visual layout of the sign text.\n    50→\n    51→* **Block 4: notes — Benchmarks**\n    52→  Provides surveyor reference points.\n    53→  READ for exact elevation values and locations of Benchmarks 1 and 2.\n    54→\n    55→* **Blocks 6, 8: notes — Sheet Cross-References**\n    56→  Brief notes pointing the reviewer to other sheets for additional data.\n    57→  READ to locate the Tree List (Sheet 32) and the Fire Flow Test results (Sheet 18).\n    58→\n    59→* **Blocks 5, 10, 12, 13: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    60→  Contains the title block, legal description (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision), Texas 811 callout, and standard disclaimers regarding existing utilities and engineer responsibility.\n    61→  READ for general project information and administrative records.\n    62→\n    63→---\n    64→\n    65→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    66→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ea0af40-45f3-4b07-b50e-bf4188546a20","uuid":"475c5b79-8769-40af-bf72-c74ef61d6485","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-10/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 10 — Fire Protection Plan\n\nSite plan illustrating fire lanes, hydrants, and fire zone details.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the Fire Protection Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the site's fire access routing, fire lane markings, fire hydrant locations, and necessary suppression system requirements to ensure compliance with the City of Austin Fire Code and NFPA standards. \n\n**Key values**:\n* Building 1: 3,290 sf, FFE = 687.50'\n* Building 2: 4,830 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n* Building 3: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n* Building 4: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n* Building 5: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0'\n* Building 6: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0'\n* Building 7: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.0'\n* Building 8: 4,997 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n* Total private fire hydrants on site: 1\n* Required fire suppression system: NFPA 13D for all buildings\n* Fire Zone curb stenciling: 4-inch high white letters at 30-foot intervals on painted red curbs\n* Fire Zone signage dimensions: 305 mm x 457 mm overall, with 38 mm to 76.2 mm lettering heights\n* Benchmark 1: Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n* Benchmark 2: Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n\n* **Block 2: drawing — Main Site Plan**\n  Contains the detailed site layout showing buildings 1-8, fire lanes, fire hydrants, walls, fences, and utility easements.\n  Use VISION for spatial layout of fire access routing, hydrant placement, and building footprints.\n\n* **Block 11: notes — Fire Zone Notes**\n  Contains rules for fire zone demarcation, including standard detail references and curb painting instructions.\n  READ for exact specifications on signage placement, red curb painting with 4-inch stenciling, and the requirement that all private hydrants must be painted red.\n\n* **Block 9: notes — General System Notes**\n  Contains requirements for underground main installation and testing for sprinkler systems.\n  READ for exact testing specifications (NFPA 13 and NFPA 24) and the required Knox-box location at the exterior fire riser room doors.\n\n* **Block 7: notes — Private Hydrant Note**\n  Details the City of Austin Water and Wastewater Utility requirements regarding the site's hydrants.\n  READ to confirm the presence of 1 private hydrant and the owner's legal obligation for annual service and flow testing.\n\n* **Block 3: notes — Fire Riser Room Note**\n  Specifies the required internal fire suppression system.\n  READ to confirm the NFPA 13D system requirement for all proposed buildings.\n\n* **Block 1: diagram — Fire Zone Signage Detail**\n  Contains City of Austin Standard Detail 901S-6 for \"NO PARKING FIRE ZONE TOW-AWAY ZONE\" signs.\n  READ for exact values of sign dimensions, letter heights, and material colors (red transparent over silver reflective background), and use VISION for the visual layout of the sign text.\n\n* **Block 4: notes — Benchmarks**\n  Provides surveyor reference points.\n  READ for exact elevation values and locations of Benchmarks 1 and 2.\n\n* **Blocks 6, 8: notes — Sheet Cross-References**\n  Brief notes pointing the reviewer to other sheets for additional data.\n  READ to locate the Tree List (Sheet 32) and the Fire Flow Test results (Sheet 18).\n\n* **Blocks 5, 10, 12, 13: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n  Contains the title block, legal description (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision), Texas 811 callout, and standard disclaimers regarding existing utilities and engineer responsibility.\n  READ for general project information and administrative records.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":66,"startLine":1,"totalLines":66}}}
