{"level":30,"time":1776957971459,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine the electrical design plan and identify all transformer pad locations. For each transformer pad, please provide:\n\n1. The location/reference (building number, corner, cardinal direction)\n2. Any dimensions shown for the pad itself\n3. Distance measurements or clearance annotations shown from the transformer to adjacent features such as:\n   - Buildings or structures\n   - Fences\n   - Sidewalks or pavement\n   - Underground utility lines (water, sewer, gas)\n   - Overhead lines\n   - Parking areas\n   - Fire escape or fire lanes\n   - Trees or vegetation\n   - Other transformer pads\n   - Retaining walls\n   - Fire hydrants\n   - Stairwells\n\n4. Any notes or callouts related to the transformers (service type, fire rating requirements, easement information, etc.)\n5. Whether access door orientation is shown or can be inferred\n6. Whether the transformers are oil-filled or dry-type equipment\n\nPlease be specific about what is shown and what information is missing from the plan.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan,\" there are **five** locations explicitly labeled with a callout box reading **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**. \n\nHere is the specific information requested for the transformer pads based *only* on what is visually present or missing on the plan:\n\n### 1. Locations\nThe five identified transformer pads are located at:\n*   **Northwest Pad:** Located in the northwest portion of the site, west of the primary northern drive aisle and northeast of the \"Sidewalk Easement\" boundary. It is situated generally west of Bldg 1.\n*   **West Central Pad:** Located on the west side of the site, directly west of **Bldg. 2** (adjacent to **Unit 201**). It sits between the building wall and the \"Sidewalk Easement\".\n*   **Southwest Pad:** Located on the southwest side of the site, directly west of **Bldg. 8** (adjacent to **Unit 801**). It sits between the building wall and the western property line/easement area.\n*   **East Pad:** Located near the eastern property boundary, directly east of **Bldg. 4** (adjacent to **Unit 404**) and north of **Bldg. 6** (Unit 601).\n*   **Central Pad:** Located in the central courtyard/parking area, situated in an island median between **Bldg. 7** (near **Unit 703**) and **Bldg. 6** (near **Unit 602**).\n\n### 2. Dimensions\n*   **Missing:** There are **no specific dimensions** (e.g., width x length) annotated for any of the transformer pads themselves. They are simply drawn as identical square symbols.\n\n### 3. Distance Measurements / Clearance Annotations\n*   **Missing:** There are **no numerical distance measurements or specific clearance annotations** provided from any transformer pad to adjacent features (buildings, sidewalks, underground utilities, parking areas, etc.).\n*   *What is shown:* Each transformer pad symbol is drawn with a dashed square perimeter surrounding the solid inner square. In standard drafting, this typically indicates a required clearance zone, but **no numerical values or clearance rules are stated** anywhere on this sheet to define that zone. \n\n### 4. Notes or Callouts\n*   *What is shown:* The only text associated with these elements are the leader callout boxes that read exactly: **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**.\n*   **Missing:** There are no notes indicating the electrical service type, required fire ratings, specific transformer easement dimensions, or protective bollard requirements. The general \"Utility Notes\" box does not contain any specifications regarding transformers.\n\n### 5. Access Door Orientation\n*   **Missing:** Access door orientation **is not shown** and cannot be definitively inferred. The symbol used is a basic, symmetrical square without indicators for a primary access or \"front\" side (such as a triangle pointer or standard architectural door indicator).\n\n### 6. Equipment Type (Oil-filled vs. Dry-type)\n*   **Missing:** The plan **does not specify** whether the transformers are oil-filled or dry-type equipment. No equipment schedules or detailed electrical notes are present on this page to provide this information.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1525,"outputTokens":696,"totalTokens":5710,"reasoningTokens":3489},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the elec