{"level":30,"time":1776957981388,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the Landscape Plan and identify: 1) Where are the proposed trees shown? Include any symbols, labels, or locations. 2) Where are the overhead electric lines shown? Are they labeled? 3) Where are any underground electric facilities shown (transformer pads, pull boxes, underground lines)? 4) What is the spatial relationship between any proposed trees and electric infrastructure? Are there any trees shown very close to electric lines, poles, pads, or underground equipment? Provide specific locations using building numbers, property lines, or other site features as reference points.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided Landscape Plan (Sheet 28 of 35), here are the findings regarding your specific questions:\n\n**1) Where are the proposed trees shown? Include any symbols, labels, or locations.**\n\nProposed trees are indicated on the plan by circular symbols of varying sizes representing tree canopies. Many of these circles contain a crosshair in the center.\n\n*   **Labels/Legend:** The text below the \"KEY NOTES\" legend defines specific tree labels found inside or adjacent to the tree symbols:\n    *   \"SY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n    *   \"PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n    *   \"P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\"\n    *   \"M - MITIGATION TREE\"\n    *   Additionally, some trees are labeled with hexagon keynotes (e.g., \"H.1\", \"H.2\", \"H.7\").\n*   **Locations:** Trees are proposed in the following main areas:\n    *   A continuous row along the northern (top) property boundary (labeled \"SY\", \"M\", \"PL\", \"H.7\").\n    *   A continuous row along the southern (bottom) property boundary (labeled \"M\", \"H.7\").\n    *   Within the shaded area along the western (left) street-facing edge, which is keyed as \"STREET YARD\" (labeled \"H.1\", \"H.3\", \"SY\", \"M\", \"H.2\", \"H.4\").\n    *   Sparsely within the interior courtyard/parking area (labeled \"PL\").\n    *   Near the \"SEDIMENTATION BASIN\" and \"FILTRATION BASIN\" on the eastern (right) side (labeled \"M\").\n\n**2) Where are the overhead electric lines shown? Are they labeled?**\n\nOverhead electric lines are shown along the southern (bottom) edge of the site plan.\n*   **Labels:** They are represented by a solid line embedded with the text label **`---OHE---`**. This line runs horizontally near the southern property line.\n\n**3) Where are any underground electric facilities shown (transformer pads, pull boxes, underground lines)?**\n\n*   **Underground Lines:** An underground electric line is shown in the upper left (northwest) corner of the site. It is represented by a dashed line embedded with the text label **`-E-`**.\n*   **Pads/Pull Boxes:** There are no explicit text labels or legend entries on this specific sheet that identify transformer pads or pull boxes. While there are small, unlabelled rectangular geometric shapes near the southwest entrance within the Street Yard area, they cannot be definitively identified as electrical equipment based solely on this page.\n\n**4) What is the spatial relationship between any proposed trees and electric infrastructure?**\n\nThere are proposed trees shown in close proximity to both overhead and underground electric infrastructure:\n\n*   **Relationship to Overhead Lines (`---OHE---`):** Along the southern (bottom) property line, a row of proposed trees (labeled \"M\" and \"H.7\") is planted directly parallel to the overhead electric line. The circular canopy symbols of at least four of these proposed trees on the eastern half of this southern boundary physically overlap the drawn **`---OHE---`** line.\n*   **Relationship to Underground Lines (`-E-`):** In the northwest (top left) corner, within the shaded \"STREET YARD\" area, there is a large proposed tree symbol (located near the keynote \"H.1\"). The dashed underground electric line labeled **`-E-`** is drawn passing directly underneath the circular canopy symbol of this proposed tree.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1426,"outputTokens":802,"totalTokens":4349,"reasoningTokens":2121},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the Landscape Plan and identify: 1) Where are the proposed trees shown? Include any symbols, labels, or locations. 2) 