oundary and near the bottom-right parking area.\n*   *Note: Key note H-3 indicates \"STREET YARD LANDSCAPING\" and H-4 indicates \"PARKING LOT LANDSCAPING\", which correspond generally to where the SY and PL trees are placed.*\n\n**3. Proposed trees and their caliper/size designations:**\nIndividual tree caliper sizes are not explicitly labeled next to the tree symbols on the plan view. However, the definitions provided below the KEY NOTES specify minimum sizes for certain designations:\n*   **SY** - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n*   **PL** - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n*   **P** - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE *(No size designated in text)*\n*   **M** - MITIGATION TREE *(No size designated in text)*\n\n**4. Dimension lines or notes indicating clearances between trees and OHE:**\n*   There are **no** visible dimension lines, restricted zone hatchings, or specific textual notes on this sheet that indicate required clearances between the proposed trees and the overhead electric infrastructure.\n\n***\n\n**Summary Description of OHE and Tree Proximity:**\nThe overhead electric (OHE) line runs horizontally across the entire bottom (southern) boundary of the site plan. Because there are no explicitly drawn restricted distance zones or clearance dimensions provided on this sheet, it is not possible to confirm if any trees violate a specific code restriction based solely on this document. \n\nHowever, visually, there are proposed trees placed in very close proximity to the OHE line:\n*   **Tree Symbol 'M' (Mitigation Tree)**: In the bottom right (southeast) corner of the plan, there are at least two proposed trees labeled 'M' whose symbols are located directly underneath or immediately adjacent to the \"- OHE -\" line.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1437,"outputTokens":651,"totalTokens":5275,"reasoningTokens":3187},"warnin