{"level":30,"time":1776957984090,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine the electrical site plan and identify: (1) all transformer pad locations on the site, (2) their approximate positions relative to buildings, parking areas, utilities, and site features, (3) any visible clearance dimensions or callouts relating to transformers, (4) the locations of pull boxes and underground electrical lines, (5) any visible equipment specifications or notes about transformer service types (single-phase vs. three-phase), (6) any transformer pad detail callouts or notes showing pad dimensions. Describe the precise spatial arrangement so that I can understand all horizontal distances to adjacent features.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" document, here is the information requested. \n\nPlease note that this drawing primarily shows the routing of the underground electrical loop and the locations of major equipment boxes, but lacks specific dimensioning or equipment specifications.\n\n### (1) & (2) Transformer Pad Locations and Relative Positions\nThere are three distinct locations identified with the exact label **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**. Note that while the pads are drawn to scale relative to the site plan, there are no specific horizontal distance dimensions (e.g., \"10'-0\"\") provided between the pads and adjacent features.\n\n*   **Transformer Pad 1 (West Side):**\n    *   Located on the western side of the site, near the main entrance driveway off the public street.\n    *   It is situated in a landscaped island area just south of the main entrance drive curve.\n    *   It is positioned directly west of **\"Bldg. 2\"** (specifically near **\"Unit 201\"**) and north of **\"Bldg. 8\"** (specifically near **\"Unit 801\"**).\n    *   It sits adjacent to a dashed line labeled **\"Sidewalk Easement\"**.\n\n*   **Transformer Pad 2 (Northeast/Center):**\n    *   Located in the central-eastern portion of the site.\n    *   It is positioned in an island or landscape buffer immediately east of the parking stalls serving **\"Bldg. 4\"** (near **\"Unit 404\"**).\n    *   It is located west of the building block containing units 501-504, specifically west of **\"Unit 504\"**.\n\n*   **Transformer Pad 3 (Southeast/Center):**\n    *   Located in the central-southeastern portion of the site, mirroring the arrangement of Pad 2.\n    *   It is positioned in an island or landscape buffer immediately east of the parking stalls serving **\"Bldg. 7\"** (near **\"Unit 704\"**).\n    *   It is located west of the building block containing units 601-604, specifically west of **\"Unit 601\"**.\n\n### (3) Visible Clearance Dimensions or Callouts Relating to Transformers\n*   **None visible.** There are no dimension lines, setback distances, or textual callouts indicating required clearance zones (e.g., \"10' clear workspace\") around any of the three identified \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" locations on this specific sheet.\n\n### (4) Locations of Pull Boxes and Underground Electrical Lines\n**Underground Electric Line:**\nThe electrical feed is designated by a solid blue line. Near the western property boundary, an arrow points to the line with the exact label **\"Underground Electric Line\"**. This blue line forms a continuous loop around the interior of the development, generally following the alignment of the central drive aisles and parking areas. It runs between the front-facing units (Bldgs 1, 3, 8, 7) and the central driveway, and loops behind the central buildings (Bldgs 2, 4) to serve the easternmost units (501-504, 601-604).\n\n**Electrical Pull Boxes:**\nThere are ten (10) distinct boxes along this underground blue line labeled exactly as **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**. Following the loop from the west entrance clockwise:\n1.  On the main incoming line, south of the entrance drive near the western property line.\n2.  Adjacent to the western **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** (between Bldg. 2 and Bldg. 8).\n3.  North of **\"Bldg. 1\"**, roughly aligned with **\"Unit 102\"**.\n4.  North of **\"Bldg. 3\"**, roughly aligned between **\"Unit 301\"** and **\"Unit 302\"**.\n5.  At the northeast corner of the internal loop, north of **\"Unit 502\"**.\n6.  Adjacent to the northeast **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** (east of Bldg. 4).\n7.  Adjacent to the southeast **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** (east of Bldg. 7).\n8.  At the southeast corner of the internal loop, southeast of **\"Unit 604\"**.\n9.  South of **\"Bldg. 7\"**, roughly aligned with **\"Unit 702\"**.\n10. South of **\"Bldg. 8\"**, roughly aligned with **\"Unit 802\"**.\n\n*(Note: There are also numerous other boxes on the blue line labeled exactly as **\"Electrical Meters\"** located on the exterior walls of the buildings).*\n\n### (5) Equipment Specifications or Notes about Transformer Service Types\n*   **None visible.** I have reviewed the title block, the drawing field, the \"Utility Notes,\" and general text. There is no text indicating single-phase vs. three-phase service, KVA ratings, voltage, or specific manufacturer equipment requirements on this sheet. \n\n### (6) Transformer Pad Detail Callouts or Notes Showing Pad Dimensions\n*   **None visible.** The pads are drawn as rectangles to represent their location, but there are no text labels providing dimensions (e.g., \"72x72 pad\"), nor are there any detail callout bubbles (e.g., \"See Detail 1/E-2\") associated with the transformer pads on this sheet.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1432,"outputTokens":1188,"totalTokens":4560,"reasoningTokens":1940},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpe