erior of the development, generally following the alignment of the central drive aisles and parking areas. It runs between the front-facing units (Bldgs 1, 3, 8, 7) and the central driveway, and loops behind the central buildings (Bldgs 2, 4) to serve the easternmost units (501-504, 601-604).\n\n**Electrical Pull Boxes:**\nThere are ten (10) distinct boxes along this underground blue line labeled exactly as **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**. Following the loop from the west entrance clockwise:\n1.  On the main incoming line, south of the entrance drive near the western property line.\n2.  Adjacent to the western **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** (between Bldg. 2 and Bldg. 8).\n3.  North of **\"Bldg. 1\"**, roughly aligned with **\"Unit 102\"**.\n4.  North of **\"Bldg. 3\"**, roughly aligned between **\"Unit 301\"** and **\"Unit 302\"**.\n5.  At the northeast corner of the internal loop, north of **\"Unit 502\"**.\n6.  Adjacent to the northeast **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** (east of Bldg. 4).\n7.  Adjacent to the southeast **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** (east of Bldg. 7).\n8.  At the southeast corner of the internal loop, southeast of **\"Unit 604\"**.\n9.  South of **\"Bldg. 7\"**, roughly aligned with **\"Unit 702\"**.\n10. South of **\"Bldg. 8\"**, roughly aligned with **\"Unit 802\"**.\n\n*(Note: There are also numerous other boxes on the blue line labeled exactly as **\"Electrical Meters\"** located on the exterior walls of the buildings).*\n\n### (5) Equipment Specifications or Notes about Transformer Service Types\n*   **None visible.** I have reviewed the title block, the drawing field, the \"Utility Notes,\" and general text. There is no text indicating single-phase vs. three-phase service, KVA ratings, voltage, or specific manufacturer equipment requirements on this sheet. \n\n### (6) Transformer Pad Detail Callouts or Notes Showing Pad Dimensions\n*   **None visible.** The pads are drawn as rectangles to represent their location, but there are no text 