{"level":30,"time":1776958245568,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JYdJdWYD74aJtDapo81G1U","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Utilities\n     2→\n     3→*Details the planned water and wastewater connections for the project's eight buildings and includes the engineer's sign-off.*\n     4→\n     5→**Utilities**\n     6→Water services will be connected to the existing 8’’ waterline along Valley View Road. Wastewater connections will be provided from the existing 8’’ wastewater line stub located at the northern property corner. Water and wastewater connections will serve all eight buildings.\n     7→\n     8→Sincerely,\n     9→\n    10→[Figure: Professional Engineer Seal of Jason K. Rodgers, License 87881, State of Texas, with signature overlay]\n    11→\n    12→Jason Rodgers\n    13→Project Manager\n    14→Bleyl Engineering\n    15→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"86ce6d80-0b13-4282-a0c1-971fcaa319e8","uuid":"384d7058-fcfd-4d15-8e87-bbcb76076cfa","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/engineer-s-summary-letter/05-utilities.md","content":"# Utilities\n\n*Details the planned water and wastewater connections for the project's eight buildings and includes the engineer's sign-off.*\n\n**Utilities**\nWater services will be connected to the existing 8’’ waterline along Valley View Road. Wastewater connections will be provided from the existing 8’’ wastewater line stub located at the northern property corner. Water and wastewater connections will serve all eight buildings.\n\nSincerely,\n\n[Figure: Professional Engineer Seal of Jason K. Rodgers, License 87881, State of Texas, with signature overlay]\n\nJason Rodgers\nProject Manager\nBleyl Engineering\n","numLines":15,"startLine":1,"totalLines":15}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776958245568,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Kb1s2Dkm2grEC7yUQXG9K4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The engineer's summary letter doesn't address the overhead electric utilities. Now let me systematically evaluate the checklist items. Based on what I've found:\n\n1. There ARE existing overhead electric utilities (poles and lines) on and adjacent to the site (along Valley View Road and northern boundary - confirmed by the Existing Conditions Survey Sheet 4 and vision analysis)\n2. The site has proposed buildings, driveways, landscaping, and other site features\n3. The site plan and landscape plan reference \"overhead electric\" lines\n\nNow I need to check each checklist item to see if the plans address the clearance requirements. The key question for each item is: Does the application provide the required documentation?\n\nLet me start evaluating:\n\n**EL-1.1 - Buildings and permanent structures: 7.5-ft horizontal clearance**\n- Applicability: YES - buildings are proposed and overhead lines exist\n- Evidence: Need to check if plans show surveyed overhead conductor elevations and clearance dimensions to building faces\n- Current finding: Sheet 21 shows electrical design but doesn't show surveyed existing overhead conductor elevations\n\n**EL-1.2 - 15-foot radial clearance from distribution primary/neutral conductors**\n- Applicability: YES - if existing lines are distribution (not transmission)\n- Evidence: Need to verify conductor type (distribution vs transmission) and check for clearance dimensions\n\n**EL-1.6 - Buildings maintain clearance from ROW facilities**\n- Applicability: YES - overhead lines exist in/adjacent to Valley View Road ROW\n- Evidence: Need to check setback dimensions from ROW\n\n**EL-1.7 - Surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors on building elevation sheets**\n- Applicability: YES - buildings proposed\n- Evidence: Building elevations need to show surveyed conductor elevations\n- Current finding: I haven't seen building elevation sheets yet - need to check if they exist and if they show overhead conductor data\n\n**EL-1.8 - Section/plan exhibits showing clearance dimensions from conductor to building edges**\n\n\n- Applicability: YES - need section views to verify clearances\n\n**EL-1.23 - Clearances measured from conductor not pole**\n- Applicability: YES - if clearances are shown on plans\n- Evidence: Check all dimension annotations\n\n**EL-31 - Survey by registered surveyor for vertical clearances**\n- Applicability: Depends on whether driveway/parking clearances appear marginal\n\n**EL-1.37 - Trees: 10 lateral feet from overhead distribution, 50 lateral feet from overhead transmission**\n- Applicability: YES - landscape plan shows tree plantings\n- Evidence: Check landscape plan tree locations relative to utility poles\n\n**EL-1.40 - Down guy wires conflicting with accessible paths/driveways**\n- Applicability: Need to check if down guys from poles are shown and if they conflict\n\n**EL-1.46 - 48-hour notification note on cover sheet**\n- Applicability: YES\n- Evidence: Check cover sheet for required notation\n\nI should systematically review the plans to identify what evidence exists. I'll need to look for building elevation sheets, section views showing vertical clearances, cover sheet notes, tree locations on the landscape plan, and driveway clearances. Starting by determining whether building elevations are present.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":445,"cache_read_input_tokens":57983,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":445},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management