is sheet calling them out. \n\n**6. Clearance Zones or Exclusion Areas**\nThere are **no clearance zones, exclusion areas, or designated keep-out areas** drawn or labeled on this landscape plan around any potential transformer locations. The only utility-related delineations clearly visible are \"SD\" (Storm Drain) lines, \"LOC\" (Limits of Construction) lines, and \"OHE\" (Overhead Electric) lines along the southern property boundary.","providerOptions":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}]}]},"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolvedProvider":"vertex","resolvedProviderApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","fallbacksAvailable":["google"],"planningReasoning":"System credentials planned for: vertex, google. Total execution order: vertex(system) → google(system)","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","finalProvider":"vertex","modelAttemptCount":1,"modelAttempts":[{"modelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","success":true,"providerAttemptCount":1,"providerAttempts":[{"provider":"vertex","internalModelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","providerApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","credentialType":"system","success":true,"startTime":1593893.394471,"endTime":1660992.692351,"statusCode":200,"providerResponseId":"IjrqaZujA7CZyOgP8efz4Aw"}]}],"totalProviderAttemptCount":1},"cost":"0.052224","marketCost":"0.052224","inferenceCost":"0.052224","inputInferenceCost":"0.00306","outputInferenceCost":"0.049164","generationId":"gen_01KPXF64ZB18AYZYGTKFA1E94Q"}}}]},"msg":"Vision response"}
{"level":30,"time":1776958245572,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Please examine the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21) and provide detailed information about transformer pads shown on this plan:\n\n1. How many transformer pads are shown on the plan?\n2. For each transformer pad, please identify:\n   - Location description (which building or area it serves, spatial position on the plan)\n   - Approximate dimensions (if shown or can be estimated)\n   - Distance to nearby buildings, structures, or site features\n   - Whether the access door orientation is shown or can be inferred\n   - Whether there are any dimension annotations or callouts showing clearances\n3. Are there any notes or details about transformer pad specifications, protection, or special requirements?\n4. Are transformer pads shown with bollards or protective barriers?\n5. What is the distance from transformer pads to parking areas, driveways, or vehicle circulation routes?\n6. Are there any overhead electric lines shown relative to transformer pad locations?\n\nPlease provide spatial details that would help assess compliance with UCM § 1.10.4 clearance requirements (5-foot clearances from buildings, 10-foot hot-stick clearance, fire escape requirements, etc.).","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21), here is the information regarding the transformer pads:\n\n**1. How many transformer pads are shown on the plan?**\nThere are exactly **5** transformer pads explicitly identified with text callout boxes stating \"Electrical Transformer Pad\". \n\n**2. Details for each transformer pad:**\nNone of the transformer pads on this plan have explicit dimension lines, clearance arcs, or hot-stick zones drawn around them. The distances below are visual estimates based on spatial relationships to nearby features, as no strict measurements are provided for them.\n\n*   **Transformer Pad 1 (Northwest):**\n    *   **Location:** West of Building 1 (near Unit 101), situated in the landscape island formed by the curved main entrance driveway.\n    *   **Approximate Dimensions:** Not explicitly dimensioned. Shown as a nested rectangular symbol.\n    *   **Distance to buildings/features:** It is located immediately adjacent to the \"Concrete Curb\" of the driveway. Visual distance to Building 1 appears to be separated only by a standard sidewalk and small landscape buffer, but no distance is dimensioned. \n    *   **Access door orientation:** Not shown or inferable from the symbol.\n    *   **Clearance annotations:** None.\n\n*   **Transformer Pad 2 (Middle West):**\n    *   **Location:** West of Building 2 (near Unit 201), adjacent to the western \"Sidewalk Easement\".\n    *   **Approximate Dimensions:** Not explicitly dimensioned.\n    *   **Distance to buildings/features:** Visually appears to be very close (within a few feet) of the western wall of Building 2.\n    *   **Access door orientation:** Not shown or inferable.\n    *   **Clearance annotations:** None.\n\n*   **Transformer Pad 3 (Southwest):**\n    *   **Location:** West of Building 8 (near Unit 801), adjacent to the western property line and sidewalk.\n    *   **Approximate Dimensions:** Not explicitly dimensioned.\n    *   **Distance to buildings/features:** Sits tightly between the sidewalk and the western wall of Building 8. Visually, it appears nearly flush with or extremely close to the building footprint. \n    *   **Access door orientation:** Not shown or inferable.\n    *   **Clearance annotations:** None.\n\n*   **Transformer Pad 4 (Middle East):**\n    *   **Location:** Centrally located on the eastern side of the site, between Building 5 (south of Unit 504) and Building 4 (east of Unit 404). \n    *   **Approximate Dimensions:** Not explicitly dimensioned.\n    *   **Distance to buildings/features:** Located in a central grassy/landscape area. It visually appears to have more buffer space from the surrounding buildings than the western pads, but no specific distance is noted.\n    *   **Access door orientation:** Not shown or inferable.\n    *   **Clearance annotations:** None.\n\n*   **Transformer Pad 5 (South Central/East):**\n    *   **Location:** Located between Building 7 (near Unit 704) and Building 6 (near Unit 602).\n    *   **Approximate Dimensions:** Not explicitly dimensioned.\n    *   **Distance to buildings/features:** Positioned in a tight corridor/courtyard between the two buildings. \n    *   **Access door orientation:** Not shown or inferable.\n    *   **Clearance annotations:** None.\n\n**3. Are there any notes or details about transformer pad specifications, protection, or special requirements?**\n**No.** There are no notes on this sheet detailing transformer pad specifications, clearances, fire escape proximities, or UCM § 1.10.4 requirements. The only notes present are standard \"Utility Notes\" (regarding horizontal/vertical utility locations and PVC pipe sizing), \"Texas 811\" requirements, and a note about geologist inspection for trenching > 5 feet.\n\n**4. Are transformer pads shown with bollards or protective barriers?**\n**No.** There are no bollards (typically indicated by small circles) or protective barrier lines drawn around any of the five transformer pads, nor are there any callouts mentioning them. \n\n**5. What is the distance from transformer pads to parking areas, driveways, or vehicle circulation routes?**\nWhile exact distances are not dimensioned:\n*   **Pad 1** is drawn immediately adjacent (virtually zero clearance) to the \"Concrete Curb\" of the main vehicle entrance driveway loop. \n*   **Pads 2 and 3** are adjacent to a pedestrian \"Sidewalk Easement\" but do not appear immediately adjacent to vehicular driveways.\n*   **Pads 4 and 5** are located near internal building circulation, but exact proximity to any designated vehicular alleyways or parking areas is not dimensioned.\n\n**6. Are there any overhead electric lines shown relative to transformer pad locations?**\n**Yes.** There is an existing overhead electric line clearly labeled \"**OHE**\" running longitudinally along the entire western boundary of the property line. \n*   Transformer Pads 1, 2, and 3 are located along this western boundary and are in close proximity to this OHE line. \n\n**Summary regarding UCM § 1.10.4 compliance assessment:**\nThis specific sheet does not contain the necessary spatial annotations to verify UCM § 1.10.4 compliance. It lacks dimensioned 5-foot building clearance lines, 10-foot hot-stick workspace zones, door orientations, or identified fire escapes/stairs relative to the pads. Furthermore, Pad 1 is adjacent to a driveway curb without depicted bollard protection, and Pads 2 and 3 visually appear very close to building walls, which would necessitate further dimensioned details to ensure the 5-foot minimum clearance is met.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1552,"outputTokens":1268,"totalTokens":5209,"reasoningTokens":2389},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely f