{"level":30,"time":1776958245573,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":4,"prompt":"Examine the existing conditions survey and identify all utility features shown. Specifically identify: 1) Are there utility poles depicted on or near the site? 2) Are there overhead utility lines (O.H.U.L.) shown? 3) Where are electric easements located? 4) Are there any transformers on pads? 5) What is the spatial relationship between these utilities and the property boundaries? Describe the location and extent of any overhead electric infrastructure visible on this survey sheet.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided Existing Conditions Survey for Valley View Townhomes, here are the findings regarding the utility features requested:\n\n**1) Are there utility poles depicted on or near the site?**\nYes, utility poles are depicted on the survey. Based on the legend symbol for \"UTILITY POLE\" (a circle with a cross or radiating lines), there are poles located primarily along the western frontage near \"VALLEY VIEW ROAD\". At least one utility pole symbol is also visible further inside the property area, near the northern boundary, connecting to an overhead line that crosses into the site.\n\n**2) Are there overhead utility lines (O.H.U.L.) shown?**\nYes, overhead utility lines are shown, designated by the line type labeled **\"- O.H.U.L. -\"** in the legend and on the plan.\n*   One major run of **\"- O.H.U.L. -\"** runs generally parallel to the western property boundary, following the right-of-way of \"VALLEY VIEW ROAD\".\n*   Another segment of **\"- O.H.U.L. -\"** is shown crossing the northern property line (bearing S63°00'28\"E) and traversing across the northern portion of the site, connecting to a utility pole.\n\n**3) Where are electric easements located?**\nElectric easements are located along the side property boundaries (the northern and southern edges of the lot as oriented on the page). They are explicitly labeled on the plan:\n*   Along the upper (northern) property line (S63°00'28\"E 419.86'), there is a dashed line labeled exactly as: **\"5' ELEC. EASEMENT VOL. 84, PG. 74 P.R.T.C.TX\"**.\n*   Along the lower (southern) property line (N63°30'57\"W 414.24'), there is a corresponding dashed line labeled exactly as: **\"5' ELEC. EASEMENT VOL. 84, PG. 74 P.R.T.C.TX\"**.\n\n**4) Are there any transformers on pads?**\nBased on a careful review of the symbols on the plan and the legend, there are no features clearly depicted or explicitly labeled as a transformer on a pad.\n\n**5) What is the spatial relationship between these utilities and the property boundaries? Describe the location and extent of any overhead electric infrastructure visible on this survey sheet.**\n*   **Overhead Lines:** The primary extent of the overhead infrastructure visible is concentrated along the street frontage. The **\"- O.H.U.L. -\"** along \"VALLEY VIEW ROAD\" runs parallel to the property line (N28°04'28\"E 93.20'), appearing to weave slightly inside and outside the exact boundary line. Additionally, an overhead line intrudes into the property, crossing the northern boundary (S63°00'28\"E) to connect to a pole located within the site's footprint.\n*   **Easements:** The electric easements are strictly edge-aligned, occupying a 5-foot strip running parallel and immediately adjacent to the long northern and southern property boundaries (S63°00'28\"E and N63°30'57\"W respectively) for a significant portion of their length.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1411,"outputTokens":730,"totalTokens":5593,"reasoningTokens":3452},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1695804]"},{"type":"text","tex