{"level":30,"time":1776958245574,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan and identify: 1) What electric infrastructure is shown? Include transformers, pull boxes, poles, conduits, and both overhead and underground lines. 2) Where are overhead electric lines and poles shown? Are there any labels indicating voltage level or classification (distribution vs transmission)? 3) Where are underground electric facilities shown? What is their specific location relative to buildings and landscape areas? 4) What is the nearest overhead or underground electric facility to any area where trees might be proposed (near property lines, parking areas, or between buildings)? Provide specific dimensions if shown, or describe spatial relationships to buildings (e.g., \"Building 1\" or \"north side of Building 3\").","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" for Valley View Townhomes, here is the requested information:\n\n**1) Electric Infrastructure Shown**\nThe plan displays a proposed electrical network primarily using a solid blue linetype for routing and blue symbols for equipment. Specific infrastructure identified by exact callout labels includes:\n*   **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**: Pointing to circular blue symbols in multiple locations around the perimeter.\n*   **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**: Pointing to dashed rectangular footprints enclosing blue equipment symbols.\n*   **\"Electrical Meters\"**: Pointing to rectangular boxes attached to the exterior walls of various buildings.\n*   **\"Underground Electric Line\"**: Pointing to the main solid blue lines routing throughout the site.\n*   **Overhead Lines**: Indicated by a dashed line type with the text **\"- OHE -\"**.\n\n**2) Overhead Electric Lines and Poles**\n*   **Location:** Overhead electric lines are shown running north-south along the western edge of the site, parallel to \"Valley View Road\". The line is designated by the text label \"- OHE -\".\n*   **Voltage/Classification:** There are **no labels** indicating specific voltage levels (e.g., 12kV) or classifications (e.g., distribution vs. transmission) on this page.\n\n**3) Underground Electric Facilities Location**\n*   **Location Relative to Buildings and Landscape:** The \"Underground Electric Line\" (solid blue line) forms a continuous loop around the outer perimeter of the townhome development, staying outside the immediate building footprints and central driveways. \n    *   It routes along the north side of Buildings 1, 3, and 4.\n    *   It turns south, routing along the east side of Buildings 4, 5, and 6 (within a \"25' Drainage Easement\").\n    *   It turns west, routing along the south side of Buildings 6, 7, and 8.\n    *   It turns north, routing along the west side of Buildings 8 and 2.\n*   The lines, \"Electrical Pull Box\" units, and \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" locations are situated in the setback areas between the building walls and the property boundary lines, which typically serve as landscape or buffer areas.\n\n**4) Proximity to Potential Tree Areas**\nElectric facilities are located in very close proximity to existing and potential tree areas, primarily along the property boundaries:\n*   **Northern Boundary:** An \"Underground Electric Line\" runs east-west parallel to the northern property line. This line routes directly underneath/through the drawn circular canopies of several large existing trees located north of Buildings 1, 3, and 4. An \"Electrical Pull Box\" is also located in this tree-heavy area near the northwest corner of Building 1.\n*   **Western Boundary (Street Frontage):** The overhead lines (\"- OHE -\") run parallel to the street and appear to pass near or through the canopies of existing trees along the western edge. Furthermore, underground lines, two \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" locations, and multiple \"Electrical Pull Box\" units are located in the space between Buildings 2 & 8 and the western property line, an area that includes existing trees and a \"Sidewalk Easement\".\n*   **Eastern Boundary:** The underground line routes north-south through a \"25' Drainage Easement\" east of Buildings 4, 5, and 6. This type of perimeter setback is a common location for proposed buffer trees. An \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" and \"Electrical Pull Box\" are located in this easement area east of Buildings 5 and 6.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1458,"outputTokens":768,"totalTokens":4997,"reasoningTokens":2771},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final revi