e site, along the southern property line.\n\n### 2) Locations of Proposed Ornamental Trees (Small Tree Symbols)\nProposed smaller/ornamental trees (indicated by smaller circles containing an 'x') are located in the following areas:\n\n*   **North Boundary:** There is a row of four small trees planted just inside the northern property line, intermixed with the large 'M' trees mentioned above.\n*   **East Boundary:** There is one small tree located near the southeast corner of the main building footprint.\n*   **South Boundary:** There is a row of four small trees planted sequentially along the southern property line, west of the large 'M' tree in that area.\n\n### 3) Spatial Relationship Between Tree Locations and Overhead Electric (OHE) Lines\n*   **Location of OHE:** A line explicitly labeled **\"- - - OHE - - -\"** runs along the entire southern boundary of the site plan, positioned just inside the \"LOC\" (Limits of Construction) line and outside the \"SD\" (Storm Drain) line. There are square symbols with an 'x' inside situated along this line, which typically represent utility poles.\n*   **Spatial Relationship:** The row of vegetation proposed along the southern boundary is placed in immediate proximity to this OHE line. Specifically, the four small (ornamental) tree symbols and the one large (shade/mitigation) tree labeled 'M' on the south side are aligned directly parallel to, and appear to be planted almost directly underneath or immediately adjacent to, the overhead electric line path.\n\n### 4) Spatial Relationship Between Tree Locations and Underground Electric Equipment\n*   Based strictly on the visual information provided on this specific Landscape Plan sheet, **there are no identifiable symbols or labels indicating proposed or existing underground electric equipment** (such as pad-mount transformers, pull boxes, or electric vaults). Therefore, a spatial relationship cannot be determined from this document alone.\n\n### 5) Areas Where Trees are Close to (Within 25 Feet of) OHE Conductors or Poles\nUsing the provided graphic scale of **1\" = 20'-0\"**:\n\n*   **Southern Boundary Conflict:** Every proposed tree along the southern boundary is located well within 25 feet of the OHE line.\n    *   Visually applying the scale bar to the drawing, the center points of the four small tree symbols and the one large 'M' tree symbol along the south property line appear to be less than 5 feet away from the dashed line representing the OHE conductors.\n    *   Furthermore, there is a utility pole symbol (square with an 'x') near the southeast corner of the site. The large tree labeled 'M' is located extremely close to this pole symbol, estimated to be within 10 to 15 feet of the pole itself, and directly adjacent to the OHE line extending from it.\n*   **Conclusion:** The entire row of proposed planting along the southern edge of the site presents a significant proximity conflict (well under the 25-foot threshold) with the overhead electric lines depicted on the plan.","providerOptions":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}]}]},"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolvedProvider":"vertex","resolvedProviderApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","fallbacksAvailable":["google"],"planningReasoning":"System credentials planned for: vertex, google. Total execution order: vertex(system) → google(system)","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","finalProvider":"vertex","modelAttemptCount":1,"modelAttempts":[{"modelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","success":true,"providerAttemptCount":1,"providerAttempts":[{"provider":"vertex","internalModelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","providerApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","credentialType":"system","success":true,"startTime":4118685.514101,"endTime":4178493.093221,"statusCode":200,"providerResponseId":"HTrqafWfFc-AxtUP1ZOMyQ0"}]}],"totalProviderAttemptCount":1},"cost":"0.044814","marketCost":"0.044814","inferenceCost":"0.044814","inputInferenceCost":"0.002934","outputInferenceCost":"0.04188","generationId":"gen_01KPXF609W5HXPJHREB3D6ESNP"}}}]},"msg":"Vision response"}
{"level":30,"time":1776958245575,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine Sheet 9 (Site Plan) and identify all features adjacent to or near the three transformer pad locations that are described on the electrical plan as: (1) West Side transformer - located west of Bldg. 2 and north of Bldg. 8 in a landscaped island, (2) Northeast/Center transformer - located east of parking for Bldg. 4, (3) Southeast/Center transformer - located east of parking for Bldg. 7. For each transformer location, identify: (a) buildings and units nearby with distances if possible, (b) parking areas and their distances, (c) fire lanes or circulation areas, (d) trees or vegetation areas, (e) any visible retaining walls or structures, (f) sidewalks or pedestrian areas, (g) any easements marked, (h) water features like the pond. Also describe the layout of the site generally - where are the buildings positioned, where is parking, where is the pond, and what features would require clearance from transformers per typical utility requirements.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided site plan (Sheet 9), here is a detailed description of the site layout and the specific features surrounding the three inferred transformer pad locations.\n\n### General Site Layout\n*   **Buildings Position:** The site contains 8 multi-family residential buildings (Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8). They are arranged around a central core of parking and drive aisles. Buildings 1, 3, 4, and 5 form a northern perimeter; Buildings 2 and 8 are on the western side; and Buildings 6 and 7 are on the eastern/southern side.\n*   **Parking:** Parking is primarily centralized in the interior of the development, organized in rows facing the buildings or drive aisles, including parallel, standard, and compact spaces.\n*   **Pond:** A \"Biofiltration / Detention Pond\" is located in the far northeast corner of the site, enclosed by a \"Pond Perimeter Fence\" and a \"Concrete Retaining Wall\".\n*   **Typical Utility Clearance:** The transformer pads are depicted as solid squares surrounded by a dashed perimeter box. Per typical utility requirements, these dashed boxes represent mandatory clearance zones (often 10 feet in front of access doors and 3-5 feet on the sides/rear) that must remain free of structures, vehicles, retaining walls, and deep-rooted vegetation.\n\n---\n\n### Transformer Pad Locations & Surrounding Features\n\nThe site plan explicitly labels one transformer pad with \"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\" and utilizes an identical symbol (a solid square surrounded by a dashed clearance box) in other corresponding locations.\n\n#### 1. West Side Transformer\n**Location:** West of Bldg. 2 and north of Bldg. 8, situated in a prominent landscaped island.\n*   **(a) Buildings/Units Nearby:** Directly east is **Bldg. 2** (Units 201-206). Directly south is **Bldg. 8** (Units 801-806). The exact distance is not dimensioned, but it is separated from the buildings by a standard two-way drive aisle.\n*   **(b) Parking Areas:** There are no parking spaces immediately adjacent to this island; the nearest parking is further east past Bldg. 2.\n*   **(c) Fire Lanes/Circulation:** The island is entirely surrounded by the primary vehicular drive aisle/fire lane. The aisle is marked **\"26'\"** wide to the north of the island and **\"29.8'\"** wide to the south.\n*   **(d) Trees/Vegetation:** The island is explicitly labeled as a **\"Tree Well\"** with a note stating **\"need to look up approp. detail\"**.\n*   **(e) Retaining Walls/Structures:** None are visible in or immediately adjacent to this island.\n*   **(f) Sidewalks/Pedestrian Areas:** A \"Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk\" wraps around the perimeter of Buildings 2 and 8, across the drive aisle from the transformer pad. A crosswalk is indicated across the drive aisle connecting to Bldg. 8.\n*   **(g) Easements:** A \"Sidewalk Easement\" runs generally near the western entry, but no specific utility easement is demarcated with lines directly over the pad on this sheet.\n*   **(h) Water Features:** None nearby; the pond is on the opposite side of the site.\n\n#### 2. Northeast/Center Transformer\n**Location:** Located east of the central parking row that sits south/southwest of Bldg. 4.\n*   **(a) Buildings/Units Nearby:** **Bldg. 4** (Units 401-405) is to the northwest. **Bldg. 5** (Units 501-504) is to the northeast across the main drive aisle.\n*   **(b) Parking Areas:** Located immediately east of the northern half of the central interior parking row.\n*   **(c) Fire Lanes/Circulation:** Bounded by parking spaces to its west and a main drive aisle to its east (which routes traffic toward Buildings 5 and 6).\n*   **(d) Trees/Vegetation:** Situated within a landscaped peninsula/end-cap that separates the parking spaces from the eastern drive aisle. Directly north of this peninsula is an area labeled **\"Common Open Space 4,960 sf\"**.\n*   **(e) Retaining Walls/Structures:** None immediately adjacent.\n*   **(f) Sidewalks/Pedestrian Areas:** Sidewalks are located across the drive aisle to the east (running along Bldg. 5) and to the north along the Common Open Space.\n*   **(g) Easements:** No distinct easement lines are drawn directly over this peninsula.\n*   **(h) Water Features:** The detention pond is further north/northeast, well separated by buildings and infrastructure.\n\n#### 3. Southeast/Center Transformer\n**Location:** Located east of the central parking row that sits north of Bldg. 7.\n*   **(a) Buildings/Units Nearby:** **Bldg. 7** (Units 701-705) is to the southwest. **Bldg. 6** (Units 601-604) is directly east across the drive aisle.\n*   **(b) Parking Areas:** Located immediately east of the southern half of the central interior parking row. A label pointing to the end of the adjacent parking row indicates **\"Bollard (Typ)\"**.\n*   **(c) Fire Lanes/Circulation:** Bounded by the parking spaces to its west and a drive aisle to its east. The drive aisle to the east is dimensioned at **\"24'\"** wide.\n*   **(d) Trees/Vegetation:** Situated within a landscaped peninsula/end-cap separating the parking from the drive aisle, identical in arrangement to the Northeast/Center transformer.\n*   **(e) Retaining Walls/Structures:** None immediately adjacent. (Note: Farther east, near the property line behind Bldg. 6, labels indicate **\"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\"** and **\"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\"**, but these are well away from the transformer).\n*   **(f) Sidewalks/Pedestrian Areas:** Sidewalks run adjacent to Bldg. 6 across the drive aisle to the east, and along Bldg. 7 to the south.\n*   **(g) Easements:** No specific easement demarcations cover the pad. A **\"25' Drainage Easement\"** exists farther to the east near the property line.\n*   **(h) Water Features:** None nearby.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1520,"outputTokens":1402,"totalTokens":6830,"reasoningTokens":3908},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the bro