unning along Bldg. 5) and to the north along the Common Open Space.\n*   **(g) Easements:** No distinct easement lines are drawn directly over this peninsula.\n*   **(h) Water Features:** The detention pond is further north/northeast, well separated by buildings and infrastructure.\n\n#### 3. Southeast/Center Transformer\n**Location:** Located east of the central parking row that sits north of Bldg. 7.\n*   **(a) Buildings/Units Nearby:** **Bldg. 7** (Units 701-705) is to the southwest. **Bldg. 6** (Units 601-604) is directly east across the drive aisle.\n*   **(b) Parking Areas:** Located immediately east of the southern half of the central interior parking row. A label pointing to the end of the adjacent parking row indicates **\"Bollard (Typ)\"**.\n*   **(c) Fire Lanes/Circulation:** Bounded by the parking spaces to its west and a drive aisle to its east. The drive aisle to the east is dimensioned at **\"24'\"** wide.\n*   **(d) Trees/Vegetation:** Situated within a landscaped peninsula/end-cap separating the parking from the drive aisle, identical in arrangement to the Northeast/Center transformer.\n*   **(e) Retaining Walls/Structures:** None immediately adjacent. (Note: Farther east, near the property line behind Bldg. 6, labels indicate **\"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\"** and **\"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\"**, but these are well away from the transformer).\n*   **(f) Sidewalks/Pedestrian Areas:** Sidewalks run adjacent to Bldg. 6 across the drive aisle to the east, and along Bldg. 7 to the south.\n*   **(g) Easements:** No specific easement demarcations cover the pad. A **\"25' Drainage Easement\"** exists farther to the east near the property line.\n*   **(h) Water Features:** None nearby.","providerOptions":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}]}]},"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-