ASEMENT VOL. 84, PG. 74 P.R.T.C.TX\"**.\n\n**4) Are there any transformers on pads?**\nBased on a careful review of the symbols on the plan and the legend, there are no features clearly depicted or explicitly labeled as a transformer on a pad.\n\n**5) What is the spatial relationship between these utilities and the property boundaries? Describe the location and extent of any overhead electric infrastructure visible on this survey sheet.**\n*   **Overhead Lines:** The primary extent of the overhead infrastructure visible is concentrated along the street frontage. The **\"- O.H.U.L. -\"** along \"VALLEY VIEW ROAD\" runs parallel to the property line (N28°04'28\"E 93.20'), appearing to weave slightly inside and outside the exact boundary line. Additionally, an overhead line intrudes into the property, crossing the northern boundary (S63°00'28\"E) to connect to a pole located within the site's footprint.\n*   **Easements:** The electric easements are strictly edge-aligned, occupying a 5-foot strip running parallel and immediately adjacent to the long northern and southern property boundaries (S63°00'28\"E and N63°30'57\"W respectively) for a significant portion of their length."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5781b726-3d4c-4d6b-bc37-a1081a1b178a","uuid":"dc7ab77b-69e8-41fd-84db-e6ea7ff600b4","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided Existing Conditions Survey for Valley View Townhomes, here are the findings regarding the utility features requested:\n\n**1) Are there utility poles depicted on or near the site?**\nYes, utility poles are depicted on the survey. Based on the legend symbol for \"UTILITY POLE\" (a circle with a cross or radiating lines), there are poles located primarily along the western frontage near \"VALLEY VIEW ROAD\". At least one utility pole symbol is also visible further inside the property area, near the northern boundary, connecting to an overhead line that crosses into the site.\n\n**2) Are 