uildings 1, 3, and 4.\n    *   It turns south, routing along the east side of Buildings 4, 5, and 6 (within a \"25' Drainage Easement\").\n    *   It turns west, routing along the south side of Buildings 6, 7, and 8.\n    *   It turns north, routing along the west side of Buildings 8 and 2.\n*   The lines, \"Electrical Pull Box\" units, and \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" locations are situated in the setback areas between the building walls and the property boundary lines, which typically serve as landscape or buffer areas.\n\n**4) Proximity to Potential Tree Areas**\nElectric facilities are located in very close proximity to existing and potential tree areas, primarily along the property boundaries:\n*   **Northern Boundary:** An \"Underground Electric Line\" runs east-west parallel to the northern property line. This line routes directly underneath/through the drawn circular canopies of several large existing trees located north of Buildings 1, 3, and 4. An \"Electrical Pull Box\" is also located in this tree-heavy area near the northwest corner of Building 1.\n*   **Western Boundary (Street Frontage):** The overhead lines (\"- OHE -\") run parallel to the street and appear to pass near or through the canopies of existing trees along the western edge. Furthermore, underground lines, two \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" locations, and multiple \"Electrical Pull Box\" units are located in the space between Buildings 2 & 8 and the western property line, an area that includes existing trees and a \"Sidewalk Easement\".\n*   **Eastern Boundary:** The underground line routes north-south through a \"25' Drainage Easement\" east of Buildings 4, 5, and 6. This type of perimeter setback is a common location for proposed buffer trees. An \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" and \"Electrical Pull Box\" are located in this easement area east of Buildings 5 and 6."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f55948b1-ec2a-4bd4-944a-41435f27a914","uuid":"686f6f56-0058-4f5e-8e14-5c95cd4