{"level":30,"time":1776958253786,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_016HUuXhq1suuUUDH1yh9CKV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0173y9bLfgATYQQs1TGtgj95","name":"mcp__conductor_tools__vision","input":{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Please examine the Site Plan (Sheet 9) for transformer-related information:\n\n1. Are transformer pads shown on this site plan? If so, how many and where?\n2. Are transformer pad clearances dimensioned on this plan (distances to buildings, structures, sidewalks, property lines)?\n3. Are property lines and easements clearly shown that would affect transformer pad placement?\n4. Are there any dumpsters, fire hydrants, fire lanes, or other site features shown that would require clearance from transformer pads (5 feet from dumpsters, 20 feet from fire escapes, 15 feet from fire lanes, etc.)?\n5. Are there any sidewalks shown relative to transformer pads?\n6. Are any retaining walls shown near transformer pad locations?\n7. What parking areas or vehicle circulation routes are shown relative to transformer pad locations?\n8. Are there any dimension callouts or notes about transformer pad protection or special requirements?\n\nThis will help assess compliance with UCM § 1.10.4 clearance requirements shown on the primary site plan."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1932,"cache_read_input_tokens":56201,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1932},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ea0af40-45f3-4b07-b50e-bf4188546a20","uuid":"2f758804-2936-4fbc-9c5d-18ea3fb97077"}
{"level":30,"time":1776958253787,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Please examine the Site Plan (Sheet 9) for transformer-related information:\n\n1. Are transformer pads shown on this site plan? If so, how many and where?\n2. Are transformer pad clearances dimensioned on this plan (distances to buildings, structures, sidewalks, property lines)?\n3. Are property lines and easements clearly shown that would affect transformer pad placement?\n4. Are there any dumpsters, fire hydrants, fire lanes, or other site features shown that would require clearance from transformer pads (5 feet from dumpsters, 20 feet from fire escapes, 15 feet from fire lanes, etc.)?\n5. Are there any sidewalks shown relative to transformer pads?\n6. Are any retaining walls shown near transformer pad locations?\n7. What parking areas or vehicle circulation routes are shown relative to transformer pad locations?\n8. Are there any dimension callouts or notes about transformer pad protection or special requirements?\n\nThis will help assess compliance with UCM § 1.10.4 clearance requirements shown on the primary site plan.","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (9)"}
{"level":30,"time":1776958253792,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Lr9RctkrAsxhuwQkidn9DN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Let me examine the fire protection plan for fire hydrant and fire lane locations relative to transformers:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3355,"cache_read_input_tokens":46023,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3355},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01b15f0e-4ea6-438f-b485-676df5e8b514","uuid":"66fbfa2a-3448-42d3-bb8d-a59ab7b9c7ee"}
{"level":30,"time":1776958254372,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_018WToz5YtGac6RBZU1FkK83","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! Now I have a much better understanding of the site and the transformer locations. Let me now look at what measures I need to take. Looking at the checklist items, I need to verify clearances for:\n\n1. Buildings (5 feet minimum for most cases)\n2. Retaining walls (5 feet minimum)\n3. Fences (5 feet for sides with operators/controls, 3 feet for sides without)\n4. Windows/doors/ventilating ducts (5 feet lateral or 12 feet horizontal depending on conditions)\n5. Sidewalks (2 feet from back of sidewalk)\n6. Fire hydrants (5 feet)\n7. Underground utilities (5 feet horizontal clearance from water/wastewater/storm drain, 12-36 inches from gas, 12 inches from other utilities)\n8. Overhead lines (7.5 feet sky-to-ground, 15-foot radius clearance)\n9. Trees (10 lateral feet minimum, 15 feet from overhead distribution)\n10. Dumpsters (5 feet)\n11. Bike racks (5 feet)\n12. Light poles (5 feet)\n13. Fire lanes (15 feet)\n14. Other transformer pads (5 feet)\n15. Parking/vehicle routes (bollards required if within 4 feet)\n\nFrom what I've seen, the transformers are in landscaped islands adjacent to parking areas. Let me measure the distances between the transformers and the adjacent parking areas, buildings, and other features. I need the scale to do this properly. The scale is 1\" = 20', which means scaleInchesPerFoot = 0.05.\n\nLet me start by measuring distances. Based on the vision analysis:\n- West Side Transformer: adjacent to a drive aisle that's 26' to 29.8' wide, surrounded by a tree well\n- Northeast/Center Transformer: east of parking row, adjacent to a main drive aisle \n\n\n- Southeast/Center Transformer: east of parking row, adjacent to a 24' wide drive aisle, with bollards noted\n\nNow I need to measure the specific distances from each transformer to adjacent buildings, parking areas, fire lanes, utilities, and sidewalks. Let me check the blocks.md for Sheet 9 to get more detail on the site plan so I can identify which measurements to prioritize.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2096,"cache_read_input_tokens":49119,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2096},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4d02d4bb-637b-4cb0-b747-3ac89c84ec14","uuid":"df440421-7663-45b5-b7d7-0189cbce9474"}
