{"level":30,"time":1776960409202,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan very carefully. Does the plan show:\n1. Any surveyed elevations or locations of existing overhead electric conductors (poles, lines)?\n2. Any dimension annotations showing clearances between buildings/driveways and overhead electric facilities?\n3. Any notes or callouts regarding overhead utility clearance requirements from Austin Energy or UCM?\n4. Any profile or section views showing vertical clearances?\n5. What electric infrastructure is proposed (underground vs overhead)? \n\nBe specific about what is or is not shown on this sheet.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" (Sheet 21 of 39), here are the findings regarding your specific questions:\n\n1.  **Surveyed elevations or locations of existing overhead electric conductors:**\n    *   The plan shows an existing utility line running north-south along the western boundary (Valley View Road) labeled with \"**OHE**\" (Overhead Electric).\n    *   However, the plan **does not show** any surveyed elevations for these overhead lines, nor does it specifically call out pole locations with corresponding elevation or survey data on this plan view.\n\n2.  **Dimension annotations showing clearances:**\n    *   **None are shown.** There are no dimension lines or annotations indicating specific horizontal or vertical clearances between the proposed buildings/driveways and the existing overhead electric facilities.\n\n3.  **Notes or callouts regarding overhead utility clearance requirements:**\n    *   **None are shown.** There are no notes referencing Austin Energy, UCM (Utility Criteria Manual), or any specific overhead utility clearance requirements on this sheet. The \"Utility Notes\" block does not mention overhead clearances.\n\n4.  **Profile or section views showing vertical clearances:**\n    *   **None are shown on this sheet.** The entire drawing is a plan (top-down) view.\n    *   *Note:* There is a callout pointing to the western boundary area that explicitly states \"**See Sht. 19 for Profile**\", indicating that profile views exist elsewhere in the broader plan set.\n\n5.  **Proposed electric infrastructure (underground vs. overhead):**\n    *   The proposed electric infrastructure is explicitly shown as **underground**.\n    *   The design uses solid blue lines routed throughout the site, which are identified by callouts as \"**Underground Electric Line**\" (pointed out twice, once on the far west near the property line and once centrally near Bldg. 4).\n    *   The proposed system routes to at-grade or pad-mounted equipment, specifically labeling \"**Electrical Pull Box**\"es, \"**Electrical Transformer Pad**\"s, and \"**Electrical Meters**\" at the buildings, which is standard for an underground routing design. There are no proposed overhead lines or poles shown for the new infrastructure.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1423,"outputTokens":472,"totalTokens":3683,"reasoningTokens":1788},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf th