{"level":30,"time":1776960409205,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MM7FqyvzCy8GA4xC24FMV1","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" (Sheet 21 of 39), here are the findings regarding your specific questions:\n\n1.  **Surveyed elevations or locations of existing overhead electric conductors:**\n    *   The plan shows an existing utility line running north-south along the western boundary (Valley View Road) labeled with \"**OHE**\" (Overhead Electric).\n    *   However, the plan **does not show** any surveyed elevations for these overhead lines, nor does it specifically call out pole locations with corresponding elevation or survey data on this plan view.\n\n2.  **Dimension annotations showing clearances:**\n    *   **None are shown.** There are no dimension lines or annotations indicating specific horizontal or vertical clearances between the proposed buildings/driveways and the existing overhead electric facilities.\n\n3.  **Notes or callouts regarding overhead utility clearance requirements:**\n    *   **None are shown.** There are no notes referencing Austin Energy, UCM (Utility Criteria Manual), or any specific overhead utility clearance requirements on this sheet. The \"Utility Notes\" block does not mention overhead clearances.\n\n4.  **Profile or section views showing vertical clearances:**\n    *   **None are shown on this sheet.** The entire drawing is a plan (top-down) view.\n    *   *Note:* There is a callout pointing to the western boundary area that explicitly states \"**See Sht. 19 for Profile**\", indicating that profile views exist elsewhere in the broader plan set.\n\n5.  **Proposed electric infrastructure (underground vs. overhead):**\n    *   The proposed electric infrastructure is explicitly shown as **underground**.\n    *   The design uses solid blue lines routed throughout the site, which are identified by callouts as \"**Underground Electric Line**\" (pointed out twice, once on the far west near the property line and once centrally near Bldg. 4).\n    *   The proposed system routes to at-grade or pad-mounted equipment, specifically labeling \"**Electrical Pull Box**\"es, \"**Electrical Transformer Pad**\"s, and \"**Electrical Meters**\" at the buildings, which is standard for an underground routing design. There are no proposed overhead lines or poles shown for the new infrastructure."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"86ce6d80-0b13-4282-a0c1-971fcaa319e8","uuid":"7e761564-3c32-40ac-b0c8-750aebaa757e","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" (Sheet 21 of 39), here are the findings regarding your specific questions:\n\n1.  **Surveyed elevations or locations of existing overhead electric conductors:**\n    *   The plan shows an existing utility line running north-south along the western boundary (Valley View Road) labeled with \"**OHE**\" (Overhead Electric).\n    *   However, the plan **does not show** any surveyed elevations for these overhead lines, nor does it specifically call out pole locations with corresponding elevation or survey data on this plan view.\n\n2.  **Dimension annotations showing clearances:**\n    *   **None are shown.** There are no dimension lines or annotations indicating specific horizontal or vertical clearances between the proposed buildings/driveways and the existing overhead electric facilities.\n\n3.  **Notes or callouts regarding overhead utility clearance requirements:**\n    *   **None are shown.** There are no notes referencing Austin Energy, UCM (Utility Criteria Manual), or any specific overhead utility clearance requirements on this sheet. The \"Utility Notes\" block does not mention overhead clearances.\n\n4.  **Profile or section views showing vertical clearances:**\n    *   **None are shown on this sheet.** The entire drawing is a plan (top-down) view.\n    *   *Note:* There is a callout pointing to the western boundary area that explicitly states \"**See Sht. 19 for Profile**\", indicating that profile views exist elsewhere in the broader plan set.\n\n5.  **Proposed electric infrastructure (underground vs. overhead):**\n    *   The proposed electric infrastructure is explicitly shown as **underground**.\n    *   The design uses solid blue lines routed throughout the site, which are identified by callouts as \"**Underground Electric Line**\" (pointed out twice, once on the far west near the property line and once centrally near Bldg. 4).\n    *   The proposed system routes to at-grade or pad-mounted equipment, specifically labeling \"**Electrical Pull Box**\"es, \"**Electrical Transformer Pad**\"s, and \"**Electrical Meters**\" at the buildings, which is standard for an underground routing design. There are no proposed overhead lines or poles shown for the new infrastructure."}]}
{"level":30,"time":1776960409205,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine the site plan and identify: 1) Are any existing utility poles or overhead lines shown on this plan? 2) Are clearance dimensions or notes indicating clearances from overhead utilities visible? 3) What is the proximity of the proposed buildings (Buildings 1-8) to any overhead utility lines that may exist based on the existing conditions? 4) Are there any dimensions, notes, or specifications showing horizontal or vertical clearances from overhead electric facilities? 5) Does the plan show surveyed conductor elevations or vertical clearance information? Describe what clearance documentation is or is not present on this site plan.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided site plan document, here are the findings regarding your specific questions:\n\n1) **Existing utility poles or overhead lines:**\nYes, existing overhead utility lines are shown on the plan. They are represented by a dashed line type containing the text `- OHE -` (indicating Overhead Electric). These lines are visible in two primary locations:\n*   Running longitudinally along the western boundary of the site, parallel to the adjacent roadway/driveway.\n*   Running horizontally along the southern boundary line of the site.\nUtility poles are also indicated along these `- OHE -` routes, typically represented by small circle symbols (for example, there is a prominent pole symbol near the bottom left intersection of the western and southern `- OHE -` lines). Additionally, there is an \"AT&T Pole\" explicitly labeled in the top left corner near the \"Wastewater Service Connection\". \n\n2) **Clearance dimensions or notes indicating clearances from overhead utilities:**\nNo explicit clearance dimensions or general safety notes indicating required clearances from the overhead utilities are visible on this plan sheet. There are no references to \"OSHA\" clearances or specific utility provider setback standards in the \"Site Plan Release Notes\" or any other text blocks.\n\n3) **Proximity of proposed buildings (Buildings 1-8) to overhead utility lines:**\nBased on the existing conditions shown in the 2D layout:\n*   **Bldg 1** is the closest structure to the western `- OHE -` line. There is a dimension of `78.21'` originating near Bldg 1 and pointing toward the western property boundary, but this dimensions the setback to the property line/R.O.W., not specifically to the utility line.\n*   **Bldg 7** and **Bldg 8** are the closest structures to the southern `- OHE -` line. While they are situated near the southern edge of the development footprint, there are no specific dimensions indicating the exact distance from the exterior walls of Buildings 7 or 8 to the `- OHE -` line. \n*   None of the proposed buildings (1-8) appear to be placed directly underneath the designated `- OHE -` lines.\n\n4) **Dimensions, notes, or specifications showing horizontal or vertical clearances:**\nThere are no dimensions, notes, or specifications visible anywhere on this sheet that explicitly define or verify horizontal or vertical clearances specifically for overhead electric facilities.\n\n5) **Surveyed conductor elevations or vertical clearance information:**\nThe plan does not show any surveyed conductor elevations, wire heights, or vertical clearance information for the overhead lines. While standard site elevations are provided (such as Finished Floor Elevations like `FFE = 687.50` and site Benchmarks like `Elevation = 679.52'`), there is no corresponding Z-axis/elevation data provided for the utility poles or the overhead wires themselves.\n\n**Summary of Clearance Documentation:**\nClearance documentation specifically pertaining to overhead utility safety and setbacks is **absent** from this particular site plan sheet. While the physical footprints of the `- OHE -` lines and poles are mapped in the 2D plane along the western and southern boundaries, there are no attached conductor elevations, explicit horizontal dimension ties from buildings to the wires, or specific utility clearance notes provided.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1433,"outputTokens":697,"totalTokens":4629,"reasoningTokens":2499},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the site plan and identify: 1) Are any existing utility poles or overhead lines shown on this plan? 2) Are clearance dim