{"level":30,"time":1776960409205,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Please examine the Site Plan (Sheet 9) for transformer-related information:\n\n1. Are transformer pads shown on this site plan? If so, how many and where?\n2. Are transformer pad clearances dimensioned on this plan (distances to buildings, structures, sidewalks, property lines)?\n3. Are property lines and easements clearly shown that would affect transformer pad placement?\n4. Are there any dumpsters, fire hydrants, fire lanes, or other site features shown that would require clearance from transformer pads (5 feet from dumpsters, 20 feet from fire escapes, 15 feet from fire lanes, etc.)?\n5. Are there any sidewalks shown relative to transformer pads?\n6. Are any retaining walls shown near transformer pad locations?\n7. What parking areas or vehicle circulation routes are shown relative to transformer pad locations?\n8. Are there any dimension callouts or notes about transformer pad protection or special requirements?\n\nThis will help assess compliance with UCM § 1.10.4 clearance requirements shown on the primary site plan.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided Site Plan (Sheet 9), here is the information regarding transformer pads and related features:\n\n**1. Are transformer pads shown on this site plan? If so, how many and where?**\nYes, one location is explicitly labeled. On the western (left) side of the site plan, south of the main entrance driveway, there is a rectangular box labeled \"**Transformer Pad (Typ.)**\". It is located along the western property line, west of Building 1 and Building 8. \n\n**2. Are transformer pad clearances dimensioned on this plan (distances to buildings, structures, sidewalks, property lines)?**\nNo. There are no dimension lines or distance callouts shown indicating the clearance from the transformer pad to the adjacent sidewalk, property line, buildings, or other structures.\n\n**3. Are property lines and easements clearly shown that would affect transformer pad placement?**\nYes, the heavy solid/dashed line denoting the property boundary is clearly shown immediately to the west of the transformer pad. Additionally, there is a \"**Sidewalk Easement Doc# [unclear]**\" indicated by a dashed line running parallel to the property line in the vicinity of the pad. \n\n**4. Are there any dumpsters, fire hydrants, fire lanes, or other site features shown that would require clearance from transformer pads?**\n*   **Fire Hydrants:** Fire hydrants (labeled \"**FH**\") are shown on the plan (e.g., near the street in the northwest corner, and near Building 4/Bldg 5), but none are shown near the transformer pad. \n*   **Dumpsters:** There are no dumpsters or trash enclosures shown near the transformer pad (a \"Trash Collection Notes\" section is present, but no physical pad is drawn nearby).\n*   **Fire Lanes:** The main drive aisle is shown, but it is not explicitly hatched or labeled as a fire lane near the pad. \nNone of these specific features appear in close enough proximity to the pad to visually suggest a clearance conflict.\n\n**5. Are there any sidewalks shown relative to transformer pads?**\nYes. A sidewalk runs generally north-south and passes immediately adjacent to the east side of the transformer pad. A leader nearby points to this path with the text \"**Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk See Dtl 432S-1**\".\n\n**6. Are any retaining walls shown near transformer pad locations?**\nNo. Retaining walls are indicated elsewhere on the plan (e.g., a note stating \"**Begin Concrete Retaining Wall**\" is located further south along the western boundary), but no retaining walls are shown adjacent to the transformer pad.\n\n**7. What parking areas or vehicle circulation routes are shown relative to transformer pad locations?**\nThe main internal vehicle drive aisle and the parallel parking spaces serving Building 1 and Building 8 are located to the east of the transformer pad. The vehicle areas are separated from the transformer pad by the 5' concrete sidewalk and a landscaped area that includes a \"**Tree Well**\".\n\n**8. Are there any dimension callouts or notes about transformer pad protection or special requirements?**\nNo. There are no notes regarding bollards, physical protection, or specific clearance requirements. The only text pointing directly to the pad reads \"**Transformer Pad (Typ.)**\" with a smaller note immediately beneath it stating \"**need to look up approx. detail**\".","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1531,"outputTokens":722,"totalTokens":4852,"reasoningTokens":2599},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Please examine the Site Plan (Sheet 9) for transformer-related information:\n\n1. Are transformer pads shown on this site plan? If so, how many and where?\n2. Are transformer pad clearances dimensioned on this plan (distances to buildings, structures, sidewalks, property lines)?\n3. Are property lines and easements clearly shown that would affect transformer pad placement?\n4. Are there any dumpsters, fire hydrants, fire lanes, or other site features shown that would require clearance from transformer pads (5 feet from dumpsters, 20 feet from fire escapes, 15 feet from fire lanes, etc.)?\n5. Are there any sidewalks shown relative to transformer pads?\n6. Are any retaining walls shown near transformer pad locations?\n7. What parking areas or vehicle circulation routes are shown relative to transformer pad locations?\n8. Are there any dimension callouts or notes about transformer pad protection or special requirements?\n\nThis will help assess compliance with UCM § 1.10.4 clearance requirements shown on the primary site plan."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-NYuRsA0M37k9AE3waUBjJKMy","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encod