n**2. Positioning of proposed Buildings 1-8 relative to existing overhead lines:**\n*   **Buildings 1 and 8:** These buildings are located on the western side of the site and are positioned parallel and adjacent to the **\"OHE\"** line running along Valley View Road.\n*   **Buildings 6 and 7:** These buildings are located on the eastern side of the site and are positioned parallel and adjacent to the **\"OHE\"** line running along the eastern property boundary.\n*   **Buildings 2, 3, 4, and 5:** These buildings are located in the interior of the site and are not directly adjacent to the perimeter overhead lines.\n\n**3. Clearance dimensions shown between proposed buildings and existing overhead utility lines:**\n**No.** There are no specific dimension lines or callouts indicating the clearance distance between the proposed building structures (Buildings 1, 8, 6, or 7) and the actual overhead electric lines (\"OHE\"). The plan does show dimension lines for building setbacks relative to the property lines (e.g., a \"20.0'\" setback near Bldg 8; a \"15.0'\" setback near Bldg 1; a \"25'\" setback near Bldg 6), but it does not dimension the distance to the utility lines themselves.\n\n**4. Location of existing utility poles conflicting with proposed site features:**\nThere are utility poles located in close proximity to proposed access points on the western boundary (Valley View Road):\n*   There is a pole symbol located immediately adjacent to the northern proposed entrance, labeled **\"Construct Type II Driveway See Detail 4/CS-2\"**. It appears to be sitting just outside or right on the edge of the proposed driveway apron and adjacent sidewalk.\n*   There is another pole symbol located near the southern proposed entrance, labeled **\"Construct Type II Driveway See Detail 1/CS-2\"**. It sits near the existing edge of pavement where the new driveway connects.\n*   *Note: While they are in very close proximity to the proposed driveway improvements, the plan does not definitively indicate a physical conflict requiring removal.*\n\n**5. Notes or callouts regarding clearances from overhead electric facilities:**\n**None found.** I reviewed the \"Site Plan Release Notes,\" \"Accessibility Notes,\" \"Lighting Note,\" \"Trash Collection Notes,\" and other general notes on the page. There are no notes stating required OSHA or utility provider clearance dimensions (either horizontal or vertical) from the overhead electric facilities.\n\n**6. Are existing utility poles shown as \"to be relocated\" or \"to remain\"?**\n**No.** The utility poles are depicted with symbols, but there are no callouts, labels, or notes pointing to these specific poles indicating whether they are \"to remain\" or \"to be relocated.\" Near the top-left pole, there is text identifying an \"Existing Water Meter\" and \"Utility Pole,\" but it does not dictate its disposition.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1481,"outputTokens":790,"totalTokens":4469,"reasoningTokens":2198},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just 