{"level":30,"time":1776960409207,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013i2yFFoM2SiBMVTyAQKhSM","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided site plan document, here are the findings regarding your specific questions:\n\n1) **Existing utility poles or overhead lines:**\nYes, existing overhead utility lines are shown on the plan. They are represented by a dashed line type containing the text `- OHE -` (indicating Overhead Electric). These lines are visible in two primary locations:\n*   Running longitudinally along the western boundary of the site, parallel to the adjacent roadway/driveway.\n*   Running horizontally along the southern boundary line of the site.\nUtility poles are also indicated along these `- OHE -` routes, typically represented by small circle symbols (for example, there is a prominent pole symbol near the bottom left intersection of the western and southern `- OHE -` lines). Additionally, there is an \"AT&T Pole\" explicitly labeled in the top left corner near the \"Wastewater Service Connection\". \n\n2) **Clearance dimensions or notes indicating clearances from overhead utilities:**\nNo explicit clearance dimensions or general safety notes indicating required clearances from the overhead utilities are visible on this plan sheet. There are no references to \"OSHA\" clearances or specific utility provider setback standards in the \"Site Plan Release Notes\" or any other text blocks.\n\n3) **Proximity of proposed buildings (Buildings 1-8) to overhead utility lines:**\nBased on the existing conditions shown in the 2D layout:\n*   **Bldg 1** is the closest structure to the western `- OHE -` line. There is a dimension of `78.21'` originating near Bldg 1 and pointing toward the western property boundary, but this dimensions the setback to the property line/R.O.W., not specifically to the utility line.\n*   **Bldg 7** and **Bldg 8** are the closest structures to the southern `- OHE -` line. While they are situated near the southern edge of the development footprint, there are no specific dimensions indicating the exact distance from the exterior walls of Buildings 7 or 8 to the `- OHE -` line. \n*   None of the proposed buildings (1-8) appear to be placed directly underneath the designated `- OHE -` lines.\n\n4) **Dimensions, notes, or specifications showing horizontal or vertical clearances:**\nThere are no dimensions, notes, or specifications visible anywhere on this sheet that explicitly define or verify horizontal or vertical clearances specifically for overhead electric facilities.\n\n5) **Surveyed conductor elevations or vertical clearance information:**\nThe plan does not show any surveyed conductor elevations, wire heights, or vertical clearance information for the overhead lines. While standard site elevations are provided (such as Finished Floor Elevations like `FFE = 687.50` and site Benchmarks like `Elevation = 679.52'`), there is no corresponding Z-axis/elevation data provided for the utility poles or the overhead wires themselves.\n\n**Summary of Clearance Documentation:**\nClearance documentation specifically pertaining to overhead utility safety and setbacks is **absent** from this particular site plan sheet. While the physical footprints of the `- OHE -` lines and poles are mapped in the 2D plane along the western and southern boundaries, there are no attached conductor elevations, explicit horizontal dimension ties from buildings to the wires, or specific utility clearance notes provided."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5781b726-3d4c-4d6b-bc37-a1081a1b178a","uuid":"d80b4581-119f-4a0e-a3a6-cd8fd1ee54a2","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided site plan document, here are the findings regarding your specific questions:\n\n1