h-south section (between Bldg 4 and Bldg 5).\n    *   **26'**: Labeled in the southern east-west section (south of Bldg 8 and Bldg 7).\n\n### 3. Relationship between Transformer Pad Locations and Fire Features\n*Important Note: Specific transformer pads are not drawn, labeled, or dimensioned on this specific \"Fire Protection Plan\" sheet. Therefore, exact distance measurements (like \"within 15 feet\") from the pads cannot be confirmed from this image alone. However, based on the general areas you provided, here are the fire features located in those zones on this plan:*\n\n*   **Northwest area (west of Building 1):** The main entrance drive (a designated 26' wide \"Fire Lane\") passes immediately south of this area. The off-site \"Existing Fire Hydrant\" is located further north/northwest of this general area.\n*   **West side (adjacent to Building 2, Unit 201):** The 26' wide \"Fire Lane\" runs immediately west and north of this unit. The westernmost \"Proposed Fire Hydrant\" is located across the drive aisle to the southwest of this unit.\n*   **Southwest area (adjacent to Building 8, Unit 801):** The 26' wide \"Fire Lane\" runs immediately west and south of this unit. The westernmost \"Proposed Fire Hydrant\" is located to the northwest of this unit, near the site entrance.\n*   **East area (adjacent to Building 4, Unit 404):** The drive aisle immediately east of this unit is labeled as a \"Fire Lane\" with a dimension of 27.3'. There are no fire hydrants shown in the immediate vicinity of this specific unit on this plan.\n*   **Central courtyard area (between Buildings 6 and 7):** The \"Proposed Fire Hydrant\" (labeled with \"FH\") is located directly in the paved area to the southwest of Building 6 and southeast of Building 7. The drive aisle curving through this area is part of the continuous \"Fire Lane\" loop.\n\n**Answers to specific sub-questions based strictly on this sheet:**\n*   **Are any transformer pads located within or adjacent to fire lanes?** W