{"level":30,"time":1776960414604,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_018VDocjdw5WXViAV4iTNw2h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The vision tool failed. Let me try with a different approach - I'll examine the landscape plan blocks.md more carefully, which I already have.\n\nActually, I already read Sheet 31's guide.md and blocks.md. From Block 2 (the main drawing), I saw that it shows \"Trees and vegetation indicated by various symbols (e.g., circles for trees)\" but doesn't show specific species labels on the drawing itself.\n\nFrom Block 5 (key notes), I saw that trees are labeled as:\n- SY - STREET YARD TREE\n- PL - PARKING LOT TREE\n- P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\n- M - MITIGATION TREE\n\nBut these are category labels, not species names.\n\nThe plant schedule is on Sheet 35, not Sheet 31. And Sheet 32 is the existing tree list.\n\nSo the question is: Are the proposed trees on the landscape plan (Sheet 31) properly cross-referenced to the plant schedule (Sheet 35)?\n\nLet me think about what the checklist items require:\n\n**EL-2.10**: \"Plant legend or plant schedule does not identify species of trees proposed near electric facilities\" - This requires checking if species are identified specifically for trees near electric facilities.\n\n**EL-2.11**: \"Large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) not differentiated on plans to allow verification of clearances from overhead electric facilities\" - This requires that large trees be differentiated.\n\n**EL-2.14**: \"Trees not shown on landscape plan in relation to overhead electric facilities, preventing clearance verification\" - This requires that trees and OHE be shown together.\n\nLet me check if the landscape plan shows both trees and OHE infrastructure clearly.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1050,"cache_read_input_tokens":59677,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1050},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8dbaef9-50fb-4056-bee6-2c0dccabc43f","uuid":"cb93f0bd-c567-4711-817a-3f9b2fa67bc6"}
{"level":30,"time":1776960414852,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_017XBSbEGtTd9BRsC5jAvs2e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! This is very revealing. The site plan shows:\n\n**CRITICAL FINDINGS:**\n1. Overhead electric lines (- OHE -) ARE shown on the site plan\n2. They run along the western boundary (parallel to Valley View Road) and southern boundary\n3. Buildings 1, 7, and 8 are closest to these overhead lines\n4. **NO clearance dimensions or vertical clearance information is documented on the plan**\n5. **NO surveyed conductor elevations are provided**\n6. **NO explicit clearance notes indicating compliance with clearance requirements**\n\nThis is a significant deficiency. According to the grouping requirements (EL-1.7, EL-1.8, EL-1.23, EL-1.31, etc.), when buildings are proposed within potential clearance distance of overhead electric facilities, the site plan should include:\n- Surveyed elevations of overhead conductors (EL-1.7)\n- Section/plan view exhibits showing dimensions from outer conductor to buildings (EL-1.8)\n- Clearance dimensions measured from outside conductor (EL-1.23)\n- Registered surveyor mid-span clearance data if clearance appears marginal (EL-1.31)\n\nNow I need to check:\n1. Landscape plan (Sheet 31) for tree placement near overhead facilities\n2. Any building elevation sheets (if they exist) that might show vertical clearances\n3. Grading plan (Sheet 11) to see if any site features might need vertical clearance verification\n\nLet me check the landscape plan next.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1398,"cache_read_input_tokens":59111,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1398},"output_tokens":3