{"level":30,"time":1776960763579,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AWhauRLDPhU6prfxtrtbxB","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 20 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 1: drawing — A profile view of the proposed water line installation, showing elevations, pipe slopes, fittings, and existing ground surface. It details the transition from an existing AC pipe to a new DI pipe, including a reducer, vault, and meter.\n     4→\n     5→A profile view graph with elevation on the y-axis (ranging from 670 to 689) and stationing on the x-axis (from 0+00 to 0+75). The title is \"Wtr-Ln-A\".\n     6→\n     7→Annotations on the profile include:\n     8→- **Sta 0+00.00 Wtr-Ln-A**: Replace AC pipe with DI. Pipe per Note this Sheet. Contractor to Verify Location and Depth Prior to Construction. 8\"x8\" Swivel Cut-in Tee, 8\" Gate Valve. FL 8\": 674.33, FL 8\": 674.33, FL 8\": 674.33.\n     9→- **Existing Ground** line.\n    10→- **Proposed Surface** line.\n    11→- **Existing 8\" AC Pipe to be Replaced with DI Pipe.**\n    12→- **47.0 lf 8\" DI @ 0.00%**\n    13→- **8\"x6\" Reducer**\n    14→- **5.0 lf 6\" DI @ -0.00%**\n    15→- **6\" Fire Demand Meter in 8' x 12' Vault**: See Detail 512-AW-02. FL In 6\": 674.42, FL Out 6\": 674.42.\n    16→- **12.0 lf 6\" DI @ 0.00%**\n    17→- **Property Line** indicated vertically.\n    18→- A note above the graph: \"Restrain all joints from the main to the meter per note this sheet.\" with a dimension line showing \"52' Restraints\" from Sta 0+00 to Sta 0+52.\n    19→\n    20→## Block 2: drawing — A top-down view of a water main utility plan showing the location of proposed and existing water lines, fire hydrants, meters, and valves. The plan includes specific annotations for installing new equipment, replacing existing infrastructure, and restraining joints.\n    21→\n    22→A detailed utility plan drawing showing the layout of water lines and associated infrastructure. \n    23→\n    24→Key features and annotations include:\n    25→- **Replace AC pipe with DI**: Pipe per Note this Sheet. Contractor to Verify Location and Depth Prior to Construction. 8\"x8\" Swivel Cut-in Tee, 8\" Gate Valve.\n    26→- **47.0 lf 8\" DI**\n    27→- **8\"x6\" Reducer**\n    28→- **Install 6\" Gate Valve on Existing 6\" Water Line**\n    29→- **Replace Existing Fire Hydrant with New Fire Hydrant**\n    30→- **6\" Fire Demand Meter in 8' x 12' Vault**: See Detail 512-AW-02.\n    31→- **8\" x 2\" Service Clamp**: 2\" Copper Service Tubing, 3/4\" Irrigation Meter with 3/4\" DCVA BFP. See Detail 520-AW-01B.\n    32→- **5.0 lf 6\" DI**\n    33→- **3.0 lf 6\" C900**\n    34→- **5.0 lf 6\" C900**\n    35→- **Sidewalk Easement**: Doc#\n    36→- **Exclusive Water Line Vault Easement**: Doc#\n    37→- Various existing and proposed lines (water, wastewater, electric, storm drain) are indicated by different linetypes and labels (e.g., W, WW, E, SD).\n    38→\n    39→## Block 3: notes — The legal description of the property.\n    40→\n    41→**Legal Description**\n    42→Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n    43→\n    44→## Block 4: notes — A note specifying requirements for restraining joints on water line bends, tees, gate valves, and dead ends.\n    45→\n    46→**Restrained Joints for all Water Line Bends, Tees, Gate Valves & Ends**\n    47→All horizontal and vertical water line bends, tee's, gate valves and dead end's shall be restrained to the water main using factory restrained joint pipe as approved in SPL WW-27F, or, mechanical joint restraint devices as approved in SPL WW-27A.\n    48→\n    49→Release of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her submittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n    50→\n    51→The location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\n    52→\n    53→## Block 5: notes — A note regarding the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule and requirements for trenching inspections by a geologist.\n    54→\n    55→**Note**\n    56→This project is subject to the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule (COA ECM 1.12.0 and COA Item No. 658S of the SSM) provision that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist (Texas P.G.) or a geologist's representative.\n    57→\n    58→## Block 7: notes — General notes regarding utility verification prior to construction.\n    59→\n    60→1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\n    61→2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\n    62→\n    63→## Block 8: notes — A note regarding the requirement for a pressure reducing valve.\n    64→\n    65→**PRV Note**\n    66→Lots/Structure with 65 psi or greater require a pressure reducing valve, set at 65 psi, to be installed on the property owner's side of the right of way.\n    67→\n    68→## Block 9: notes — A legend explaining the symbols and linetypes used in the utility plan drawings.\n    69→\n    70→| Symbol/Linetype | Description |\n    71→|---|---|\n    72→| — W — | Existing Water Line |\n    73→| — **W** — | Proposed Water Line |\n    74→| [black square half filled diagonally] | Single Water Service |\n    75→| [black square fully filled] | Double Water Service |\n    76→| — WW — | Existing Wastewater Line |\n    77→| — **WW** — | Proposed Wastewater Line |\n    78→| [line with an arrow] | Wastewater Service |\n    79→| — RW — | Existing Reclaimed Water Line |\n    80→| — **RW** — | Proposed Reclaimed Water Line |\n    81→| — E — | Proposed Underground Electric |\n    82→| — SD — | Proposed Storm Drain |\n    83→| FH | Fire Hydrant |\n    84→| [valve symbol] | Gate Valve |\n    85→| [circle with dot] | AARV |\n    86→| [square with T] | Transformer Pad |\n    87→\n    88→## Block 10: notes — Instructions for replacing existing AC pipe with DI pipe and handling the asbestos pipe.\n    89→\n    90→**Water Tap Note**\n    91→The existing AC pipe must be replaced with DI pipe and a Tee cut into the DI pipe. The AC pipe must be worked on by a certified company that is licensed to handle AC pipes and the pipe disposed of in a pre-approved landfill for Asbestos pipe. Dispose of AC pipe per STATE regulations.\n    92→\n    93→## Block 11: notes — Information on the benchmarks used for elevation reference.\n    94→\n    95→**Benchmarks**\n    96→B.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    97→Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    98→\n    99→B.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n   100→Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n   101→\n   102→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"86ce6d80-0b13-4282-a0c1-971fcaa319e8","uuid":"b0d5e693-20d5-42dd-9ad4-f8161d24bf21","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-20/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 20 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 1: drawing — A profile view of the proposed water line installation, showing elevations, pipe slopes, fittings, and existing ground surface. It details the transition from an existing AC pipe to a new DI pipe, including a reducer, vault, and meter.\n\nA profile view graph with elevation on the y-axis (ranging from 670 to 689) and stationing on the x-axis (from 0+00 to 0+75). The title is \"Wtr-Ln-A\".\n\nAnnotations on the profile include:\n- **Sta 0+00.00 Wtr-Ln-A**: Replace AC pipe with DI. Pipe per Note this Sheet. Contractor to Verify Location and Depth Prior to Construction. 8\"x8\" Swivel Cut-in Tee, 8\" Gate Valve. FL 8\": 674.33, FL 8\": 674.33, FL 8\": 674.33.\n- **Existing Ground** line.\n- **Proposed Surface** line.\n- **Existing 8\" AC Pipe to be Replaced with DI Pipe.**\n- **47.0 lf 8\" DI @ 0.00%**\n- **8\"x6\" Reducer**\n- **5.0 lf 6\" DI @ -0.00%**\n- **6\" Fire Demand Meter in 8' x 12' Vault**: See Detail 512-AW-02. FL In 6\": 674.42, FL Out 6\": 674.42.\n- **12.0 lf 6\" DI @ 0.00%**\n- **Property Line** indicated vertically.\n- A note above the graph: \"Restrain all joints from the main to the meter per note this sheet.\" with a dimension line showing \"52' Restraints\" from Sta 0+00 to Sta 0+52.\n\n## Block 2: drawing — A top-down view of a water main utility plan showing the location of proposed and existing water lines, fire hydrants, meters, and valves. The plan includes specific annotations for installing new equipment, replacing existing infrastructure, and restraining joints.\n\nA detailed utility plan drawing showing the layout of water lines and associated infrastructure. \n\nKey features and annotations include:\n- **Replace AC pipe with DI**: Pipe per Note this Sheet. Contractor to Verify Location and Depth Prior to Construction. 8\"x8\" Swivel Cut-in Tee, 8\" Gate Valve.\n- **47.0 lf 8\" DI**\n- **8\"x6\" Reducer**\n- **Install 6\" Gate Valve on Existing 6\" Water Line**\n- **Replace Existing Fire Hydrant with New Fire Hydrant**\n- **6\" Fire Demand Meter in 8' x 12' Vault**: See Detail 512-AW-02.\n- **8\" x 2\" Service Clamp**: 2\" Copper Service Tubing, 3/4\" Irrigation Meter with 3/4\" DCVA BFP. See Detail 520-AW-01B.\n- **5.0 lf 6\" DI**\n- **3.0 lf 6\" C900**\n- **5.0 lf 6\" C900**\n- **Sidewalk Easement**: Doc#\n- **Exclusive Water Line Vault Easement**: Doc#\n- Various existing and proposed lines (water, wastewater, electric, storm drain) are indicated by different linetypes and labels (e.g., W, WW, E, SD).\n\n## Block 3: notes — The legal description of the property.\n\n**Legal Description**\nLot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n\n## Block 4: notes — A note specifying requirements for restraining joints on water line bends, tees, gate valves, and dead ends.\n\n**Restrained Joints for all Water Line Bends, Tees, Gate Valves & Ends**\nAll horizontal and vertical water line bends, tee's, gate valves and dead end's shall be restrained to the water main using factory restrained joint pipe as approved in SPL WW-27F, or, mechanical joint restraint devices as approved in SPL WW-27A.\n\nRelease of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her submittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n\nThe location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\n\n## Block 5: notes — A note regarding the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule and requirements for trenching inspections by a geologist.\n\n**Note**\nThis project is subject to the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule (COA ECM 1.12.0 and COA Item No. 658S of the SSM) provision that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist (Texas P.G.) or a geologist's representative.\n\n## Block 7: notes — General notes regarding utility verification prior to construction.\n\n1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\n2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\n\n## Block 8: notes — A note regarding the requirement for a pressure reducing valve.\n\n**PRV Note**\nLots/Structure with 65 psi or greater require a pressure reducing valve, set at 65 psi, to be installed on the property owner's side of the right of way.\n\n## Block 9: notes — A legend explaining the symbols and linetypes used in the utility plan drawings.\n\n| Symbol/Linetype | Description |\n|---|---|\n| — W — | Existing Water Line |\n| — **W** — | Proposed Water Line |\n| [black square half filled diagonally] | Single Water Service |\n| [black square fully filled] | Double Water Service |\n| — WW — | Existing Wastewater Line |\n| — **WW** — | Proposed Wastewater Line |\n| [line with an arrow] | Wastewater Service |\n| — RW — | Existing Reclaimed Water Line |\n| — **RW** — | Proposed Reclaimed Water Line |\n| — E — | Proposed Underground Electric |\n| — SD — | Proposed Storm Drain |\n| FH | Fire Hydrant |\n| [valve symbol] | Gate Valve |\n| [circle with dot] | AARV |\n| [square with T] | Transformer Pad |\n\n## Block 10: notes — Instructions for replacing existing AC pipe with DI pipe and handling the asbestos pipe.\n\n**Water Tap Note**\nThe existing AC pipe must be replaced with DI pipe and a Tee cut into the DI pipe. The AC pipe must be worked on by a certified company that is licensed to handle AC pipes and the pipe disposed of in a pre-approved landfill for Asbestos pipe. Dispose of AC pipe per STATE regulations.\n\n## Block 11: notes — Information on the benchmarks used for elevation reference.\n\n**Benchmarks**\nB.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\nB.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\n","numLines":102,"startLine":1,"totalLines":102}}}
