{"level":30,"time":1776960763582,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Uah2AM3SCqHU64KZxsmRoX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VeLXCeQPfuEty9SX28SGPE","name":"mcp__conductor_tools__vision","input":{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":11,"prompt":"Examine the Grading Plan and identify drainage characteristics around transformer pad locations. The electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows 5 transformer pads in these general areas:\n- Northwest area (west of Building 1)\n- West side (adjacent to Building 2, Unit 201)\n- Southwest area (adjacent to Building 8, Unit 801)\n- East area (adjacent to Building 4, Unit 404)\n- Central courtyard area (between Buildings 6 and 7)\n\nFor each general transformer location area, please:\n1. Describe the surface slope/contours shown\n2. Identify spot elevations or contour lines in that area\n3. Describe which direction drainage/surface water flows (toward or away from buildings)\n4. Note any catch basins, inlets, or drainage swales shown near transformers\n5. Note whether any areas are paved, unpaved, or landscaped\n\nAlso note if any transformer pad locations appear to be in grading easements or restricted areas."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2669,"cache_read_input_tokens":50981,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2669},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01b15f0e-4ea6-438f-b485-676df5e8b514","uuid":"e6b8ba5f-a14e-4279-89b8-aaeb09b16712"}
{"level":30,"time":1776960763583,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":11,"prompt":"Examine the Grading Plan and identify drainage characteristics around transformer pad locations. The electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows 5 transformer pads in these general areas:\n- Northwest area (west of Building 1)\n- West side (adjacent to Building 2, Unit 201)\n- Southwest area (adjacent to Building 8, Unit 801)\n- East area (adjacent to Building 4, Unit 404)\n- Central courtyard area (between Buildings 6 and 7)\n\nFor each general transformer location area, please:\n1. Describe the surface slope/contours shown\n2. Identify spot elevations or contour lines in that area\n3. Describe which direction drainage/surface water flows (toward or away from buildings)\n4. Note any catch basins, inlets, or drainage swales shown near transformers\n5. Note whether any areas are paved, unpaved, or landscaped\n\nAlso note if any transformer pad locations appear to be in grading easements or restricted areas.","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (11)"}
