e \"OHE\" line. Another tree is located just north of the OHE line near the \"H-7\" tag.\n*   **Western Boundary (Left side, Valley View Road):** Numerous trees (labeled SY, M) are proposed along this boundary. However, there is no line explicitly labeled as \"OHE\" drawn along this western edge on this specific plan sheet.\n*   **Eastern Boundary (Right side):** There is no line explicitly labeled as \"OHE\" drawn along the eastern boundary.\n\n**3. Distance estimates between proposed trees and the overhead electric lines (OHE) shown on the plan**\nUsing the graphic scale provided in the bottom right corner (\"SCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\"):\n*   For the trees along the southern boundary near the line labeled \"--OHE--\", the center points of the tree symbols near the bottom right corner appear to be within approximately **0 to 10 feet** horizontally from the OHE line. The drawn circular canopies of these trees overlap the OHE line.\n*   Because no OHE line is visually depicted on the western or eastern boundaries on this sheet, distances cannot be estimated for those areas.\n\n**4. Whether the key notes legend shows tree callouts (SY, PL, P, M) and their locations**\nYes, the legend located on the right side of the sheet (underneath the \"KEY NOTES\" H-1 through H-7) defines these callouts. They are transcribed exactly as follows:\n*   \"**SY** - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n*   \"**PL** - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n*   \"**P** - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\"\n*   \"**M** - MITIGATION TREE\"\n\nThese letter callouts are located inside the circular tree symbols drawn throughout the site plan (e.g., \"SY\" and \"M\" are visible along the western boundary; \"PL\" is visible near the central parking areas).\n\n**5. Any notes or specifications regarding clearances from overhead utilities for landscape plantings**\nA careful review of all text blocks on the sheet—including \"IRRIGATION NOTES\", \"NOTE:\", and \"KEY NOTES\"—reveals **no notes or specifications** regarding clearance distances from overhead utilities for landscape plantings.\n\n**6. Whether the proposed trees appear to be within the required clearance distances (10 feet for distribution lines, 50 feet for transmission lines based on the grouping guidance)**\nBased on visual estimation using the scale:\n*   The trees proposed along the southern boundary line labeled \"--OHE--\" appear to have their trunks located within approximately 0 to 10 feet of the line. Therefore, they appear to be **encroaching within or sitting exactly upon the 10-foot clearance boundary** required for distribution lines, and they are definitively within the 50-foot clearance boundary if it is a transmission line.\n*   Clearance compliance for the trees along Valley View Road cannot be determined from this sheet, as no overhead lines are drawn in that area.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1462,"outputTokens":876,"totalTokens":5119,"reasoningTokens":2781},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a si