{"level":30,"time":1776960796680,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21) and identify:\n1. The locations of all transformers shown on the plan - indicate if they are pad-mounted (ground-level boxes) or underground\n2. The locations of all pull boxes and electrical meters\n3. Any dimensional clearances or notes about clearances from trees or landscape features\n4. The routing of underground electric lines and where they connect to buildings\n\nPlease describe the spatial distribution of these electrical elements across the eight buildings (Bldg. 1-8) on the site. This is needed to verify whether trees might be planted too close to these electrical features.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" (Sheet 21), here are the details regarding the electrical infrastructure and its spatial distribution across the site relative to Buildings 1 through 8.\n\nThe electrical infrastructure is denoted primarily by blue lines, boxes, and symbols.\n\n### 1. Locations and Types of Transformers\nThe plan shows four transformers. All are labeled explicitly as \"Electrical Transformer Pad\", indicating they are pad-mounted (ground-level boxes), not underground.\n*   **West Side (Near property entrance):** There are two transformer pads located on the western edge of the site, near the main ingress/egress curve.\n    *   One is located west/northwest of **Bldg. 1**.\n    *   One is located immediately to the west of **Bldg. 8**.\n*   **East Side (Between buildings):**\n    *   One transformer pad is located in the narrow space between the eastern wall of **Bldg. 4** and the western edge of **Bldg. 5**.\n    *   One transformer pad is located in the narrow space between the southern edge of **Bldg. 6** and the northern edge of **Bldg. 7**.\n\n### 2. Locations of Pull Boxes and Electrical Meters\n**Pull Boxes** (denoted by circles with an 'E' inside and pointing labels):\n*   West property line near the incoming electric line.\n*   Northwest corner of **Bldg. 1**.\n*   West side of **Bldg. 8** (near the northwest corner).\n*   Southwest corner of **Bldg. 8**.\n*   Between the northeast corner of **Bldg. 3** and the northwest corner of **Bldg. 4**.\n*   East of **Bldg. 4**, near the north property line curve.\n*   Southeast corner of **Bldg. 7**.\n*   Far southeast corner of the property boundary.\n\n**Electrical Meters** (denoted by clusters of small rectangles attached to building walls and pointing labels):\n*   **Bldg. 1:** Mounted on the exterior North facade.\n*   **Bldg. 2:** Mounted on the exterior West facade (near the southwest corner).\n*   **Bldg. 3:** Mounted on the exterior North facade.\n*   **Bldg. 4:** Mounted on the exterior North facade.\n*   **Bldg. 5:** Mounted on the exterior East facade.\n*   **Bldg. 6:** Mounted on the exterior East facade.\n*   **Bldg. 7:** Mounted on the exterior South facade.\n*   **Bldg. 8:** Two separate banks of meters are shown on the exterior West facade.\n\n### 3. Dimensional Clearances / Notes about Trees\n*   **Finding:** There are **no** dimensional clearances, setback lines, or text notes indicating required distances between electrical features (transformers, lines, pull boxes) and trees or landscape features on this specific sheet.\n*   Large faint circles representing existing tree canopies are drawn across the site, and the indicated underground electrical lines run directly through or under several of these existing canopies (particularly near Bldgs. 1, 8, and the center spine).\n*   A box labeled \"Tree List\" directs the reader to: \"Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\"\n\n### 4. Routing of Underground Electric Lines\nThe main electrical line, labeled \"Underground Electric Line\", routes through the site as follows:\n*   **Entry:** The main line enters from the far western property boundary.\n*   **Western Split:** Immediately upon entering, it hits a pull box and splits. One branch routes north along the west side of **Bldg. 1** to serve the northern buildings. The other branch routes south along the west side of **Bldg. 8**.\n*   **Central Spine:** A main trunk line runs straight West-to-East through the center of the property. It runs in the space exactly between the northern row of buildings (**Bldg. 2, 3**) and the southern row (**Bldg. 8, 7**).\n*   **Eastern Branches:** As the central spine reaches the eastern half of the site, it branches out:\n    *   A line shoots straight North between **Bldg. 3** and **Bldg. 4**, then wraps around the north side of **Bldg. 4** to a pull box, and drops a line south to the transformer pad between **Bldgs. 4 and 5**.\n    *   A line shoots East and connects to the transformer pad between **Bldgs. 6 and 7**.\n    *   A line continues to the far Southeast corner of the property.\n*   **Connections to Buildings:** Smaller lines (service laterals) branch off from the main underground lines, pull boxes, or transformer pads and route directly to the exterior walls of Buildings 1-8 to connect to the \"Electrical Meters\" banks described in section 2.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1441,"outputTokens":1079,"totalTokens":4740,"reasoningTokens":2220},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21) and identify:\n1. The locations of all transformers shown on the plan - indicate if they are pad-mounted (ground-level boxes) or underground\n2. The locations of all pull boxes and electrical meters\n3. Any dimensional clearances or notes about clearances from trees or landscape features\n4. The routing of underground electric lines and where they connect to buildings\n\nPlease describe the spatial distribution of these electrical elements across the eight buildings (Bldg. 1-8) on the site. This is needed to verify whether trees might be planted too close to these electrical features."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-vauGtUl2hDG4Ptd4YcRwixHt","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-mode