erty line near the incoming electric line.\n*   Northwest corner of **Bldg. 1**.\n*   West side of **Bldg. 8** (near the northwest corner).\n*   Southwest corner of **Bldg. 8**.\n*   Between the northeast corner of **Bldg. 3** and the northwest corner of **Bldg. 4**.\n*   East of **Bldg. 4**, near the north property line curve.\n*   Southeast corner of **Bldg. 7**.\n*   Far southeast corner of the property boundary.\n\n**Electrical Meters** (denoted by clusters of small rectangles attached to building walls and pointing labels):\n*   **Bldg. 1:** Mounted on the exterior North facade.\n*   **Bldg. 2:** Mounted on the exterior West facade (near the southwest corner).\n*   **Bldg. 3:** Mounted on the exterior North facade.\n*   **Bldg. 4:** Mounted on the exterior North facade.\n*   **Bldg. 5:** Mounted on the exterior East facade.\n*   **Bldg. 6:** Mounted on the exterior East facade.\n*   **Bldg. 7:** Mounted on the exterior South facade.\n*   **Bldg. 8:** Two separate banks of meters are shown on the exterior West facade.\n\n### 3. Dimensional Clearances / Notes about Trees\n*   **Finding:** There are **no** dimensional clearances, setback lines, or text notes indicating required distances between electrical features (transformers, lines, pull boxes) and trees or landscape features on this specific sheet.\n*   Large faint circles representing existing tree canopies are drawn across the site, and the indicated underground electrical lines run directly through or under several of these existing canopies (particularly near Bldgs. 1, 8, and the center spine).\n*   A box labeled \"Tree List\" directs the reader to: \"Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\"\n\n### 4. Routing of Underground Electric Lines\nThe main electrical line, labeled \"Underground Electric Line\", routes through the site as follows:\n*   **Entry:** The main line enters from the far western property boundary.\n*   **Western Split:** Immediately upon entering, it hits a pull box and splits. One branch routes north along the west side of **Bldg. 1** to serve the northern buildings. The other branch routes south along the west side of **Bldg. 8**.\n*   **Central Spine:** A main trunk line runs straight West-to-East through the center of the property. It runs in the space exactly between the northern row of buildings (**Bldg. 2, 3**) and the southern row (**Bldg. 8, 7**).\n*   **Eastern Branches:** As the central spine reaches the eastern half of the site, it branches out:\n    *   A line shoots straight North between **Bldg. 3** and **Bldg. 4**, then wraps around the north side of **Bldg. 4** to a pull box, and drops a line south to the transformer pad between **Bldgs. 4 and 5**.\n    *   A line shoots East and connects to the transformer pad between **Bldgs. 6 and 7**.\n    *   A line continues to the far Southeast corner of the property.\n*   **Connections to Buildings:** Smaller lines (service laterals) branch off from the main underground lines, pull boxes, or transformer pads and route directly to the exterior walls of Buildings 1-8 to connect to the \"Electrical Meters\" banks described in section 2.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1441,"outputTokens":1079,"totalTokens":4740,"reasoningTokens":2220},"warnings":[],"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolvedProvider":"vertex","resolvedProviderApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","fallbacksAvailable":["google"],"planningReasoning":"System credentials planned for: vertex, google. Total execution order: vertex(system) → google(system)","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","finalProvider":"vertex","modelAttemptCount":1,"modelAttempts":[{"modelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","success":true,"pro