{"level":30,"time":1776961359982,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Rz6iT2fYRBpDQdiWr4YZBA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a MAJOR FINDING:\n\n**Landscape Plan Issues:**\n1. Overhead electric lines (OHE) are shown on the landscape plan\n2. Mitigation trees labeled \"M\" are being planted along the bottom boundary where the OHE line runs\n3. **NO tree species are identified** - can't verify if they're utility-compatible\n4. **NO clearance dimensions or spacing notes** between trees and overhead conductors\n5. The trees appear to be placed directly along/beneath the overhead lines\n6. **NO notes about utility-compatible trees or clearance requirements**\n\nThis is a clear violation of ECM § 2.4.1.D and § 2.4.2.C which requires trees planted within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors must be utility-compatible (from ECM Appendix F, marked \"UC\").\n\nNow I need to check:\n1. Sheet 32 or the tree list to see what species are being planted\n2. Grading plan (Sheet 11) for any driveway clearances\n3. Any building elevation sheets (if they exist)\n\nLet me check the tree list (Sheet 32).","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":935,"cache_read_input_tokens":62237,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":935},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5781b726-3d4c-4d6b-bc37-a1081a1b178a","uuid":"25345402-1d00-4b4c-8c49-7a8c808c3b79"}
