{"level":30,"time":1776961373351,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01QJAqYypwjhtgWhd8uvwgvs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! I now have the tree list. Let me summarize what I see:\n\n**Trees on Site:**\n- Many trees are listed as being removed (marked \"Remove\")\n- Many trees are remaining (marked \"Remain\")\n- The \"APPENDIX F\" column shows which trees are in ECM Appendix F (the Utility Compatible list)\n- Trees marked \"Y\" in the Appendix F column are utility-compatible\n\n**Notable Findings:**\n- Trees that are \"Y\" (Appendix F) are utility-compatible\n- Trees marked \"N\" are NOT on Appendix F - these are NOT utility-compatible\n- Trees marked \"I\" are invasive species\n\nBut I still need to know which MITIGATION trees (the \"M\" trees shown on the landscape plan near the OHE lines) are being planted. The landscape plan showed \"M\" symbols but didn't identify which specific species. I need to check Sheet 35 or another document to see what species are being planted as mitigation.\n\nLet me also check:\n1. Grading plan (Sheet 11) for driveway clearances\n2. Any building elevation sheets\n3. Check if there's more information about the mitigation trees\n\nLet me read Sheet 35 (Landscape Calculations) to see if it specifies the mitigation tree species.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5876,"cache_read_input_tokens":65450,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5876},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5781b726-3d4c-4d6b-bc37-a1081a1b178a","uuid":"16c04654-8849-41a4-93fe-5fd02a2e5138"}
