{"level":30,"time":1776961383915,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PbdXwufDQrbg5KeXqS91v8","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 35 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 4: notes — Plant list section heading.\n     4→\n     5→PLANT LIST\n     6→\n     7→## Block 5: notes — Notes related to the plant list.\n     8→\n     9→NOTES:\n    10→1. THE CONTRACTORS (GENERAL AND SUBCONTRACTORS) SHALL PROVIDE UNIT COSTS FOR ALL\n    11→SOFTSCAPE AND HARDSCAPE MATERIAL SPECIFIED ON THE DRAWINGS AND SPECIFICATIONS. UNIT\n    12→COSTS SHALL BE PROVIDED FOR MATERIALS AND INSTALLATION SEPARATELY. UNIT COSTS SHALL\n    13→BE: 'EACH' FOR PLANT MATERIAL, 'SQUARE FOOT' OR 'SQUARE YARD' FOR PAVEMENTS, LINEAR FOOT\n    14→FOR WALL AND FENCE, 'EACH' FOR SITE FURNISHINGS AND SITE AMENITIES, 'CUBIC YARD' OR 'CUBIC\n    15→FOOT' FOR SOIL, MULCH AND OTHER BULK PRODUCTS AND 'EACH' OR 'LUMP SUM' FOR\n    16→MISCELLANEOUS ITEMS. THE UNIT COST SHALL BE FORMATTED TO HAVE COLUMNS FOR; ITEMS, UNIT,\n    17→UNIT COST, TOTAL ITEM COST.\n    18→2. PLANT QUANTITIES ARE PROVIDED FOR OWNER CONVENIENCE ONLY. CONTRACTOR IS\n    19→RESPONSIBLE FOR VERIFYING AND PROVIDING PLANT QUANTITIES SHOWN ON THE LANDSCAPE PLAN.\n    20→3. CONTRACTOR IS RESPONSIBLE FOR LOCATING AND SECURING TREE AND PLANT MATERIAL IN\n    21→ADVANCE. BECAUSE OF THE LONG LEAD TIME ON THIS INSTALLATION AND THE RECENT SHORTAGE\n    22→ON TREE CROP, CONTRACTOR SHALL RESERVE OR CONTRACT GROW TREES WITH A GROWER.\n    23→\n    24→## Block 6: notes — Notes on special construction techniques.\n    25→\n    26→SPECIAL CONSTRUCTION TECHNIQUES\n    27→ECM 3.5.4 (D)\n    28→1. PRIOR TO EXCAVATION WITHIN TREE DRIP LINES OR THE REMOVAL OF\n    29→TREES ADJACENT TO OTHER TREES THAT ARE TO REMAIN, MAKE A\n    30→CLEAN CUT BETWEEN THE DISTURBED AND UNDISTURBED ROOT ZONES\n    31→WITH A ROCK SAW OR SIMILAR EQUIPMENT TO MINIMIZE ROOT DAMAGE.\n    32→2. IN CRITICAL ROOT ZONE AREAS THAT CANNOT BE PROTECTED DURING\n    33→CONSTRUCTION WITH FENCING AND WHERE HEAVY VEHICULAR TRAFFIC\n    34→IS ANTICIPATED, COVER THOSE AREAS WITH A MINIMUM OF 12 INCHES OF\n    35→ORGANIC MULCH TO MINIMIZE SOIL COMPACTION. IN AREAS WITH HIGH\n    36→SOIL PLASTICITY GEOTEXTILE FABRIC, PER STANDARD SPECIFICATION\n    37→620S, SHOULD BE PLACED UNDER THE MULCH TO PREVENT EXCESSIVE\n    38→MIXING OF THE SOIL AND MULCH. ADDITIONALLY, MATERIAL SUCH AS\n    39→PLYWOOD AND METAL SHEETS, COULD BE REQUIRED BY THE CITY\n    40→ARBORIST TO MINIMIZE ROOT IMPACTS FROM HEAVY EQUIPMENT.\n    41→3. ONCE THE PROJECT IS COMPLETED, ALL MATERIALS SHOULD BE\n    42→REMOVED, AND THE MULCH SHOULD BE REDUCED TO A DEPTH OF 3\n    43→INCHES. PERFORM ALL GRADING WITHIN CRITICAL ROOT ZONE AREAS BY\n    44→HAND OR WITH SMALL EQUIPMENT TO MINIMIZE ROOT DAMAGE.\n    45→4. WATER ALL TREES MOST HEAVILY IMPACTED BY CONSTRUCTION\n    46→ACTIVITIES DEEPLY ONCE A WEEK DURING ACCUMULATION OF THE\n    47→LEAVES.\n    48→5. WHEN INSTALLING CONCRETE ADJACENT TO THE ROOT ZONE OF A TREE,\n    49→USE A PLASTIC VAPOR BARRIER BEHIND THE CONCRETE TO PROHIBIT\n    50→LEACHING OF LIME INTO THE SOIL.\n    51→\n    52→## Block 8: notes — Notes related to tree preservation calculations.\n    53→\n    54→NOTES:\n    55→1. CHINABERRY AND BRADFORD PEAR ARE INVASIVE TREES AND REQUIRE NO MITIGATION.\n    56→2. ASH TREES REQUIRE NO MITIGATION DUE TO EMERALD ASH BORER.\n    57→\n    58→## Block 11: table — Table listing shade trees.\n    59→\n    60→SHADE TREES\n    61→\n    62→| SYM. | QTY. | COMMON NAME, BOTANICAL NAME | MIN. SPEC. |\n    63→|---|---|---|---|\n    64→| [circle with dot] | | EXISTING TREE, TO BE PERSERVED | |\n    65→| [circle with cross] | 2 | LIVE OAK, QUERCUS VIRGINIANA | 100 GAL., 4\" CAL., 16' HT. MINIMUM CONTAINER GROWN |\n    66→| [circle with hash] | 10 | CEDAR ELM, ULMUS CRASSIFOLIA | 100 GAL., 4\" CAL., 16' HT. MINIMUM CONTAINER GROWN |\n    67→\n    68→## Block 12: table — Calculations related to landscaping.\n    69→\n    70→CITY OF AUSTIN\n    71→LANDSCAPE CALCULATIONS:\n    72→\n    73→STREET YARD AREA:\n    74→| | REQUIRED | PROVIDED |\n    75→|---|---|---|\n    76→| TOTAL SITE AREA | N/A | 94,203 SF |\n    77→| TOTAL STREET-YARD AREA | N/A | 6,314 SF |\n    78→| STREET-YARD / LANDSCAPE (20%) | 1,263 SF | 5,206 SF |\n    79→\n    80→STREET YARD TREES:\n    81→EXISTING TREES CREDIT\n    82→| | | |\n    83→|---|---|---|\n    84→| 2\" DIAMETER TO 6\" DIAMETER | 0 | |\n    85→| 6\" DIAMETER OR GREATER | 4 | |\n    86→\n    87→EXISTING TREES CREDIT | PROVIDED |\n    88→|---|---|\n    89→| | 8 CREDITS |\n    90→\n    91→PROPOSED TREES CREDIT | PROVIDED |\n    92→|---|---|\n    93→| | 0 CREDITS |\n    94→\n    95→TOTAL STREET YARD TREES, EXISTING TREES CREDIT PLUS PROPOSED TREES CREDIT:\n    96→| | REQUIRED | PROVIDED |\n    97→|---|---|---|\n    98→| | 5 | 8 |\n    99→\n   100→LANDSCAPE IN PARKING LOTS:\n   101→90SF / 12 PARKING SPACES LOCATED IN SY\n   102→| | REQUIRED | PROVIDED |\n   103→|---|---|---|\n   104→| | 0 | 0 |\n   105→\n   106→60SF / 12 PARKING SPACES LOCATED IN NON SY\n   107→| | REQUIRED | PROVIDED |\n   108→|---|---|---|\n   109→| | 60 | 816 |\n   110→\n   111→LANDSCAPE ISLAND MUST BE WITHIN 50' OF EACH SPACE, 8' MIN. INSIDE WIDTH\n   112→1 TREE MUST BE WITHIN 50' OF EACH SPACE\n   113→\n   114→BUFFERING POINTS FOR DRIVE AISLE:\n   115→| | SIZE | QTY | PREFERRED | OTHER | PROVIDED |\n   116→|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n   117→| LARGE TREE | 4\" | 0 | YES | | 0 |\n   118→| SMALL TREE | 2.5\" | 1 | YES | | 9 |\n   119→| MEDIUM SHRUB | 5 GAL. | 0 | YES | | 0 |\n   120→| LARGE SHRUB | 7 GAL. | 16 | YES | | 48 |\n   121→\n   122→BUFFER POINTS REQUIRED: 40\n   123→BUFFER POINTS PROVIDED: 57\n   124→\n   125→PRIVATE COMMON OPEN SPACE & PEDESTRIAN AMENITIES: SUB CHAPTER E\n   126→REQUIRED (5% OF SITE AREA) (5% X 94,293) 4,715 SF\n   127→PROVIDED 5,855 SF\n   128