umns referencing Appendix F for the *existing surveyed* trees:\n*   \"APPENDIX F (Y/N) OR INVASIVE (I)\"\n*   \"ECM APPENDIX F TREES\"\n*   \"ECM NON-APPENDIX F TREES\"\n\nHowever, nothing on this specific sheet explicitly links \"Appendix F\" to \"Utility Compatible\" status or applies it to new plantings. The only note provided is at the bottom left: \"* TREE SURVEY PROVIDED BY SINCLAIR LAND SURVEYING, INC. SURVEY DATE: 03/28/2023\".\n\n**Conclusion:**\nThis specific sheet is solely a survey and mitigation calculation for *existing* trees. To find information regarding the specific species of *proposed new plantings* and their utility compatibility, you will need to review a different sheet from the site plan, such as a \"Landscape Plan\" or \"Proposed Planting List\"."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"86ce6d80-0b13-4282-a0c1-971fcaa319e8","uuid":"dcd7bf8d-a6f8-4662-93d1-d91f3251d94a","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a meticulous visual analysis of the provided \"Tree List\" document, here are the answers to your questions:\n\n**1. What are the specific tree species listed in the table for NEW plantings (proposed trees)?**\nThere are **no new plantings (proposed trees)** listed on this document. The large table is explicitly titled \"SURVEYED TREES\" and only catalogs *existing* trees found on the site. The \"STATUS\" column only contains two designations for these existing trees: \"Remain\" and \"Remove\". While there is a section for \"REQUIRED TREE MITIGATION\" that calculates the *inches* of mitigation required, it does not specify the actual species to be planted. \n\n**2. For trees being planted within 10-15 feet of the overhead electric facilities (which we know exist on Valley View Road and adjacent boundaries), what species are listed?**\nBecause there is no list of proposed new plantings on this sheet, there is no information available regarding species being planted near overhead electric facilities. Additionally, the table