lationship to transformer pads cannot be determined.\n\n**3. Are fire hydrants shown? If so, what is their distance from transformer pad locations (minimum 5-foot clearance required)?**\nYes, fire hydrants are shown. The plan identifies an \"Existing Fire Hydrant\" in the top left (off-site) and has two callouts for a \"Proposed Fire Hydrant\" (one near the site entrance along the bottom left, and one centrally located marked \"FH\" between Bldg 4 and Bldg 7). However, because no transformer pads are shown on this plan, their distance from the fire hydrants cannot be determined.\n\n**4. Are fire lanes clearly marked or labeled on the plan? If so, are any transformer pads located within 15 feet of fire lanes?**\nYes, \"Fire Lane\" is clearly labeled in multiple locations along the central loop drive. Because transformer pads are not depicted on this plan, it is not possible to determine if any are located within 15 feet of these fire lanes.\n\n**5. Are there dimension callouts showing distances between fire safety features and any transformer pads?**\nNo. Since transformer pads are not shown, there are no dimension lines or callouts indicating distances between them and any fire safety features.\n\n**6. Are there any notes on this plan about electrical equipment placement or clearances from fire protection infrastructure?**\nNo. A review of all text blocks on the sheet—including the \"City of Austin Water and Wastewater Utility\" box, \"Fire Zone Notes\", \"Notes\", \"Fire Flow Test\", and \"Fire Riser Room Note\"—reveals no mention of electrical equipment, transformer pads, or specific clearance requirements for them relative to fire infrastructure.\n\n**7. What is the general spatial relationship between the single private fire hydrant and the transformer pad locations?**\nBecause transformer pads are absent from this drawing, no spatial relationship can be established. *(Note: The plan actually depicts two \"Proposed Fire Hydrant\" locations on the property, rather than a single one).*\n\n**Summary for Validation Purposes:**\nThis particular sheet (Fire Protection Plan) does not contain the necessary information regarding transformer pad locations to validate compliance with UCM § 1.10.4 clearance requirements. This information would likely need to be verified on a dedicated Site Plan, Utility Plan, or Electrical Plan within the broader submission set.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1546,"outputTokens":614,"totalTokens":4339,"reasoningTokens":2179},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2043616]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Please examine the Fire Protection Plan (S