{"level":30,"time":1776961397050,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":32,"prompt":"Please examine the Tree List (Sheet 32) and provide:\n1. What is the source and date of the tree survey?\n2. List all tree species shown on the sheet (both existing trees and proposed/mitigation trees)\n3. For each tree species, identify if it is marked as \"UC\" (Utility Compatible) or if it's suitable for planting near overhead electric lines\n4. Are there any notes about tree species restrictions related to overhead utilities?\n5. Total numbers: How many trees are being removed vs. how many are being planted as mitigation?\n6. Any reference to utility-compatible species from ECM Appendix F?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided image of the Tree List (which is labeled as Sheet **29 of 35** in the bottom right corner, rather than 32), here are the details requested:\n\n**1. What is the source and date of the tree survey?**\n*   **Source:** SINCLAIR LAND SURVEYING, INC.\n*   **Date:** 03/28/2023\n*(Note found in the bottom left corner: \"* TREE SURVEY PROVIDED BY SINCLAIR LAND SURVEYING, INC. SURVEY DATE: 03/28/2023\")*\n\n**2. List all tree species shown on the sheet (both existing trees and proposed/mitigation trees)**\nBased strictly on the \"TREE SPECIES\" column in the \"SURVEYED TREES\" table, the following species are listed:\n*   Live Oak\n*   China Berry\n*   Hackberry\n*   Cedar Elm\n*   Unkown *(transcribed exactly as spelled in row 4012)*\n*   Poplar\n*   Pecan\n*   American Elm\n*   Arizona Ash\n*   Bradford Pear\n*   Pine\n\n*(Note: There are no specific proposed or mitigation tree species listed by name on this sheet; the table only provides mitigation totals in inches).*\n\n**3. For each tree species, identify if it is marked as \"UC\" (Utility Compatible) or if it's suitable for planting near overhead electric lines**\n*   There are no columns, markers, or designations for \"UC\" (Utility Compatible) or suitability for planting near overhead electric lines for any of the tree species on this sheet. \n\n**4. Are there any notes about tree species restrictions related to overhead utilities?**\n*   No. There are no notes regarding overhead utilities or related tree species restrictions anywhere on this sheet.\n\n**5. Total numbers: How many trees are being removed vs. how many are being planted as mitigation?**\n*   **Trees Removed:** By counting the rows where the \"STATUS\" column is explicitly marked as \"Remove\", there are **22** specific surveyed trees designated for removal.\n*   **Trees Planted as Mitigation:** This sheet does not specify the *number* of trees being planted. Instead, it provides a calculation in inches under the \"REQUIRED TREE MITIGATION\" section. The total required mitigation listed at the bottom of the table is **217.00** \"TOTAL INCHES\".\n\n**6. Any reference to utility-compatible species from ECM Appendix F?**\n*   While there is no mention of \"utility-compatible\" species, there are multiple column headers referencing ECM Appendix F exactly as written:\n    *   \"APPENDIX F (Y/N) OR INVASIVE (I)\"\n    *   \"ECM APPENDIX F TREES\"\n    *   \"ECM NON-APPENDIX F TREES\"\n    *   \"REMOVED APPENDIX F TREES 19\"-23.9\"\"\n    *   \"REMOVED APPENDIX F TREES 8\"-18.9\"\"\n    *   \"APPENDIX F TREES 19\"-23.9\" (100%)\"\n    *   \"APPENDIX F TREES 8\"-18.9\" (50%)\"","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1447,"outputTokens":685,"totalTokens":6653,"reasoningTokens":4521},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1495484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze