{"level":30,"time":1776961399244,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01N5XgEKV7E9PLgLjtFAnttX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So Sheet 32 (Tree List) only shows existing surveyed trees, not proposed plantings. The proposed trees would be identified on the Landscape Plan (Sheet 31), but the landscape plan only shows trees as generic symbols (M, SY, PL, P) without species identification.\n\nThis is a deficiency: The landscape plan shows proposed trees being planted but doesn't specify the species or indicate which ones are Utility Compatible.\n\nNow let me consolidate my findings. Based on my comprehensive research, here are the key deficiencies I've identified:\n\n**Summary of Research Findings:**\n\n1. **Overhead electric facilities exist**: Existing overhead utility poles and lines are depicted on the Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4), shown as \"OHE\" on the Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21), and referenced on the Landscape Plan (Sheet 31). These run along Valley View Road (west boundary) and possibly the northern boundary.\n\n2. **Surveyed overhead conductor elevations - NOT PROVIDED**: No sheet shows surveyed elevations of the existing overhead conductors. Sheet 21 references \"See Sht. 19 for Profile\" but Sheet 19 is the Utility Tap Plan for water lines, not a profile showing overhead conductors.\n\n3. **Clearance dimensions - NOT SHOWN**: No dimension lines or callouts show clearances from buildings, driveways, or other site features to the overhead electric facilities.\n\n4. **Building elevations showing overhead conductors - NOT PROVIDED**: No architectural elevation sheets are included in the submittal that would show surveyed conductor elevations relative to building faces and projections.\n\n5. **Section/profile views with vertical clearances - NOT PROVIDED**: No sections or profiles document vertical clearances from overhead conductors to building roofs, driveways, or other site features.\n\n6. **Overhead clearance notes on cover sheet - NOT PROVIDED**: No note on the cover sheet (Sheet 1) addresses the required 48-hour notification to Austin Energy before work near high-voltage overhead lines (Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003).\n \n7. **Proposed trees lack species identification and Utility Compatible designation**: The Landscape Plan shows trees marked as M, SY, and PL positioned near overhead utility lines, but provides no species names or documentation of Utility Compatible status per ECM Appendix F. Trees within 10 feet of overhead lines are not identified as meeting utility compatibility requirements.\n\n8. **Landscape Plan lacks dimensional clearances to overhead facilities**: No distances are dimensionally shown between proposed trees and the overhead utility poles or lines.\n\nNow I need to evaluate each checklist item based on these findings.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":967,"cache_read_input_tokens":80284,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":967},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"86ce6d80-0b13-4282-a0c1-971fcaa319e8","uuid":"c4fd0b80-0f12-4b0d-9dfb-9b99a4ce9ba8"}
