{"level":30,"time":1776961636728,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01HggcmXpP4q1RMD8HQ1z4hZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The grading plan shows building elevations and topography, but the guide doesn't mention anything about overhead utility clearances or driveway vertical clearances. Let me now compile my comprehensive research findings and move to Step 4 (Evaluate Checklist Items).\n\n## RESEARCH SUMMARY - OVERHEAD ELECTRIC CLEARANCES\n\n**EXISTING FACILITIES CONFIRMED:**\n1. ✓ Overhead utility lines (OHE) exist along the western boundary (Valley View Road) and southern boundary\n2. ✓ Utility poles are present near the property\n3. ✓ 5-foot electric easements documented along property boundaries\n4. ✓ Transmission facilities references indicate transmission structures with 25-foot and 20-foot clearance requirements\n\n**PROPOSED BUILDINGS & STRUCTURES:**\n1. ✓ 8 buildings proposed across the site\n2. ✓ Buildings 1, 7, 8 are closest to overhead lines\n3. ✓ Multiple driveways and parking areas\n4. ✓ Retaining walls\n5. ✓ Landscape/mitigation trees\n\n**CLEARANCE DOCUMENTATION - CRITICAL GAPS FOUND:**\n1. ✗ NO surveyed conductor elevations documented on any sheet\n2. ✗ NO vertical clearance dimensions from overhead lines to buildings\n3. ✗ NO section/profile views showing clearances from outer conductor to buildings\n4. ✗ NO clearance dimensions measured from outside conductor (not pole)\n5. ✗ NO 48-hour notification note required for work near overhead lines\n6. ✗ NO building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor data\n7. ✗ NO clearance verification exhibits\n\n**LANDSCAPE/TREE ISSUES - UTILITY COMPATIBILITY VIOLATIONS:**\n1. ✗ Mitigation trees (6 Mexican Redbud, 2 Texas Mountain Laurel) are being planted near overhead lines\n2. ✗ Mexican Redbud and Texas Mountain Laurel are NOT in ECM Appendix F utility-compatible list\n\n\n3. ✗ Landscape plan lacks tree species details needed to confirm utility compatibility\n4. ✗ No spacing or clearance notes between plantings and conductors documented\n5. ✓ Cedar Elm and Live Oak selections do meet utility compatibility standards\n\n**UNABLE TO LOCATE:**\nSurveyed conductor heights, mid-span clearance data, vertical clearances for driveways and parking areas, building elevation sheets with conductor data, measurements from outside conductor rather than pole centerline, 48-hour notification requirements, easement access documentation, and section views with clearance dimensions.\n\nI'm working through the checklist systematically to identify what's present and what's missing from the documentation.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1769,"cache_read_input_tokens":79116,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1769},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5781b726-3d4c-4d6b-bc37-a1081a1b178a","uuid":"483b81ff-d28c-40e1-89cb-847838ec86d3"}
