of buildings and building projections are provided. Clearance verification dimensions are absent from both the site plan and grading plan sheets."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric facilities shown on site plan sheets"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"While overhead electric lines (OHE) are shown on the existing conditions survey and site plan, no clearance dimensions are provided on the plans. Where clearances would typically be dimensioned, they are completely absent. Dimension lines must originate from the outside conductor (not from pole centerline or utility pole), with specific clearance distances documented for all site features within potential clearance zones."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways, parking areas, and buildings with potential marginal overhead clearances"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan data does not include surveyed conductor heights or estimated overhead line elevations. A registered surveyor mid-span clearance survey is required to determine if proposed site features (driveways, parking, buildings) maintain adequate vertical clearance from overhead lines. Without conductor elevation data, compliance cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary where overhead electric lines run and mitigation trees are proposed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Six Mexican Redbud (Cercis canadensis var. mexicana) and two Texas Mountain Laurel (Sophora secundiflora) trees are proposed as mitigation plantings along the southern boundary where overhead electric lines run. These species do not appear in the ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible Shade Trees list and are therefore not acceptable for planting within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors. Additionally, no lateral distance dimensions or clearance documentation between the proposed trees and overhead conductors are provided on the landscape plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Cover sheet or general notes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No plan note requiring owner/contractor notification to Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines is present on the cover sheet, general notes, or site plan. Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003 requires this notification, and it must be documented in the contract documents."}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1769,"cache_read_input_tokens":79116,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1769},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5781b726-3d4c-4d6b-bc37-a1081a1b178a","uuid":"72f52c04-1093-4ca0-b450-83241b982a77"}
