s."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Section views and plan details showing buildings and site features near overhead lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No section or plan view exhibits showing dimensions from the outer electric conductor to the outermost edge of buildings and building projections are provided. Clearance verification dimensions are absent from both the site plan and grading plan sheets."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric facilities shown on site plan sheets"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"While overhead electric lines (OHE) are shown on the existing conditions survey and site plan, no clearance dimensions are provided on the plans. Where clearances would typically be dimensioned, they are completely absent. Dimension lines must originate from the outside conductor (not from pole centerline or utility pole), with specific clearance distances documented for all site features within potential clearance zones."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways, parking areas, and buildings with potential marginal overhead clearances"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan data does not include surveyed conductor heights or estimated overhead line elevations. A registered surveyor mid-span clearance survey is required to determine if proposed site features (driveways, parking, buildings) maintain adequate vertical clearance from overhead lines. Without conductor elevation data, compliance cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary where overhead electric lines run and mitigation trees are proposed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Six Mexican Redbud (Cercis canadensis var. mexicana) and two Texas Mountain Laurel (Sophora secundiflora) trees are proposed as mitigation plantings along the southern boundary where overhead electric lines run. These species do not appear in the ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible Shade Trees list and are therefore not acceptable for planting within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors. Additionally, no lateral distance dimensions or clearance documentation between the proposed trees and overhead conductors are provided on the landscape plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Cover sheet or general notes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No plan note requiring owner/contractor notification to Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines is present on the cover sheet, general notes, or site plan. Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003 requires this notification, and it must be documented in the contract documents."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"28a67438-915f-4130-9e45-527b1e539a85"}
{"level":30,"time":1776961636733,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01EUDJeA6v7T5MH1jonVxmLd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Critical finding from Sheet 19 (Utility Tap Plan): **Transformer pads are NOT shown on this sheet**. The legend indicates they should be shown as a solid square, but they are not actually drawn on the utility plan. This is a major issue - the transformer locations shown on the electrical plan (Sheet 21) are not correlated with the utility plan (Sheet 19).\n\nLet me now compile a summary of what I've found:\n\n## RESEARCH SUMMARY - TRANSFORMER PAD CLEARANCES AND LOCATION REQUIREMENTS\n\n### What I Found:\n\n1. **Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan):**\n   - 5 transformer pads are identified with callout boxes labeled \"Electrical Transformer Pad\"\n   - Locations: NW (west of Bldg 1), W (adjacent Bldg 2/Unit 201), SW (adjacent Bldg 8/Unit 801), E (adjacent Bldg 4/Unit 404), Central (between Bldgs 6 & 7)\n   - NO dimensions for pad size\n   - NO clearance measurements to adjacent features\n   - NO access door orientation shown or indicated\n   - NO information on equipment type (oil-filled vs dry-type)\n   - NO service type specification\n   - NO references to AE Design approval documents\n\n2. **Sheet 9 (Site Plan):**\n   - Building layouts, parking areas shown\n   - No specific transformer pad dimensions or clearances\n   - Fire lane information provided on separate sheet\n\n3. **Sheet 10 (Fire Protection Plan):**\n   - 3 fire hydrants shown (1 existing off-site, 2 proposed on-site)\n   - Fire lanes clearly designated and dimensioned (26' to 27.3' wide)\n   - Transformer pads are NOT shown on this sheet\n   - Transformer locations appear to be ADJACENT to fire lanes (based on location descriptions)\n   - Fire escapes/stairwells NOT shown on this sheet\n   \n4. **Sheet 11 (Grading Plan):**\n   - Drainage flows away from buildings at all transformer locations\n   - Multiple easements cross through transformer pad areas: wastewater, sidewalk, drainage, water/wastewater, greenbelt access, and public utility easements\n   - Transformer pads themselves are not depicted on the grading plan\n   - No drainage details specific to transformer installations\n\n5. **Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan):**\n   - Trees and shrubs shown with categorizations (SY, P\n\n, L, P, M) but no root barriers specified\n   - Transformer locations lack clearance zones or pad delineation\n   - Individual plant species and sizes are not labeled\n\n6. **Sheet 19 (Utility Tap Plan):**\n   - Underground utilities documented with pipe materials and sizes\n   - Transformer pads are conspicuously absent despite being listed in the legend\n   - Cannot verify clearances to transformers without their locations shown\n\n### Missing Information:\n\nTransformer pad dimensions, clearance measurements, access door orientation, and equipment specifications (oil-filled or dry-type) are not documented anywhere in the plans.\n\nAdditionally, several critical items are absent: AE Design approval, bollard specifications for pads near parking areas, fire rating documentation, root barrier details, transformer easement delineations, verification that electrical routing stays on private property, dimensioned pad locations relative to property lines and structures, and overhead distribution line locations on the site plan.\n\nThe transformer pads appear only on Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) but are missing from the Site Plan, Fire Protection Plan, Grading Plan, Utility Tap Plan, and Landscape Plan—preventing verification of clearances from buildings, fire hydrants, drainage patterns, utilities, and vegetation. This coordination gap requires the pads to be added across all relevant sheets with dimensions and clearance callouts clearly marked.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2003,"cache_read_input_tokens":55556,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2003},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01b15f0e-4ea6-438f-b485-676df5e8b514","uuid":"14302356-bc1e-46f1-a99a-01cf7d8a7f5d"}
