{"level":30,"time":1776961636735,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GNdYm6BqxiXaN1JBcfKuti","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Electric Review\n     2→\n     3→*Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.*\n     4→\n     5→Electric Review – Rosemary Avila (512) 972-8488 - rosemary.avila@austinenergy.com\n     6→\n     7→See Bluebeam link below to download AE site comments:\n     8→Link: https://studio.bluebeam.com/share/epcafnizivuefw\n     9→Applicant, for your comment responses use the color BLUE.\n    10→\n    11→Site Plan Preliminary Design Requirements\n    12→Austin Energy Design Criteria Effective December 12th, 2023\n    13→* UCM § 1.3.8 - Customer Electrical Facilities that Cross Property Lines\n    14→* UCM § 1.3.12 - AE Line Extension Policy\n    15→* UCM § 1.3.16- Truck Access to AE Construction and Existing Facility Sites\n    16→* UCM § 1.9.3 - Installation of Metering Equipment\n    17→* UCM § 1.10.3 - Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities\n    18→* UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\n    19→* UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees\n    20→* Appendix F of the Environmental Criteria Manual\n    21→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01b15f0e-4ea6-438f-b485-676df5e8b514","uuid":"1e3c5035-07b5-424b-a81a-5b100a34b18d","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/02-electric-review.md","content":"# Electric Review\n\n*Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.*\n\nElectric Review – Rosemary Avila (512) 972-8488 - rosemary.avila@austinenergy.com\n\nSee Bluebeam link below to download AE site comments:\nLink: https://studio.bluebeam.com/share/epcafnizivuefw\nApplicant, for your comment responses use the color BLUE.\n\nSite Plan Preliminary Design Requirements\nAustin Energy Design Criteria Effective December 12th, 2023\n* UCM § 1.3.8 - Customer Electrical Facilities that Cross Property Lines\n* UCM § 1.3.12 - AE Line Extension Policy\n* UCM § 1.3.16- Truck Access to AE Construction and Existing Facility Sites\n* UCM § 1.9.3 - Installation of Metering Equipment\n* UCM § 1.10.3 - Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities\n* UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\n* UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees\n* Appendix F of the Environmental Criteria Manual\n","numLines":21,"startLine":1,"totalLines":21}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776961636735,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_014zFuS4Jq7d8miNGw9Q845F","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the master comment report references Austin Energy review comments in a Bluebeam link, but that's external to the site plan set. The Electric Review section lists the relevant code sections that apply (UCM § 1.10.4 is explicitly mentioned - that's the main section for transformer pad clearances).\n\nNow I need to complete my evaluation. Based on all my research, here's what I have:\n\n## SUMMARY OF RESEARCH FINDINGS:\n\n### Evidence Found:\n1. **5 transformer pads identified** on Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) with callout boxes\n2. **Locations described but not dimensioned:**\n   - Northwest (west of Building 1)\n   - West (adjacent Building 2, Unit 201)\n   - Southwest (adjacent Building 8, Unit 801)\n   - East (adjacent Building 4, Unit 404)\n   - Central (between Buildings 6 and 7)\n\n3. **Information shown on relevant sheets:**\n   - Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10): Fire lanes, fire hydrants shown but transformer pads NOT shown\n   - Grading Plan (Sheet 11): Drainage direction shown but transformer pads NOT shown\n   - Utility Plan (Sheet 19): Underground utilities shown but transformer pads NOT shown\n   - Landscape Plan (Sheet 31): Plantings shown but transformer pads NOT shown and NO root barriers called out\n   - Site Plan (Sheet 9): Buildings and parking shown but NO transformer pad details\n\n### Critical Information MISSING from the Site Plan:\n1. **Pad dimensions** - no dimensions shown (required to verify clearances)\n2. **Clearance dimensions** to any feature - zero dimensions to buildings, utilities, fire features, trees, parking, etc.\n3. **Access door orientation** - not indicated\n4. **Equipment type** (oil-filled vs. dry-type) - not specified\n5. **Service type** (single-phase vs. three-phase) - not specified\n\n\n6. **Bollard specifications and placement** - not shown\n7. **Transformer easement boundaries** - not delineated\n8. **Root barrier details** - not called out despite trees shown on landscape plan\n9. **Fire rating documentation** - not provided\n10. **AE Design approval documents** (ESPA, transformer pad details, service approvals) - not included\n\n### Coordination Problems:\nThe transformer pads shown on the Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) don't appear on the Site Plan, Fire Protection Plan, Grading Plan, Utility Plan, or Landscape Plan. This creates significant gaps in verifying compliance with clearance requirements, drainage coordination, utility conflicts, and vegetation management around each pad location.\n\nSince the transformer pads lack consistent representation across the drawing set and most clearances aren't dimensioned, I'll need to evaluate the 39 checklist items against what can actually be verified. Most will likely be marked not-verifiable due to missing dimensions and incomplete coordination between sheets. For example, EL-13.1 regarding the 5-foot clearance from buildings and structures cannot be verified because the pads aren't shown on the Site Plan and no dimensions are provided to measure distances. Similarly, EL-13.2 for retaining wall clearances is not-verifiable without dimensional documentation. not shown on building elevation details. Sidewalk clearances cannot be verified since transformer pad locations aren't dimensioned relative to adjacent sidewalks. Stairwell and fire escape locations are missing from the fire protection plan, making it impossible to confirm required separation distances from these features.\n\nHot-stick use areas lack sufficient documentation—transformer pad positioning and access door orientation aren't indicated on the site plan, preventing verification of the 10-foot clearance to open areas or adjacent structures. When confined spaces are present, the 15-foot clearance requirement also cannot be confirmed due to missing niche configurations and access details. Fire hydrant distances are indeterminate because while hydrants appear on Sheet 10, the transformer pads themselves don't appear on that same sheet. Trees serving utility functions remain unidentified on the drawings.\n\nLandscape plan (Sheet 31) doesn't show transformer pad locations relative to vegetation, and overhead lines from Sheet 21 aren't cross-referenced with tree placement, making it impossible to verify species compliance or the 15-foot radius requirement. Shrub clearances from transformer access doors cannot be assessed without knowing pad locations and door orientations. Root barriers for trees within 20 lateral feet of underground equipment are completely absent from the design.\n\nSeveral clearance requirements cannot be verified: dumpster locations lack dimensioning relative to transformer pads, bike racks are shown but not positioned relative to equipment, and light poles aren't clearly identified in relation to transformer locations.\n\nFire lanes are clearly marked on Sheet 10, but transformer pads don't appear on that sheet—based on the electrical plan, they seem positioned immediately adjacent to fire lanes with no clearance dimensions provided. The five transformer pads on Sheet 21 have no spacing dimensions between them. Water and wastewater lines are shown on separate utility sheets but transformer locations aren't included, making clearance verification impossible.\n\nGas service type isn't specified and gas lines aren't shown on the utility plan. Underground utilities lack dimensional verification since transformer pads don't appear on the utility sheet. Overhead distribution lines are shown on Sheet 21 but transformer pad proximity to them isn't dimensioned. No niche service is proposed—all transformers are ground-level installations.\n\nCross-section drawings are missing for the courtyard transformers located between Buildings 6 and 7, which is critical since parking structures and building overhangs are present above or nearby. Equipment type (oil-filled versus dry-type) isn't specified, so drainage requirements can't be verified. Property line dimensions aren't provided to confirm transformer locations are entirely on private property.\n\nThe transformer pad east of Building 4 appears to fall within the Greenbelt Access & Public Utility Easement marked as a NO-BUILD zone per the recorded instrument. No transformer easements are delineated on any plan despite the grouping notes requiring them with AE Design-determined widths. Electrical routing from transformers to meters isn't shown in detail, and transformer pad dimensions don't appear on any sheet.\n\nTransformer pads positioned in the central courtyard parking circulation area lack bollard specifications and details. Bollards are required within 4 feet of parking per UCM § 1.10.4, but no AE Design-approved details are provided. The critical failures are the missing cross-sections for vertical clearances, transformer pads in prohibited easements, absent transformer easement delineations, missing pad dimensions and AE Design details, and absent bollard specifications.\n\nReviewing the easement documentation more carefully—the facts indicate the greenbelt easement (Instrument 2010070731) covers 0.31 acres in the NE interior but isn't depicted on the submitted site plan. The vision tool identified a different instrument number (2016140321) on the grading plan. This discrepancy requires careful verification before concluding whether transformer placement violates easement restrictions.\n\nI've identified several easements that do appear on the plans: drainage, wastewater, water/wastewater, sidewalk, and electric easements. Some of these seem to coincide with transformer pad locations based on the grading plan. I should focus on what the documentation explicitly shows rather than making assumptions about missing depictions.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":641,"cache_read_input_tokens":62279,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":641},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01b15f0e-4ea6-438f-b485-676df5e8b514","uuid":"921b7b62-f70f-4b7f-b531-01c7a25c018e"}
{"level":30,"time":1776961636735,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_014zFuS4Jq7d8miNGw9Q845F","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive research of the site plan documentation, I now need to evaluate each checklist item. Let me compile my findings based on the evidence gathered:\n\n## RESEARCH SUMMARY - Transformer Pad Evidence\n\n**What I Found:**\n- **Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan):** 5 transformer pads shown with callout labels, but NO dimensions, NO clearances, NO access door orientation, NO equipment specifications\n- **Transformer locations described:** NW (Bldg 1), W (Bldg 2), SW (Bldg 8), E (Bldg 4), Central (between Bldgs 6-7)\n- **Critical Coordination Issue:** Transformer pads are shown ONLY on Sheet 21 and are NOT shown on Sheet 9 (Site Plan), Sheet 10 (Fire Protection), Sheet 11 (Grading), Sheet 19 (Utility), or Sheet 31 (Landscape)\n\n**Critical Information MISSING:**\n1. Pad dimensions (required for all clearance verification)\n2. All clearance dimensions to any features\n3. Access door orientation\n4. Equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type)\n5. Service type (single-phase vs. three-phase)\n6. Bollard details (transformer in parking courtyard area - EL-13.38 applies)\n7. Transformer easement boundaries\n8. Root barrier details (multiple trees on landscape plan, EL-13.15 applies)\n9. Cross-section drawings for vertical clearances (EL-13.31 applies)\n10. AE Design approval documents (pad details, service approval)\n\n**Not Verified - Cannot determine from available plans:**\n- Fire hydrant distances (shown on Sheet 10, transformer pads not shown there)\n- Fire lane distances (transformer locations adjacent to fire lanes per Sheet 10 analysis, but no dimensions provided)\n- Underground utility clearances (utilities on Sheet 19, transformer pads not shown)\n- Building clearances (pads not shown on Site Plan Sheet 9 with dimensions)\n- Tree/vegetation clearances (pads not shown on Landscape Plan Sheet 31)\n\nNow let me evaluate each checklist item:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":641,"cache_read_input_tokens":62279,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":641},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01b15f0e-4ea6-438f-b485-676df5e8b514","uuid":"e1fb3928-efeb-482e-b8df-e5f2732bb791"}
{"level":30,"time":1776961636736,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_014zFuS4Jq7d8miNGw9Q845F","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HtXJ86NTuNiJ8a7ZDArxXo","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"13","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.15","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["landscape plantings throughout site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) identifies multiple trees requiring mitigation (marked SY, PL, M categories) within the site but does not provide root barrier detail specifications or dimensions anywhere in the plan set. Root barriers (minimum 4 feet deep, installed 5 feet from equipment per UCM § 1.10.10.4) must be shown on detail sheets for all trees proposed within 20 lateral feet of the underground electrical equipment."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations in parking courtyard and adjacent to buildings"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad locations (Sheet 21) include installations in the central courtyard area between Buildings 6 and 7, which is surrounded by parking structures, garages, and building overhangs. No cross-section drawings are provided demonstrating vertical clearances from transformer pads to parking structures, building overhangs, or other overhead elements. Cross-sections must be provided showing 35-foot minimum clearance for niche configurations or appropriate clearance for exposed pad locations."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all 5 transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad easement boundaries are not delineated on any site plan sheet. UCM § 1.10.3 requires transformer easements to be shown around all pads with width determined by Austin Energy Design for accessibility. The electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pad locations but provides no easement boundary annotations, widths, or reference to easement area calculations."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6"],"applicableAreas":["all 5 transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad dimensions are not specified on any sheet. The electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pad locations with schematic symbols only, without dimensions (length × width). No service type (single-phase or three-phase) is specified. AE Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets required for the specified equipment must be provided to verify pad dimensions comply with Austin Energy requirements."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["central courtyard transformer pad between Buildings 6 and 7"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"A transformer pad is located in the central courtyard area (between Buildings 6 and 7) that is immediately adjacent to and within parking/vehicle circulation areas (fire lane designation shown on Sheet 10). No bollard specifications, details, or placement drawings are provided. UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 requires 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal posts (bollards) when equipment pad is installed within 4 feet of parking areas or vehicle routes, with spacing that allows equipment door opening. Provide AE Design-approved bollard detail showing specifications, spacing, and orientation."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["all 5 transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads are shown on electrical plan (Sheet 21) but not shown on site plan (Sheet 9) with dimensions and clearance annotations. No distances are dimensioned from transformer pad edges to buildings, structures, or foundations. Clearance compliance cannot be verified without dimensional callouts from transformer pads to adjacent structures."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.2","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["retaining wall locations throughout site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining walls are shown on grading plan (Sheet 11) at site perimeter and around pond area. Transformer pad locations not shown on grading plan. No dimensions provided from transformer pads to retaining walls to verify 5-foot clearance requirement."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["if fences present adjacent to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"F