cations exist beneath or adjacent to existing overhead electric facilities shown on the site. Vertical clearance dimensions from the lowest point of overhead facilities to finished driveway grades are not documented on grading plan or section views. Minimum 16-foot clearance (parking without truck traffic) or 18-foot clearance (areas with truck traffic) must be verified with mid-span clearance data."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Site locations where clearance dimensions are shown"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimensions are shown on plans. However, if clearances are dimensioned in future submittals, dimensions must originate from outside conductor location, not from utility pole centerline or pole structure, particularly critical on multi-conductor installations where conductor offset from pole center may be several feet."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape areas adjacent to overhead electric facilities on west and north boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows proposed trees (marked M for mitigation trees) planted in close proximity to existing overhead electric facilities. Trees appear to be within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors based on visual scale analysis. However, specific tree species are not identified on the landscape plan, and no indication is provided of which species are Utility Compatible per ECM Appendix F. Required documentation must specify species for all proposed trees within 50 lateral feet of transmission lines and 10 lateral feet of distribution line