{"level":30,"time":1776961636737,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Enzh5Hi3PBViRmePJNPNEm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! I've successfully output the findings. Let me review what I've identified:\n\n**Fail items (2):**\n1. EL-1.37 - Trees proposed within required clearance distances from overhead facilities without species identification or Utility Compatible confirmation\n2. EL-1.46 - Missing 48-hour notification note on cover sheet\n\n**Not-verifiable items (7):**\n1. EL-1.1 - Building clearances from overhead conductors not documented\n2. EL-1.3 - Building projection clearances not documented\n3. EL-1.6 - Buildings and ROW facility clearances not documented\n4. EL-1.7 - Surveyed overhead conductor elevations not provided on building elevation sheets\n5. EL-1.8 - Section/plan exhibits with clearance dimensions not provided\n6. EL-1.18 - Driveway vertical clearances not documented\n7. EL-1.23 - Dimension origin basis cannot be verified (no dimensions shown yet)\n\nThe other 40 checklist items either:\n- Don't apply to this project (e.g., transmission facilities requirements when only distribution exists, or facilities not proposed like gas pump canopies, transmission line crossing roads, etc.)\n- Are not applicable because the specific feature is not proposed (e.g., emergency access bridges, marquee signs, streetlight poles, etc.)\n\nI believe I've completed a thorough evaluation of the grouping. The key deficiencies are the lack of surveyed overhead conductor data, missing clearance dimensions and profiles, failure to identify proposed tree species and their utility compatibility status, and the missing 48-hour notification note.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2605,"cache_read_input_tokens":81251,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2605},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"86ce6d80-0b13-4282-a0c1-971fcaa319e8","uuid":"d54937b6-d879-4d81-9068-5e82d52a0e61"}
{"level":30,"time":1776961636738,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Enzh5Hi3PBViRmePJNPNEm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary\n\nI have completed a comprehensive review of the EL-1 grouping (Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines) for the Valley View Townhomes project. \n\n### Key Findings:\n\n**Applicability:** This grouping **is applicable** to the project. The Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) and site plan documents confirm that existing overhead electric (OHE) utility poles and lines are present along Valley View Road (western boundary) and extend into/along the northern property boundary. The project proposes eight buildings, driveways, landscaping, and other site features that must maintain required clearances.\n\n### Research Summary:\n\n**What WAS Found:**\n- Existing overhead electric infrastructure depicted on Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) and referenced as \"OHE\" on Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21)\n- Multiple poles identified along Valley View Road frontage and northern boundary via vision analysis\n- Site plan and landscape plan acknowledge overhead utilities with \"OHE\" labeling\n\n**What WAS NOT Found:**\n- No surveyed elevations of existing overhead conductors on any submitted plan\n- No clearance dimensions between buildings/driveways and overhead facilities\n- No building elevation sheets showing overhead conductor elevations\n- No section or profile views documenting vertical clearances\n- No identification of proposed tree species or Utility Compatible status on landscape plan\n- No 48-hour Austin Energy notification requirement note on cover sheet\n- No dimension lines originating from conductor locations (all clearance documentation absent)\n\n### Deficiencies Identified:\n\nI have identified **9 findings** that require applicant response:\n- **2 items marked as \"fail\"** (EL-1.37 on tree species/Utility Compatible status; EL-1.46 on 48-hour notification note)\n- **7 items marked as \"not-verifiable\"** (missing surveyed conductor elevations, clearance dimensions, section views, and profile documentation needed to confirm compliance with horizontal sky-to-ground and radial clearance requirements for buildings, projections, driveways, and landscaping)\n\nThe remaining 38 checklist items are either not applicable to this specific project or pass (e.g., items requiring facilities not proposed such as transmission line roads, gas pump canopies, or underground service pole spacing)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2605,"cache_read_input_tokens":81251,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2605},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"86ce6d80-0b13-4282-a0c1-971fcaa319e8","uuid":"ab5611cd-b8a4-48c1-8c45-8690ce251305"}
