{"level":30,"time":1776961645187,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","tool":"run_measure_distance","command":"npx tsx /Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/bureau/jurisdictions/austin/workflows/review/scripts/measure-distance.ts --outputPath='/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/output/measure-distance.json' --reasoning='The utility tap plan (Sheet 19) shows water, wastewater, and storm drain lines. I need to measure distances from transformer pad locations (as shown on Sheet 21) to these utility lines to verify the 5-foot minimum horizontal clearance required by UCM § 2.9.1.B.2 for water, wastewater, and storm drain lines. This will verify clearances for items EL-13.21, EL-13.22, and EL-13.23.' --applicable_checklist_items='[{\"checklist_id\":\"EL-13.21\",\"checklist_deficiency_text\":\"Transformer pads lack minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from water lines\"},{\"checklist_id\":\"EL-13.22\",\"checklist_deficiency_text\":\"Transformer pads lack minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from wastewater lines\"},{\"checklist_id\":\"EL-13.23\",\"checklist_deficiency_text\":\"Transformer pads lack minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from storm drain lines\"}]' --documentId='1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777' --sheetNum='19' --objectPairs='[{\"objectA\":\"Transformer Pad 1 location (near northwest entrance driveway)\",\"objectB\":\"Nearest water service line (W)\"},{\"objectA\":\"Transformer Pad 2 location (west of Building 2)\",\"objectB\":\"Nearest wastewater service line (WW)\"},{\"objectA\":\"Transformer Pad 3 location (west of Building 8)\",\"objectB\":\"Nearest wastewater service line (WW)\"}]' --scaleInchesPerFoot='0.05'","msg":"Executing typed script tool"}
{"level":30,"time":1776961761491,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01GD5mHZ4keYPspyCPKUknCk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! Now I have identified the specific trees that are in violation of the EL-2.7 requirement:\n\n1. **Building 8 pad-mount (0.4 feet away - CRITICAL VIOLATION):**\n   - Tree labeled \"SY/M\" (Street Yard/Mitigation tree) - a large shade tree with complex branching pattern\n   - This tree is essentially right on top of the transformer pad\n\n2. **Building 1 pad-mount (6.2 feet away - VIOLATION):**\n   - Tree 1: \"SY/M\" (Street Yard/Mitigation tree) - a large shade tree\n   - Tree 2: \"P\" (Parking Buffer Point Tree) - a smaller ornamental tree\n   - The SY/M tree is within the 10-foot clearance zone\n\n3. **Buildings 6-7 pad-mount (1.9 feet away - CRITICAL VIOLATION):**\n   - Tree labeled \"M\" (Mitigation tree) - a small/medium tree\n   - This tree is essentially right against the transformer pad\n\nNow, from the plant schedule (Sheet 35, Block 11 and 17), I know the proposed trees are:\n- **Shade Trees**: 2 Live Oak, 10 Cedar Elm\n- **Ornamental Trees**: 6 Mexican Redbud, 2 Texas Mountain Laurel\n\nThe \"SY/M\" trees could be Live Oak or Cedar Elm (shade trees). The \"P\" tree would be one of the ornamental trees or possibly a small shade tree. The \"M\" tree would be a mitigation tree, likely one of the ornamental species.\n\nThe critical issue is that trees are positioned way too close to pad-mounted transformers:\n- EL-2.7 requires minimum 10 feet clearance from pad-mounted equipment\n- Bldg 8: 0.4 feet (VIOLATES by 9.6 feet)\n\n\n- Bldg 1: 6.2 feet (VIOLATES by 3.8 feet)\n- Bldgs 6-7: 1.9 feet (VIOLATES by 8.1 feet)\n\nThis is a clear FAIL for EL-2.7. Now I need to check the remaining standards—EL-2.10 and EL-2.11 regarding plant identification, plus EL-2.8 and EL-2.9 for any underground equipment conflicts.\n\nFor EL-2.10, the plant legend uses symbols (SY, PL, P, M) but doesn't display actual species names on the landscape plan itself. While Sheet 35 contains the plant schedule with species information, it's separate from the plan showing electric facilities. Trees near electrical infrastructure aren't identified by species where they appear on the landscape drawing—this is a FAIL.\n\nEL-2.11 presents a similar issue: large shade trees like Live Oak and Cedar Elm (100 gal.) are marked with SY, while ornamental varieties use P or M designations. The size differentiation is visible through container notation, but there's no clear maturity height designation on the plan to distinguish which trees will reach 40+ feet.\n\nThe interpretation of whether this meets requirements depends on how strictly the standard is applied. I should review if there are additional compliance issues before concluding my assessment.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1706,"cache_read_input_tokens":71839,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1706},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8dbaef9-50fb-4056-bee6-2c0dccabc43f","uuid":"6b12942e-166b-485b-8065-f631423378bd"}
