ify drainage/grading requirement without equipment specifications."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.33","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan and plat show property boundaries and easements, but transformer locations relative to property lines are not dimensioned. Cannot definitively verify that all three transformer pads are 100% on private property and do not straddle property lines based on scale drawings alone."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads within or near drainage, water, sewer, or electric easements"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Multiple easements are shown on the plat (drainage, electric, wastewater, water, utility), but specific boundaries and transformer locations relative to easements are not dimensioned. Facts.md notes critical easements not depicted on the plans (Greenbelt Access, City of Austin Drainage). Cannot verify that transformers are not located in prohibited easements without explicit confirmation and AE Design approval."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer easements are not shown as distinct easement areas on site plans or electrical plan. Electrical plan notes mention easement requirements but do not show easement boundaries around pads. Cannot ver