{"level":30,"time":1776961761568,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_015j2UWWVWfgL3DSQX1gpg7J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've returned findings for the items that are NOT VERIFIABLE. However, I realize I haven't thoroughly evaluated ALL 39 items yet. Let me check if there are any FAIL items (where I found evidence of non-compliance) that I should include, and verify I haven't missed any items that have clear PASS status but should be noted.\n\nLooking back at my evaluations:\n- EL-13.1 (5-foot clearance from buildings): All measured at 5.6 to 12.2 feet - PASS\n- EL-13.2 (5-foot clearance from retaining walls): No measurements taken yet - need to check\n- EL-13.3 (fence clearance): No fences shown immediately adjacent - PASS\n- EL-13.4 (reduced clearances): NOT-VERIFIABLE (no approval docs)\n- EL-13.5 (overhangs/balconies): Building elevations not provided - NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- EL-13.6 (windows/doors): NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- EL-13.7 (sidewalk): 57.2 feet away - PASS\n- EL-13.8 (stairwells): NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- EL-13.9 (fire escapes): NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- EL-13.10 (hot-stick): NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- EL-13.11 (confined space): NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- EL-13.12 (fire hydrants): 60-80+ feet away - PASS\n- EL-13.13 (trees utility-compatible): NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- EL-13.14 (shrubs clearance): NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- EL-13.15 (root barriers): NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- EL-13.16 (dumpsters): Not shown near transformers - PASS (or N/A)\n\n\n- EL-13.17 (bike racks): Not shown near transformers - PASS (or N/A)\n- EL-13.18 (light poles): Not shown near transformers - PASS (or N/A)\n- EL-13.19 (fire lanes): Not dimensioned but transformers in landscaped islands - likely PASS\n- EL-13.20 (other transformer pads): 71.6-241.8 feet - PASS\n- EL-13.21 (water lines): NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- EL-13.22 (wastewater): NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- EL-13.23 (storm drain): NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- EL-13.24 (gas): Cannot determine from available documentation - NOT-VERIFIABLE\n\n. Most remaining items related to utilities, easements, and infrastructure details lack sufficient plan information to verify compliance. Gas lines, water/wastewater/storm systems, overhead electrical lines and their clearances, utility routing, easement locations, and pad specifications all fall into this category. Niche requirements don't apply as none are shown, and bollard protection isn't required for this installation. exceeds 5 feet) and the sidewalk sits at 57 feet away (also exceeds the 2-foot minimum). No fire lanes appear to encroach on the transformer locations.\n\nI don't have actual evidence of non-compliance—just items I can't verify due to incomplete information. My findings correctly list only the NOT-VERIFIABLE items while omitting those that pass or don't apply. Let me check if I've overlooked any clear violations by examining the retaining walls more carefully. The site plan shows them primarily around the pond perimeter, and I need to determine if any are positioned within 5 feet of the transformers.\n\nThe transformers appear to be situated in central landscaped areas rather than directly against the main retaining walls, though I haven't explicitly measured these distances. Similarly, the fences shown around the pond and property boundary don't seem immediately adjacent to the transformer locations based on the site plan, but this also lacks precise measurement. For the dumpsters, bike racks, and light poles—which only apply when present adjacent to transformers—I haven't confirmed their exact positioning relative to the transformer areas, so these should likely be marked as not applicable rather than not-verifiable.\n\nReconsidering the conditional requirements: retaining walls do exist on-site, but I can't verify if they're within 5 feet of any transformer without explicit measurement. Fences are shown on the plans,