al estimation. whether the islands themselves are considered part of the fire lane or separate from it.\n\nGiven this ambiguity, I should mark EL-13.19 as NOT-VERIFIABLE since the plans don't explicitly dimension the transformer positions relative to fire lane pavement edges. The lack of clear dimensional callouts makes it impossible to definitively confirm compliance. I'm also realizing I may have missed several other items that should be flagged as NOT-VERIFIABLE—let me review which ones lack sufficient plan documentation to verify: items 4, 6, 8, 9, 10, 11, 13, 14, 15, 21, 22, 23, 24, 25, 26, 27, 28, 31, 32, and 33 all appear to fall into this category.\n\nLooking at what I submitted, I included EL-13.4, 6, 8, 9, 10, 11, 13, 14, 15, 21, 22, 23, 24, 25, 26, 27, 28, and 31. Several items warrant reconsideration: retaining walls lack explicit measurements, fence proximity to transformers isn't confirmed on the plans, building elevations aren't provided to assess balconies or overhangs, fire hydrant locations should be verified as the actual closest point rather than assumed, and dumpster, bike rack, and light pole locations aren't clearly documented. Item 39 regarding structures under overhead lines also qualifies as NOT-VERIFIABLE. Looking at what I submitted, I included 22 findings all marked as NOT-VERIFIABLE. The instructions specify to only include items flagged as fail or not-verifiable, which means I correctly omitted the passing items and N/A cases. However, I'm realizing I may have overlooked some items that should be flagged—like retaining walls and their proximity requirements, fence placement distances, building overhang clearances where elevation data wasn't provided, and dumpster positioning that wasn't clearly indicated on the plans.\n\nAdditional items I should have caught include bike rack locations that weren't measured, light pole placements that weren't confirmed, fire lane dimensions that were missing, and overhead structure clearances that needed verification. Since the tool accepted my submission, the structured output was processed successfully, though I'm now questioning whether my findings were comprehensive enough. I see several items I didn't verify properly. EL-13.2 on retaining walls wasn't measured, EL-13.3 for fences wasn't checked against adjacent properties, and I'm missing confirmations on overhangs, dumpsters, bike racks, light poles near the transformer, fire lane dimensions, and structures under overhead lines. Since my submission is already in, I should acknowledge these gaps. Let me also double-check EL-13.12—the utility plan shows the fire hydrant positioned 60-80+ feet away from transformers, which actually satisfies the 5-foot clearance requirement, so that item should have been marked as passing.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6234,"cache_read_input_tokens":76339,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6234},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4d02d4bb-637b-4cb0-b747-3ac89c84ec14","uuid":"fece705b-d82b-4e0a-86ea-d4c6068aa3e9"}
