ries and easements, but transformer locations relative to property lines are not dimensioned. Cannot definitively verify that all three transformer pads are 100% on private property and do not straddle property lines based on scale drawings alone."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads within or near drainage, water, sewer, or electric easements"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Multiple easements are shown on the plat (drainage, electric, wastewater, water, utility), but specific boundaries and transformer locations relative to easements are not dimensioned. Facts.md notes critical easements not depicted on the plans (Greenbelt Access, City of Austin Drainage). Cannot verify that transformers are not located in prohibited easements without explicit confirmation and AE Design approval."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer easements are not shown as distinct easement areas on site plans or electrical plan. Electrical plan notes mention easement requirements but do not show easement boundaries around pads. Cannot verify that transformer easements are properly shown or that easement width is adequate for Austin Energy accessibility."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Electrical routing from transformers to meters"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical plan shows pull boxes and underground electric routing but does not explicitly document that electrical routing from transformers to meters is 100% on private property. Cannot verify compliance without detailed routing plan and property boundary confirmation."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad dimensions are not shown on electrical plan. Transformer equipment specifications (service type, single-phase vs. three-phase, KVA, voltage) are not provided. Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets are not submitted with application. Cannot verify that pad dimensions match AE Design specifications for the specified service type."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"8e3f12c8-662e-4721-b444-b903c08604ac"}
