11) does NOT show transformer pad locations\n   - Surface drainage direction not shown\n\n8. **Fire Safety Clearances Not Addressed:**\n   - Fire protection plan (Sheet 10) does NOT show transformer pad locations\n   - Fire escape, fire hydrant, and fire lane distances not verifiable\n\nNow let me evaluate each checklist item:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2884,"cache_read_input_tokens":67215,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2884},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ea0af40-45f3-4b07-b50e-bf4188546a20","uuid":"2e96675b-8650-417e-8cc9-ac29bbd3dbda"}
{"level":30,"time":1776961790896,"pid":43999,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01VwevxJFKLEEgPj7YuWqCNe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have comprehensive understanding of the site conditions. Let me create a summary of my research findings before evaluating the checklist items:\n\n## Research Phase Summary\n\n**EXISTING OVERHEAD ELECTRIC FACILITIES IDENTIFIED:**\n1. **Western boundary (Valley View Road)**: Continuous overhead electric line (OHE) with multiple utility poles, 7.5' PUE easement\n2. **Eastern boundary**: Continuous overhead electric line (OHE) with multiple utility poles, 5' electric easement\n3. **Transmission structures**: Transmission easement with transmission lines requiring 25-foot no-dig/no-plant zone, 20-foot equipment clearance\n4. **Service drops**: Existing overhead service drops from poles\n\n**PROPOSED SITE IMPROVEMENTS:**\n- Buildings 1 & 8: Adjacent to western overhead line\n- Buildings 6 & 7: Adjacent to eastern overhead line\n- Buildings 2, 3, 4, 5: Interior location (not directly adjacent to perimeter lines)\n- Landscape plan shows trees proposed near overhead lines (especially southern boundary)\n- Grading plan shows driveway and parking areas near poles\n\n**CRITICAL DOCUMENTATION GAPS:**\n- ❌ NO clearance dimensions from buildings to outside conductors\n- ❌ NO building elevations with surveyed conductor elevations\n- ❌ NO section/profile views showing vertical clearances to overhead lines\n- ❌ NO plan notes about clearance requirements from overhead lines\n- ❌ NO 48-hour notification note to Austin Energy on plans\n- ❌ NO specification of tree species for planting near overhead lines\n- ❌ NO distance measurements from proposed trees to overhead conductors\n- ⚠️ NO pole relocation/utility coordination documentation\n- ⚠️ Trees appear within 10 feet of overhead lines (violates distribution line requirement)\n\nNow let me evaluate each checklist item. Based on my research, I'll mark items as:\n- **pass** = requirement clearly met\n- **fail** = deficiency clearly present\n- **not-verifiable** = cannot determine from available evidence\n- **n/a** = not applicable to this project\n\nLet me now systematically evaluate all 47 checklist items:\n\n**EL-1.1**: Buildings and 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance - **FAIL** - No clearance dimensions shown on plans from Buildings 1, 6, 7, 8 to outside conductors of existing OHE lines\n\n**EL-1.2**: Customer facilities and 15-foot radial clearance - **FAIL** - No 15-foot radial clearance dimensions shown for proposed buildings adjacent to distribution lines\n\n**EL-1.3**: Building projections clearances - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** - Building elevations not provided to determine if projections maintain clearances\n\n**EL-1.4**: Gas pump canopies - **N/A** - No gas pump canopies proposed\n\n**EL-1.5**: Stairs, elevated walkways, platforms clearances - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** - No profile views showing clearances for pedestrian bridges or elevated features\n\n**EL-1.6**: Buildings adjacent to ROW clearances - **FAIL** - Buildings adjacent to ROW (Valley View Road) but no clearance documentation provided\n\n**EL-1.7**: Surveyed elevations of overhead conductors - **FAIL** - No building elevation sheets showing surveyed conductor elevation data\n\n**EL-1.8**: Section/plan exhibits with dimensions - **FAIL** - No section views showing dimensions from outer conductor to building edges\n\n**EL-1.9**: Fence clearances from conductors - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** - Fences shown but no clearance dimensions provided\n\n**EL-1.10**: Fence posts clearance from poles - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** - Fence locations and pole locations shown but clearance dimensions not provided\n\n**EL-1.11**: Fence isolation at substation - **N/A** - No substation shown adjacent to fencing\n\n**EL-1.12**: Transmission line fencing specifications - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** - Transmission easement exists but no fencing details provided for gates/access within easement\n\n**EL-1.13**: Vehicle barrier fencing clearance - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** - No vehicle barriers shown beneath overhead lines\n\n**EL-1.14**: Retaining wall clearances from overhead lines - **FAIL** - Retaining walls shown around site but no clearance dimensions from outside electric lines provided\n\n**EL-1.15**: Retaining walls near substation - **N/A** - No substation adjacent to site\n\n**EL-1.16**: Emergency access structures clearances - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** - No emergency access structures identified with overhead lines\n\n**EL-1.17**: Retaining wall section exhibits - **FAIL** - Retaining wall sections shown but do not include dimensions from outer electric conductor\n\n**EL-1.18**: Driveway vertical clearance - **FAIL** - No vertical clearance dimensions shown for driveways beneath existing OHE lines; no mid-span clearance verification provided\n\n**EL-1.19**: Vehicle parking pads clearance - **FAIL** - Parking areas exist near overhead lines but no vertical clearance dimensions or notes provided\n\n**EL-1.20**: Transmission line road clearance (30 feet) - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** - Transmission structures exist but vertical clearance from transmission lines to roads/driveways not dimensioned\n\n**EL-1.21**: Highway/freeway distribution underbuilt clearance - **N/A** - Not applicable; no highway/freeway with distribution underbuilt\n\n**EL-1.22**: Poles relocated from driveway - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** - Existing poles shown adjacent to driveways but no relocation notes or disposition indicated\n\n**EL-1.23**: Clearance measured from pole vs. conductor - **FAIL** - Where clearance dimensions appear to exist, they do not clearly identify whether measured from outside conductor vs. pole centerline\n\n**EL-1.24**: Streetlight poles under overhead lines - **FAIL** - Landscape plan may show light poles but clearance verification not provided if located under OHE lines\n\n**EL-1.25**: Sidewalks and power poles - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** - Sidewalks shown but clearance from power poles at property ends not documented\n\n**EL-1.26**: Trash areas under overhead facilities - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** - Trash collection area location not clearly identified relative to overhead lines\n\n**EL-1.27**: Customer facilities under/over distribution lines prohibition - **FAIL** - Proposed buildings and features may be positioned beneath or too close to existing OHE lines without documentation of special permission or relocation\n\n**EL-1.28**: Water meters clearance from overhead lines - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** - Water meter locations not clearly shown relative to overhead service drops\n\n**EL-1.29**: Water lines clearance from overhead distribution - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** - Water line routing shown but no clearance verification from overhead distribution\n\n**EL-1.30**: Foundations within 5 feet of property line - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** - Building foundations exist near property line but clearance space for electric facilities not documented\n\n**EL-1.31**: Registered surveyor mid-span clearance data - **FAIL** - Vertical clearances appear marginal; no registered surveyor data provided for existing pole locations and mid-span clearances\n\n**EL-1.32**: Overhead line crossing roadway angles - **N/A** - No new overhead lines proposed; existing lines run parallel to boundaries\n\n**EL-1.33**: Secondary over primary line crossing - **N/A** - No secondary lines shown crossing primary lines\n\n**EL-1.34**: Marquee signs clearance verification - **N/A** - No marquee signs proposed\n\n**EL-1.35**: New power poles spacing - **N/A** - No new power poles for underground conversion proposed\n\n**EL-1.36**: Decorative lighting under overhead lines - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** - Lighting plan exists but clearance from overhead lines not documented\n\n**EL-1.37**: Trees near overhead conductors species and clearance - **FAIL** - Trees proposed (especially visible on southern boundary) appear within 10 feet of overhead lines; tree species not verified against ECM Appendix F utility-compatible list; no clearance dimensions provided\n\n**EL-1.38**: Meter location obstructions - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** - Proposed meter locations shown but obstructions/access not fully verified\n\n**EL-1.39**: Development clearance from existing streetlights - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** - Streetlight poles exist but clearance documentation from buildings not provided\n\n**EL-1.40**: Down guy wire conflicts - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** - Down guy wires shown on existing conditions survey but conflicts with proposed accessible paths/driveways not addressed on site plan\n\n**EL-1.41**: Guy easements for down guy anchors (transmission) - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** - Transmission structures exist but guy easement details not provided\n\n**EL-1.42**: Down guy anchor easements (distribution) - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** - Distribution poles exist but down guy anchor easement details not provided\n\n**EL-1.43**: Transformer vertical clearances - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** - Transformers shown on electrical plan but vertical clearance to overhead lines not documented\n\n**EL-1.44**: Transformer niche clearances - **N/A** - No transformer niches proposed\n\n**EL-1.45**: Construction staging clearance from overhead lines - **FAIL** - No plan notes or construction logistics plan provided showing 10-foot radial clearance from energized overhead lines during construction\n\n**EL-1.46**: 48-hour Austin Energy notification note - **FAIL** - No note on cover sheet or general notes requiring owner/contractor to notify Austin Energy 48 hours before work near high-voltage overhead lines\n\n**EL-1.47**: Service-mast roof clearance - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** - Service details shown but clearance not dimensioned on building elevations\n\nNow let me compile the final findings output with only the FAIL and NOT-VERIFIABLE items:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"ca